:Paragraph_Article_100_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The European Data Protection Supervisor may impose administrative fines on Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies falling within the scope of this Regulation. When deciding whether to impose an administrative fine and when deciding on the amount of the administrative fine in each individual case, all relevant circumstances of the specific situation shall be taken into account and due regard shall be given to the following:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement and of its consequences, taking into account the purpose of the AI system concerned, as well as, where appropriate, the number of affected persons and the level of damage suffered by them;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the degree of responsibility of the Union institution, body, office or agency, taking into account technical and organisational measures implemented by them;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) any action taken by the Union institution, body, office or agency to mitigate the damage suffered by affected persons;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the degree of cooperation with the European Data Protection Supervisor in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement, including compliance with any of the measures previously ordered by the European Data Protection Supervisor against the Union institution, body, office or agency concerned with regard to the same subject matter;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_1_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(1)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) any similar previous infringements by the Union institution, body, office or agency;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_1_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(1)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) the manner in which the infringement became known to the European Data Protection Supervisor, in particular whether, and if so to what extent, the Union institution, body, office or agency notified the infringement;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_1_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(1)(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) the annual budget of the Union institution, body, office or agency."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5 shall be subject to administrative fines of up to EUR 1 500 000."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The non-compliance of the AI system with any requirements or obligations under this Regulation, other than those laid down in Article 5, shall be subject to administrative fines of up to EUR 750 000."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Before taking decisions pursuant to this Article, the European Data Protection Supervisor shall give the Union institution, body, office or agency which is the subject of the proceedings conducted by the European Data Protection Supervisor the opportunity of being heard on the matter regarding the possible infringement. The European Data Protection Supervisor shall base his or her decisions only on elements and circumstances on which the parties concerned have been able to comment. Complainants, if any, shall be associated closely with the proceedings."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The rights of defence of the parties concerned shall be fully respected in the proceedings. They shall be entitled to have access to the European Data Protection Supervisor’s file, subject to the legitimate interest of individuals or undertakings in the protection of their personal data or business secrets."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. Funds collected by imposition of fines in this Article shall contribute to the general budget of the Union. The fines shall not affect the effective operation of the Union institution, body, office or agency fined."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_100_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 100(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. The European Data Protection Supervisor shall, on an annual basis, notify the Commission of the administrative fines it has imposed pursuant to this Article and of any litigation or judicial proceedings it has initiated."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_101_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 101(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) infringed the relevant provisions of this Regulation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_101_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 101(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) failed to comply with a request for a document or for information pursuant to Article 91, or supplied incorrect, incomplete or misleading information;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_101_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 101(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) failed to comply with a measure requested under Article 93;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_101_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 101(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) failed to make available to the Commission access to the general-purpose AI model or general-purpose AI model with systemic risk with a view to conducting an evaluation pursuant to Article 92."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_101_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 101(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Before adopting the decision pursuant to paragraph 1, the Commission shall communicate its preliminary findings to the provider of the general-purpose AI model and give it an opportunity to be heard."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_101_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 101(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Fines imposed in accordance with this Article shall be effective, proportionate and dissuasive."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_101_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 101(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Information on fines imposed under this Article shall also be communicated to the Board as appropriate."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_101_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 101(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The Court of Justice of the European Union shall have unlimited jurisdiction to review decisions of the Commission fixing a fine under this Article. It may cancel, reduce or increase the fine imposed."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_101_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 101(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. The Commission shall adopt implementing acts containing detailed arrangements and procedural safeguards for proceedings in view of the possible adoption of decisions pursuant to paragraph 1 of this Article. Those implementing acts shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_102 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 102"@en ;
    :hasSummary "In Article 4(3) of Regulation (EC) No 300/2008, the following subparagraph is added:"^^xsd:string,
        "‘When adopting detailed measures related to technical specifications and procedures for approval and use of security equipment concerning Artificial Intelligence systems within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council ( * ) , the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_103 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 103"@en ;
    :hasSummary "In Article 17(5) of Regulation (EU) No 167/2013, the following subparagraph is added:"^^xsd:string,
        "‘When adopting delegated acts pursuant to the first subparagraph concerning artificial intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council ( * ) , the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_104 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 104"@en ;
    :hasSummary "In Article 22(5) of Regulation (EU) No 168/2013, the following subparagraph is added:"^^xsd:string,
        "‘When adopting delegated acts pursuant to the first subparagraph concerning Artificial Intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council ( * ) , the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_105 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 105"@en ;
    :hasSummary "In Article 8 of Directive 2014/90/EU, the following paragraph is added:"^^xsd:string,
        "‘5. For Artificial Intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council ( * ) , when carrying out its activities pursuant to paragraph 1 and when adopting technical specifications and testing standards in accordance with paragraphs 2 and 3, the Commission shall take into account the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_106 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 106"@en ;
    :hasSummary "In Article 5 of Directive (EU) 2016/797, the following paragraph is added:"^^xsd:string,
        "‘12. When adopting delegated acts pursuant to paragraph 1 and implementing acts pursuant to paragraph 11 concerning Artificial Intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council ( * ) , the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_107 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 107"@en ;
    :hasSummary "In Article 5 of Regulation (EU) 2018/858 the following paragraph is added:"^^xsd:string,
        "‘4. When adopting delegated acts pursuant to paragraph 3 concerning Artificial Intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council ( * ) , the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_108 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 108"@en ;
    :hasSummary "Regulation (EU) 2018/1139 is amended as follows:"^^xsd:string,
        "‘3. When adopting delegated acts pursuant to paragraphs 1 and 2 concerning Artificial Intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account.’"^^xsd:string,
        "‘3. When adopting delegated acts pursuant to paragraphs 1 and 2 concerning Artificial Intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account.’."^^xsd:string,
        "‘3. Without prejudice to paragraph 2, when adopting implementing acts pursuant to paragraph 1 concerning Artificial Intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council ( * ) , the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account."^^xsd:string,
        "‘4. When adopting delegated acts pursuant to paragraphs 1 and 2 concerning Artificial Intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account.’"^^xsd:string,
        "‘4. When adopting implementing acts pursuant to paragraph 1 concerning Artificial Intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account.’"^^xsd:string,
        "‘When adopting those implementing acts concerning Artificial Intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account.’"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_108_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 108(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(1) in Article 17, the following paragraph is added:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_108_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 108(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(2) in Article 19, the following paragraph is added:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_108_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 108(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(3) in Article 43, the following paragraph is added:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_108_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 108(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(4) in Article 47, the following paragraph is added:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_108_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 108(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(5) in Article 57, the following subparagraph is added:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_108_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 108(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(6) in Article 58, the following paragraph is added:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_109 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 109"@en ;
    :hasSummary "In Article 11 of Regulation (EU) 2019/2144, the following paragraph is added:"^^xsd:string,
        "‘3. When adopting the implementing acts pursuant to paragraph 2, concerning artificial intelligence systems which are safety components within the meaning of Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council ( * ) , the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, of that Regulation shall be taken into account."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. High-risk AI systems which make use of techniques involving the training of AI models with data shall be developed on the basis of training, validation and testing data sets that meet the quality criteria referred to in paragraphs 2 to 5 whenever such data sets are used."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the relevant design choices;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) data collection processes and the origin of data, and in the case of personal data, the original purpose of the data collection;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_2_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(2)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) relevant data-preparation processing operations, such as annotation, labelling, cleaning, updating, enrichment and aggregation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_2_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(2)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the formulation of assumptions, in particular with respect to the information that the data are supposed to measure and represent;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_2_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(2)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) an assessment of the availability, quantity and suitability of the data sets that are needed;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_2_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(2)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) examination in view of possible biases that are likely to affect the health and safety of persons, have a negative impact on fundamental rights or lead to discrimination prohibited under Union law, especially where data outputs influence inputs for future operations;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_2_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(2)(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) appropriate measures to detect, prevent and mitigate possible biases identified according to point (f);"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_2_h a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(2)(h)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(h) the identification of relevant data gaps or shortcomings that prevent compliance with this Regulation, and how those gaps and shortcomings can be addressed."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_5_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(5)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the bias detection and correction cannot be effectively fulfilled by processing other data, including synthetic or anonymised data;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_5_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(5)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the special categories of personal data are subject to technical limitations on the re-use of the personal data, and state-of-the-art security and privacy-preserving measures, including pseudonymisation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_5_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(5)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the special categories of personal data are subject to measures to ensure that the personal data processed are secured, protected, subject to suitable safeguards, including strict controls and documentation of the access, to avoid misuse and ensure that only authorised persons have access to those personal data with appropriate confidentiality obligations;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_5_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(5)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the special categories of personal data are not to be transmitted, transferred or otherwise accessed by other parties;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_5_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(5)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) the special categories of personal data are deleted once the bias has been corrected or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period, whichever comes first;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_5_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(5)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) the records of processing activities pursuant to Regulations (EU) 2016/679 and (EU) 2018/1725 and Directive (EU) 2016/680 include the reasons why the processing of special categories of personal data was strictly necessary to detect and correct biases, and why that objective could not be achieved by processing other data."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_10_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 10(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. For the development of high-risk AI systems not using techniques involving the training of AI models, paragraphs 2 to 5 apply only to the testing data sets."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_110 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 110"@en ;
    :hasSummary "In Annex I to Directive (EU) 2020/1828 of the European Parliament and of the Council ( 58 ) , the following point is added:"^^xsd:string,
        "Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 13 June 2024 laying down harmonised rules on artificial intelligence and amending Regulations (EC) No 300/2008, (EU) No 167/2013, (EU) No 168/2013, (EU) 2018/858, (EU) 2018/1139 and (EU) 2019/2144 and Directives 2014/90/EU, (EU) 2016/797 and (EU) 2020/1828 (Artificial Intelligence Act) ( OJ L, 2024/1689, 12.7.2024, ELI: http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2024/1689/oj ).’."^^xsd:string,
        "‘(68)"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_111_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 111(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Without prejudice to the application of Article 5 as referred to in Article 113(3), point (a), AI systems which are components of the large-scale IT systems established by the legal acts listed in Annex X that have been placed on the market or put into service before 2 August 2027 shall be brought into compliance with this Regulation by 31 December 2030."^^xsd:string,
        "The requirements laid down in this Regulation shall be taken into account in the evaluation of each large-scale IT system established by the legal acts listed in Annex X to be undertaken as provided for in those legal acts and where those legal acts are replaced or amended."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission shall assess the need for amendment of the list set out in Annex III and of the list of prohibited AI practices laid down in Article 5, once a year following the entry into force of this Regulation, and until the end of the period of the delegation of power laid down in Article 97. The Commission shall submit the findings of that assessment to the European Parliament and the Council."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_10 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(10)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "10. The Commission shall, if necessary, submit appropriate proposals to amend this Regulation, in particular taking into account developments in technology, the effect of AI systems on health and safety, and on fundamental rights, and in light of the state of progress in the information society."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_11 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(11)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "11. To guide the evaluations and reviews referred to in paragraphs 1 to 7 of this Article, the AI Office shall undertake to develop an objective and participative methodology for the evaluation of risk levels based on the criteria outlined in the relevant Articles and the inclusion of new systems in:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_11_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(11)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the list set out in Annex III, including the extension of existing area headings or the addition of new area headings in that Annex;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_11_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(11)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the list of prohibited practices set out in Article 5; and"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_11_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(11)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the list of AI systems requiring additional transparency measures pursuant to Article 50."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_12 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(12)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "12. Any amendment to this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 10, or relevant delegated or implementing acts, which concerns sectoral Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I shall take into account the regulatory specificities of each sector, and the existing governance, conformity assessment and enforcement mechanisms and authorities established therein."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_13 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(13)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "13. By 2 August 2031, the Commission shall carry out an assessment of the enforcement of this Regulation and shall report on it to the European Parliament, the Council and the European Economic and Social Committee, taking into account the first years of application of this Regulation. On the basis of the findings, that report shall, where appropriate, be accompanied by a proposal for amendment of this Regulation with regard to the structure of enforcement and the need for a Union agency to resolve any identified shortcomings."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. By 2 August 2028 and every four years thereafter, the Commission shall evaluate and report to the European Parliament and to the Council on the following:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the need for amendments extending existing area headings or adding new area headings in Annex III;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) amendments to the list of AI systems requiring additional transparency measures in Article 50;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_2_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(2)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) amendments enhancing the effectiveness of the supervision and governance system."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. By 2 August 2029 and every four years thereafter, the Commission shall submit a report on the evaluation and review of this Regulation to the European Parliament and to the Council. The report shall include an assessment with regard to the structure of enforcement and the possible need for a Union agency to resolve any identified shortcomings. On the basis of the findings, that report shall, where appropriate, be accompanied by a proposal for amendment of this Regulation. The reports shall be made public."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. The reports referred to in paragraph 2 shall pay specific attention to the following:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_4_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(4)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the status of the financial, technical and human resources of the national competent authorities in order to effectively perform the tasks assigned to them under this Regulation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_4_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(4)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the state of penalties, in particular administrative fines as referred to in Article 99(1), applied by Member States for infringements of this Regulation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_4_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(4)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) adopted harmonised standards and common specifications developed to support this Regulation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_4_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(4)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the number of undertakings that enter the market after the entry into application of this Regulation, and how many of them are SMEs."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. By 2 August 2028, the Commission shall evaluate the functioning of the AI Office, whether the AI Office has been given sufficient powers and competences to fulfil its tasks, and whether it would be relevant and needed for the proper implementation and enforcement of this Regulation to upgrade the AI Office and its enforcement competences and to increase its resources. The Commission shall submit a report on its evaluation to the European Parliament and to the Council."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. By 2 August 2028 and every four years thereafter, the Commission shall submit a report on the review of the progress on the development of standardisation deliverables on the energy-efficient development of general-purpose AI models, and asses the need for further measures or actions, including binding measures or actions. The report shall be submitted to the European Parliament and to the Council, and it shall be made public."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. By 2 August 2028 and every three years thereafter, the Commission shall evaluate the impact and effectiveness of voluntary codes of conduct to foster the application of the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 for AI systems other than high-risk AI systems and possibly other additional requirements for AI systems other than high-risk AI systems, including as regards environmental sustainability."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "8. For the purposes of paragraphs 1 to 7, the Board, the Member States and national competent authorities shall provide the Commission with information upon its request and without undue delay."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_112_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 112(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. In carrying out the evaluations and reviews referred to in paragraphs 1 to 7, the Commission shall take into account the positions and findings of the Board, of the European Parliament, of the Council, and of other relevant bodies or sources."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_113 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 113"@en ;
    :hasSummary "However:"^^xsd:string,
        "It shall apply from 2 August 2026."^^xsd:string,
        "This Regulation shall enter into force on the twentieth day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union ."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_113_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 113(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) Chapters I and II shall apply from 2 February 2025;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_113_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 113(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) Chapter III Section 4, Chapter V, Chapter VII and Chapter XII and Article 78 shall apply from 2 August 2025, with the exception of Article 101;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_113_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 113(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) Article 6(1) and the corresponding obligations in this Regulation shall apply from 2 August 2027."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_11_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 11(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The technical documentation of a high-risk AI system shall be drawn up before that system is placed on the market or put into service and shall be kept up-to date."^^xsd:string,
        "The technical documentation shall be drawn up in such a way as to demonstrate that the high-risk AI system complies with the requirements set out in this Section and to provide national competent authorities and notified bodies with the necessary information in a clear and comprehensive form to assess the compliance of the AI system with those requirements. It shall contain, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex IV. SMEs, including start-ups, may provide the elements of the technical documentation specified in Annex IV in a simplified manner. To that end, the Commission shall establish a simplified technical documentation form targeted at the needs of small and microenterprises. Where an SME, including a start-up, opts to provide the information required in Annex IV in a simplified manner, it shall use the form referred to in this paragraph. Notified bodies shall accept the form for the purposes of the conformity assessment."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_11_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 11(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Where a high-risk AI system related to a product covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I is placed on the market or put into service, a single set of technical documentation shall be drawn up containing all the information set out in paragraph 1, as well as the information required under those legal acts."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_11_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 11(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend Annex IV, where necessary, to ensure that, in light of technical progress, the technical documentation provides all the information necessary to assess the compliance of the system with the requirements set out in this Section."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_12_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 12(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) identifying situations that may result in the high-risk AI system presenting a risk within the meaning of Article 79(1) or in a substantial modification;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_12_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 12(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) facilitating the post-market monitoring referred to in Article 72; and"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_12_2_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 12(2)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) monitoring the operation of high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 26(5)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_12_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 12(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. For high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1 (a), of Annex III, the logging capabilities shall provide, at a minimum:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_12_3_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 12(3)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) recording of the period of each use of the system (start date and time and end date and time of each use);"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_12_3_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 12(3)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the reference database against which input data has been checked by the system;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_12_3_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 12(3)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the input data for which the search has led to a match;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_12_3_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 12(3)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the identification of the natural persons involved in the verification of the results, as referred to in Article 14(5)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The instructions for use shall contain at least the following information:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the identity and the contact details of the provider and, where applicable, of its authorised representative;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the characteristics, capabilities and limitations of performance of the high-risk AI system, including:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the changes to the high-risk AI system and its performance which have been pre-determined by the provider at the moment of the initial conformity assessment, if any;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the human oversight measures referred to in Article 14, including the technical measures put in place to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of the high-risk AI systems by the deployers;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) the computational and hardware resources needed, the expected lifetime of the high-risk AI system and any necessary maintenance and care measures, including their frequency, to ensure the proper functioning of that AI system, including as regards software updates;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) where relevant, a description of the mechanisms included within the high-risk AI system that allows deployers to properly collect, store and interpret the logs in accordance with Article 12."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) its intended purpose;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_ii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(ii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(ii) the level of accuracy, including its metrics, robustness and cybersecurity referred to in Article 15 against which the high-risk AI system has been tested and validated and which can be expected, and any known and foreseeable circumstances that may have an impact on that expected level of accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_iii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(iii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iii) any known or foreseeable circumstance, related to the use of the high-risk AI system in accordance with its intended purpose or under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse, which may lead to risks to the health and safety or fundamental rights referred to in Article 9(2);"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_iv a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(iv)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iv) where applicable, the technical capabilities and characteristics of the high-risk AI system to provide information that is relevant to explain its output;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_v a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(v)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(v) when appropriate, its performance regarding specific persons or groups of persons on which the system is intended to be used;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_vi a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(vi)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(vi) when appropriate, specifications for the input data, or any other relevant information in terms of the training, validation and testing data sets used, taking into account the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_13_3_vii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 13(3)(vii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(vii) where applicable, information to enable deployers to interpret the output of the high-risk AI system and use it appropriately;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_14_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 14(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. For the purpose of implementing paragraphs 1, 2 and 3, the high-risk AI system shall be provided to the deployer in such a way that natural persons to whom human oversight is assigned are enabled, as appropriate and proportionate:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_15_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 15(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. To address the technical aspects of how to measure the appropriate levels of accuracy and robustness set out in paragraph 1 and any other relevant performance metrics, the Commission shall, in cooperation with relevant stakeholders and organisations such as metrology and benchmarking authorities, encourage, as appropriate, the development of benchmarks and measurement methodologies."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_15_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 15(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. High-risk AI systems shall be as resilient as possible regarding errors, faults or inconsistencies that may occur within the system or the environment in which the system operates, in particular due to their interaction with natural persons or other systems. Technical and organisational measures shall be taken in this regard."^^xsd:string,
        "High-risk AI systems that continue to learn after being placed on the market or put into service shall be developed in such a way as to eliminate or reduce as far as possible the risk of possibly biased outputs influencing input for future operations (feedback loops), and as to ensure that any such feedback loops are duly addressed with appropriate mitigation measures."^^xsd:string,
        "The robustness of high-risk AI systems may be achieved through technical redundancy solutions, which may include backup or fail-safe plans."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_15_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 15(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. High-risk AI systems shall be resilient against attempts by unauthorised third parties to alter their use, outputs or performance by exploiting system vulnerabilities."^^xsd:string,
        "The technical solutions aiming to ensure the cybersecurity of high-risk AI systems shall be appropriate to the relevant circumstances and the risks."^^xsd:string,
        "The technical solutions to address AI specific vulnerabilities shall include, where appropriate, measures to prevent, detect, respond to, resolve and control for attacks trying to manipulate the training data set (data poisoning), or pre-trained components used in training (model poisoning), inputs designed to cause the AI model to make a mistake (adversarial examples or model evasion), confidentiality attacks or model flaws."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16"@en ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems shall:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) ensure that their high-risk AI systems are compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) indicate on the high-risk AI system or, where that is not possible, on its packaging or its accompanying documentation, as applicable, their name, registered trade name or registered trade mark, the address at which they can be contacted;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) have a quality management system in place which complies with Article 17;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) keep the documentation referred to in Article 18;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) when under their control, keep the logs automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems as referred to in Article 19;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) ensure that the high-risk AI system undergoes the relevant conformity assessment procedure as referred to in Article 43, prior to its being placed on the market or put into service;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) draw up an EU declaration of conformity in accordance with Article 47;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_h a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(h)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(h) affix the CE marking to the high-risk AI system or, where that is not possible, on its packaging or its accompanying documentation, to indicate conformity with this Regulation, in accordance with Article 48;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) comply with the registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1);"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_j a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(j)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(j) take the necessary corrective actions and provide information as required in Article 20;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_k a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(k)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(k) upon a reasoned request of a national competent authority, demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_16_l a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 16(l)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(l) ensure that the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements in accordance with Directives (EU) 2016/2102 and (EU) 2019/882."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_17_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 17(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Providers of high-risk AI systems that are subject to obligations regarding quality management systems or an equivalent function under relevant sectoral Union law may include the aspects listed in paragraph 1 as part of the quality management systems pursuant to that law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_17_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 17(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. For providers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law, the obligation to put in place a quality management system, with the exception of paragraph 1, points (g), (h) and (i) of this Article, shall be deemed to be fulfilled by complying with the rules on internal governance arrangements or processes pursuant to the relevant Union financial services law. To that end, any harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 shall be taken into account."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_18_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 18(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The provider shall, for a period ending 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market or put into service, keep at the disposal of the national competent authorities:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_18_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 18(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the technical documentation referred to in Article 11;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_18_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 18(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the documentation concerning the quality management system referred to in Article 17;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_18_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 18(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the documentation concerning the changes approved by notified bodies, where applicable;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_18_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 18(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the decisions and other documents issued by the notified bodies, where applicable;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_18_1_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 18(1)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_18_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 18(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Each Member State shall determine conditions under which the documentation referred to in paragraph 1 remains at the disposal of the national competent authorities for the period indicated in that paragraph for the cases when a provider or its authorised representative established on its territory goes bankrupt or ceases its activity prior to the end of that period."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_18_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 18(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Providers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law shall maintain the technical documentation as part of the documentation kept under the relevant Union financial services law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_1_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 1(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The purpose of this Regulation is to improve the functioning of the internal market and promote the uptake of human-centric and trustworthy artificial intelligence (AI), while ensuring a high level of protection of health, safety, fundamental rights enshrined in the Charter, including democracy, the rule of law and environmental protection, against the harmful effects of AI systems in the Union and supporting innovation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_1_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 1(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. This Regulation lays down:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_1_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 1(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) harmonised rules for the placing on the market, the putting into service, and the use of AI systems in the Union;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_1_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 1(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) prohibitions of certain AI practices;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_1_2_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 1(2)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) specific requirements for high-risk AI systems and obligations for operators of such systems;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_1_2_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 1(2)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) harmonised transparency rules for certain AI systems;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_1_2_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 1(2)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) harmonised rules for the placing on the market of general-purpose AI models;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_1_2_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 1(2)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) rules on market monitoring, market surveillance, governance and enforcement;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_1_2_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 1(2)(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) measures to support innovation, with a particular focus on SMEs, including start-ups."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_21_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 21(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Any information obtained by a competent authority pursuant to this Article shall be treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_22_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 22(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Prior to making their high-risk AI systems available on the Union market, providers established in third countries shall, by written mandate, appoint an authorised representative which is established in the Union."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_22_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 22(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The provider shall enable its authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_22_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 22(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The authorised representative shall perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider. It shall provide a copy of the mandate to the market surveillance authorities upon request, in one of the official languages of the institutions of the Union, as indicated by the competent authority. For the purposes of this Regulation, the mandate shall empower the authorised representative to carry out the following tasks:"^^xsd:string,
        "The mandate shall empower the authorised representative to be addressed, in addition to or instead of the provider, by the competent authorities, on all issues related to ensuring compliance with this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_23_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 23(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Before placing a high-risk AI system on the market, importers shall ensure that the system is in conformity with this Regulation by verifying that:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_25_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 25(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) they put their name or trademark on a high-risk AI system already placed on the market or put into service, without prejudice to contractual arrangements stipulating that the obligations are otherwise allocated;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_25_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 25(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) they make a substantial modification to a high-risk AI system that has already been placed on the market or has already been put into service in such a way that it remains a high-risk AI system pursuant to Article 6;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_25_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 25(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) they modify the intended purpose of an AI system, including a general-purpose AI system, which has not been classified as high-risk and has already been placed on the market or put into service in such a way that the AI system concerned becomes a high-risk AI system in accordance with Article 6."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_25_3_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 25(3)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the high-risk AI system is placed on the market together with the product under the name or trademark of the product manufacturer;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_25_3_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 25(3)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the high-risk AI system is put into service under the name or trademark of the product manufacturer after the product has been placed on the market."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_25_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 25(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. Paragraphs 2 and 3 are without prejudice to the need to observe and protect intellectual property rights, confidential business information and trade secrets in accordance with Union and national law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_26_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 26(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The obligations set out in paragraphs 1 and 2, are without prejudice to other deployer obligations under Union or national law and to the deployer’s freedom to organise its own resources and activities for the purpose of implementing the human oversight measures indicated by the provider."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_27_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 27(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) a description of the deployer’s processes in which the high-risk AI system will be used in line with its intended purpose;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_27_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 27(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) a description of the period of time within which, and the frequency with which, each high-risk AI system is intended to be used;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_27_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 27(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the categories of natural persons and groups likely to be affected by its use in the specific context;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_27_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 27(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the specific risks of harm likely to have an impact on the categories of natural persons or groups of persons identified pursuant to point (c) of this paragraph, taking into account the information given by the provider pursuant to Article 13;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_27_1_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 27(1)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) a description of the implementation of human oversight measures, according to the instructions for use;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_27_1_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 27(1)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) the measures to be taken in the case of the materialisation of those risks, including the arrangements for internal governance and complaint mechanisms."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_28_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 28(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Each Member State shall designate or establish at least one notifying authority responsible for setting up and carrying out the necessary procedures for the assessment, designation and notification of conformity assessment bodies and for their monitoring. Those procedures shall be developed in cooperation between the notifying authorities of all Member States."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_28_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 28(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Member States may decide that the assessment and monitoring referred to in paragraph 1 is to be carried out by a national accreditation body within the meaning of, and in accordance with, Regulation (EC) No 765/2008."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_28_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 28(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Notifying authorities shall be established, organised and operated in such a way that no conflict of interest arises with conformity assessment bodies, and that the objectivity and impartiality of their activities are safeguarded."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_28_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 28(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Notifying authorities shall be organised in such a way that decisions relating to the notification of conformity assessment bodies are taken by competent persons different from those who carried out the assessment of those bodies."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_28_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 28(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. Notifying authorities shall offer or provide neither any activities that conformity assessment bodies perform, nor any consultancy services on a commercial or competitive basis."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_28_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 28(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. Notifying authorities shall safeguard the confidentiality of the information that they obtain, in accordance with Article 78."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_28_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 28(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. Notifying authorities shall have an adequate number of competent personnel at their disposal for the proper performance of their tasks. Competent personnel shall have the necessary expertise, where applicable, for their function, in fields such as information technologies, AI and law, including the supervision of fundamental rights."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_29_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 29(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Conformity assessment bodies shall submit an application for notification to the notifying authority of the Member State in which they are established."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_29_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 29(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The application for notification shall be accompanied by a description of the conformity assessment activities, the conformity assessment module or modules and the types of AI systems for which the conformity assessment body claims to be competent, as well as by an accreditation certificate, where one exists, issued by a national accreditation body attesting that the conformity assessment body fulfils the requirements laid down in Article 31."^^xsd:string,
        "Any valid document related to existing designations of the applicant notified body under any other Union harmonisation legislation shall be added."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_29_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 29(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Where the conformity assessment body concerned cannot provide an accreditation certificate, it shall provide the notifying authority with all the documentary evidence necessary for the verification, recognition and regular monitoring of its compliance with the requirements laid down in Article 31."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_29_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 29(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. For notified bodies which are designated under any other Union harmonisation legislation, all documents and certificates linked to those designations may be used to support their designation procedure under this Regulation, as appropriate. The notified body shall update the documentation referred to in paragraphs 2 and 3 of this Article whenever relevant changes occur, in order to enable the authority responsible for notified bodies to monitor and verify continuous compliance with all the requirements laid down in Article 31."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. This Regulation applies to:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_10 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(10)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "10. This Regulation does not apply to obligations of deployers who are natural persons using AI systems in the course of a purely personal non-professional activity."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_11 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(11)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "11. This Regulation does not preclude the Union or Member States from maintaining or introducing laws, regulations or administrative provisions which are more favourable to workers in terms of protecting their rights in respect of the use of AI systems by employers, or from encouraging or allowing the application of collective agreements which are more favourable to workers."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_12 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(12)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "12. This Regulation does not apply to AI systems released under free and open-source licences, unless they are placed on the market or put into service as high-risk AI systems or as an AI system that falls under Article 5 or 50."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) providers placing on the market or putting into service AI systems or placing on the market general-purpose AI models in the Union, irrespective of whether those providers are established or located within the Union or in a third country;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) deployers of AI systems that have their place of establishment or are located within the Union;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) providers and deployers of AI systems that have their place of establishment or are located in a third country, where the output produced by the AI system is used in the Union;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) importers and distributors of AI systems;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_1_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(1)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) product manufacturers placing on the market or putting into service an AI system together with their product and under their own name or trademark;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_1_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(1)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) authorised representatives of providers, which are not established in the Union;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_1_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(1)(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) affected persons that are located in the Union."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. For AI systems classified as high-risk AI systems in accordance with Article 6(1) related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I, only Article 6(1), Articles 102 to 109 and Article 112 apply. Article 57 applies only in so far as the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. This Regulation does not apply to areas outside the scope of Union law, and shall not, in any event, affect the competences of the Member States concerning national security, regardless of the type of entity entrusted by the Member States with carrying out tasks in relation to those competences."^^xsd:string,
        "This Regulation does not apply to AI systems where and in so far they are placed on the market, put into service, or used with or without modification exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes, regardless of the type of entity carrying out those activities."^^xsd:string,
        "This Regulation does not apply to AI systems which are not placed on the market or put into service in the Union, where the output is used in the Union exclusively for military, defence or national security purposes, regardless of the type of entity carrying out those activities."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. This Regulation applies neither to public authorities in a third country nor to international organisations falling within the scope of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1, where those authorities or organisations use AI systems in the framework of international cooperation or agreements for law enforcement and judicial cooperation with the Union or with one or more Member States, provided that such a third country or international organisation provides adequate safeguards with respect to the protection of fundamental rights and freedoms of individuals."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. This Regulation shall not affect the application of the provisions on the liability of providers of intermediary services as set out in Chapter II of Regulation (EU) 2022/2065."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. This Regulation does not apply to AI systems or AI models, including their output, specifically developed and put into service for the sole purpose of scientific research and development."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. Union law on the protection of personal data, privacy and the confidentiality of communications applies to personal data processed in connection with the rights and obligations laid down in this Regulation. This Regulation shall not affect Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or (EU) 2018/1725, or Directive 2002/58/EC or (EU) 2016/680, without prejudice to Article 10(5) and Article 59 of this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "8. This Regulation does not apply to any research, testing or development activity regarding AI systems or AI models prior to their being placed on the market or put into service. Such activities shall be conducted in accordance with applicable Union law. Testing in real world conditions shall not be covered by that exclusion."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_2_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 2(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. This Regulation is without prejudice to the rules laid down by other Union legal acts related to consumer protection and product safety."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3"@en ;
    :hasSummary "For the purposes of this Regulation, the following definitions apply:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_30_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 30(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Notifying authorities may notify only conformity assessment bodies which have satisfied the requirements laid down in Article 31."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_30_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 30(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Notifying authorities shall notify the Commission and the other Member States, using the electronic notification tool developed and managed by the Commission, of each conformity assessment body referred to in paragraph 1."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_30_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 30(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The notification referred to in paragraph 2 of this Article shall include full details of the conformity assessment activities, the conformity assessment module or modules, the types of AI systems concerned, and the relevant attestation of competence. Where a notification is not based on an accreditation certificate as referred to in Article 29(2), the notifying authority shall provide the Commission and the other Member States with documentary evidence which attests to the competence of the conformity assessment body and to the arrangements in place to ensure that that body will be monitored regularly and will continue to satisfy the requirements laid down in Article 31."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_30_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 30(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. The conformity assessment body concerned may perform the activities of a notified body only where no objections are raised by the Commission or the other Member States within two weeks of a notification by a notifying authority where it includes an accreditation certificate referred to in Article 29(2), or within two months of a notification by the notifying authority where it includes documentary evidence referred to in Article 29(3)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_30_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 30(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. Where objections are raised, the Commission shall, without delay, enter into consultations with the relevant Member States and the conformity assessment body. In view thereof, the Commission shall decide whether the authorisation is justified. The Commission shall address its decision to the Member State concerned and to the relevant conformity assessment body."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. A notified body shall be established under the national law of a Member State and shall have legal personality."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_10 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(10)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "10. Notified bodies shall be capable of carrying out all their tasks under this Regulation with the highest degree of professional integrity and the requisite competence in the specific field, whether those tasks are carried out by notified bodies themselves or on their behalf and under their responsibility."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_11 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(11)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "11. Notified bodies shall have sufficient internal competences to be able effectively to evaluate the tasks conducted by external parties on their behalf. The notified body shall have permanent availability of sufficient administrative, technical, legal and scientific personnel who possess experience and knowledge relating to the relevant types of AI systems, data and data computing, and relating to the requirements set out in Section 2."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_12 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(12)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "12. Notified bodies shall participate in coordination activities as referred to in Article 38. They shall also take part directly, or be represented in, European standardisation organisations, or ensure that they are aware and up to date in respect of relevant standards."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Notified bodies shall satisfy the organisational, quality management, resources and process requirements that are necessary to fulfil their tasks, as well as suitable cybersecurity requirements."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The organisational structure, allocation of responsibilities, reporting lines and operation of notified bodies shall ensure confidence in their performance, and in the results of the conformity assessment activities that the notified bodies conduct."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Notified bodies shall be independent of the provider of a high-risk AI system in relation to which they perform conformity assessment activities. Notified bodies shall also be independent of any other operator having an economic interest in high-risk AI systems assessed, as well as of any competitors of the provider. This shall not preclude the use of assessed high-risk AI systems that are necessary for the operations of the conformity assessment body, or the use of such high-risk AI systems for personal purposes."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. Neither a conformity assessment body, its top-level management nor the personnel responsible for carrying out its conformity assessment tasks shall be directly involved in the design, development, marketing or use of high-risk AI systems, nor shall they represent the parties engaged in those activities. They shall not engage in any activity that might conflict with their independence of judgement or integrity in relation to conformity assessment activities for which they are notified. This shall, in particular, apply to consultancy services."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. Notified bodies shall be organised and operated so as to safeguard the independence, objectivity and impartiality of their activities. Notified bodies shall document and implement a structure and procedures to safeguard impartiality and to promote and apply the principles of impartiality throughout their organisation, personnel and assessment activities."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. Notified bodies shall have documented procedures in place ensuring that their personnel, committees, subsidiaries, subcontractors and any associated body or personnel of external bodies maintain, in accordance with Article 78, the confidentiality of the information which comes into their possession during the performance of conformity assessment activities, except when its disclosure is required by law. The staff of notified bodies shall be bound to observe professional secrecy with regard to all information obtained in carrying out their tasks under this Regulation, except in relation to the notifying authorities of the Member State in which their activities are carried out."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "8. Notified bodies shall have procedures for the performance of activities which take due account of the size of a provider, the sector in which it operates, its structure, and the degree of complexity of the AI system concerned."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_31_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. Notified bodies shall take out appropriate liability insurance for their conformity assessment activities, unless liability is assumed by the Member State in which they are established in accordance with national law or that Member State is itself directly responsible for the conformity assessment."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_32 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 32"@en ;
    :hasSummary "Where a conformity assessment body demonstrates its conformity with the criteria laid down in the relevant harmonised standards or parts thereof, the references of which have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union , it shall be presumed to comply with the requirements set out in Article 31 in so far as the applicable harmonised standards cover those requirements."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_33_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 33(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Where a notified body subcontracts specific tasks connected with the conformity assessment or has recourse to a subsidiary, it shall ensure that the subcontractor or the subsidiary meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, and shall inform the notifying authority accordingly."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_33_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 33(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Notified bodies shall take full responsibility for the tasks performed by any subcontractors or subsidiaries."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_33_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 33(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Activities may be subcontracted or carried out by a subsidiary only with the agreement of the provider. Notified bodies shall make a list of their subsidiaries publicly available."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_33_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 33(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. The relevant documents concerning the assessment of the qualifications of the subcontractor or the subsidiary and the work carried out by them under this Regulation shall be kept at the disposal of the notifying authority for a period of five years from the termination date of the subcontracting."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_34_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 34(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Notified bodies shall avoid unnecessary burdens for providers when performing their activities, and take due account of the size of the provider, the sector in which it operates, its structure and the degree of complexity of the high-risk AI system concerned, in particular in view of minimising administrative burdens and compliance costs for micro- and small enterprises within the meaning of Recommendation 2003/361/EC. The notified body shall, nevertheless, respect the degree of rigour and the level of protection required for the compliance of the high-risk AI system with the requirements of this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_35_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 35(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission shall assign a single identification number to each notified body, even where a body is notified under more than one Union act."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_35_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 35(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The Commission shall make publicly available the list of the bodies notified under this Regulation, including their identification numbers and the activities for which they have been notified. The Commission shall ensure that the list is kept up to date."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The notifying authority shall notify the Commission and the other Member States of any relevant changes to the notification of a notified body via the electronic notification tool referred to in Article 30(2)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The procedures laid down in Articles 29 and 30 shall apply to extensions of the scope of the notification."^^xsd:string,
        "For changes to the notification other than extensions of its scope, the procedures laid down in paragraphs (3) to (9) shall apply."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Where a notified body decides to cease its conformity assessment activities, it shall inform the notifying authority and the providers concerned as soon as possible and, in the case of a planned cessation, at least one year before ceasing its activities. The certificates of the notified body may remain valid for a period of nine months after cessation of the notified body’s activities, on condition that another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume responsibilities for the high-risk AI systems covered by those certificates. The latter notified body shall complete a full assessment of the high-risk AI systems affected by the end of that nine-month-period before issuing new certificates for those systems. Where the notified body has ceased its activity, the notifying authority shall withdraw the designation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Where a notifying authority has sufficient reason to consider that a notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31, or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations, the notifying authority shall without delay investigate the matter with the utmost diligence. In that context, it shall inform the notified body concerned about the objections raised and give it the possibility to make its views known. If the notifying authority comes to the conclusion that the notified body no longer meets the requirements laid down in Article 31 or that it is failing to fulfil its obligations, it shall restrict, suspend or withdraw the designation as appropriate, depending on the seriousness of the failure to meet those requirements or fulfil those obligations. It shall immediately inform the Commission and the other Member States accordingly."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. Where its designation has been suspended, restricted, or fully or partially withdrawn, the notified body shall inform the providers concerned within 10 days."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. In the event of the restriction, suspension or withdrawal of a designation, the notifying authority shall take appropriate steps to ensure that the files of the notified body concerned are kept, and to make them available to notifying authorities in other Member States and to market surveillance authorities at their request."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. In the event of the restriction, suspension or withdrawal of a designation, the notifying authority shall:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_7_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(7)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) assess the impact on the certificates issued by the notified body;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_7_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(7)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) submit a report on its findings to the Commission and the other Member States within three months of having notified the changes to the designation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_7_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(7)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) require the notified body to suspend or withdraw, within a reasonable period of time determined by the authority, any certificates which were unduly issued, in order to ensure the continuing conformity of high-risk AI systems on the market;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_7_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(7)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) inform the Commission and the Member States about certificates the suspension or withdrawal of which it has required;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_7_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(7)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) provide the national competent authorities of the Member State in which the provider has its registered place of business with all relevant information about the certificates of which it has required the suspension or withdrawal; that authority shall take the appropriate measures, where necessary, to avoid a potential risk to health, safety or fundamental rights."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "8. With the exception of certificates unduly issued, and where a designation has been suspended or restricted, the certificates shall remain valid in one of the following circumstances:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_8_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(8)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the notifying authority has confirmed, within one month of the suspension or restriction, that there is no risk to health, safety or fundamental rights in relation to certificates affected by the suspension or restriction, and the notifying authority has outlined a timeline for actions to remedy the suspension or restriction; or"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_8_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(8)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the notifying authority has confirmed that no certificates relevant to the suspension will be issued, amended or re-issued during the course of the suspension or restriction, and states whether the notified body has the capability of continuing to monitor and remain responsible for existing certificates issued for the period of the suspension or restriction; in the event that the notifying authority determines that the notified body does not have the capability to support existing certificates issued, the provider of the system covered by the certificate shall confirm in writing to the national competent authorities of the Member State in which it has its registered place of business, within three months of the suspension or restriction, that another qualified notified body is temporarily assuming the functions of the notified body to monitor and remain responsible for the certificates during the period of suspension or restriction."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. With the exception of certificates unduly issued, and where a designation has been withdrawn, the certificates shall remain valid for a period of nine months under the following circumstances:"^^xsd:string,
        "In the circumstances referred to in the first subparagraph, the national competent authority of the Member State in which the provider of the system covered by the certificate has its place of business may extend the provisional validity of the certificates for additional periods of three months, which shall not exceed 12 months in total."^^xsd:string,
        "The national competent authority or the notified body assuming the functions of the notified body affected by the change of designation shall immediately inform the Commission, the other Member States and the other notified bodies thereof."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_9_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(9)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the national competent authority of the Member State in which the provider of the high-risk AI system covered by the certificate has its registered place of business has confirmed that there is no risk to health, safety or fundamental rights associated with the high-risk AI systems concerned; and"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_36_9_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 36(9)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) another notified body has confirmed in writing that it will assume immediate responsibility for those AI systems and completes its assessment within 12 months of the withdrawal of the designation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_38_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 38(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission shall ensure that, with regard to high-risk AI systems, appropriate coordination and cooperation between notified bodies active in the conformity assessment procedures pursuant to this Regulation are put in place and properly operated in the form of a sectoral group of notified bodies."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_38_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 38(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Each notifying authority shall ensure that the bodies notified by it participate in the work of a group referred to in paragraph 1, directly or through designated representatives."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_38_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 38(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The Commission shall provide for the exchange of knowledge and best practices between notifying authorities."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_39 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 39"@en ;
    :hasSummary "Conformity assessment bodies established under the law of a third country with which the Union has concluded an agreement may be authorised to carry out the activities of notified bodies under this Regulation, provided that they meet the requirements laid down in Article 31 or they ensure an equivalent level of compliance."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(1) ‘AI system’ means a machine-based system that is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy and that may exhibit adaptiveness after deployment, and that, for explicit or implicit objectives, infers, from the input it receives, how to generate outputs such as predictions, content, recommendations, or decisions that can influence physical or virtual environments;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_10 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(10)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(10) ‘making available on the market’ means the supply of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model for distribution or use on the Union market in the course of a commercial activity, whether in return for payment or free of charge;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_11 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(11)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(11) ‘putting into service’ means the supply of an AI system for first use directly to the deployer or for own use in the Union for its intended purpose;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_12 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(12)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(12) ‘intended purpose’ means the use for which an AI system is intended by the provider, including the specific context and conditions of use, as specified in the information supplied by the provider in the instructions for use, promotional or sales materials and statements, as well as in the technical documentation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_13 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(13)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(13) ‘reasonably foreseeable misuse’ means the use of an AI system in a way that is not in accordance with its intended purpose, but which may result from reasonably foreseeable human behaviour or interaction with other systems, including other AI systems;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_14 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(14)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(14) ‘safety component’ means a component of a product or of an AI system which fulfils a safety function for that product or AI system, or the failure or malfunctioning of which endangers the health and safety of persons or property;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_15 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(15)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(15) ‘instructions for use’ means the information provided by the provider to inform the deployer of, in particular, an AI system’s intended purpose and proper use;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_16 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(16)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(16) ‘recall of an AI system’ means any measure aiming to achieve the return to the provider or taking out of service or disabling the use of an AI system made available to deployers;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_17 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(17)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(17) ‘withdrawal of an AI system’ means any measure aiming to prevent an AI system in the supply chain being made available on the market;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_18 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(18)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(18) ‘performance of an AI system’ means the ability of an AI system to achieve its intended purpose;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_19 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(19)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(19) ‘notifying authority’ means the national authority responsible for setting up and carrying out the necessary procedures for the assessment, designation and notification of conformity assessment bodies and for their monitoring;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(2) ‘risk’ means the combination of the probability of an occurrence of harm and the severity of that harm;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_20 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(20)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(20) ‘conformity assessment’ means the process of demonstrating whether the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 relating to a high-risk AI system have been fulfilled;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_21 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(21)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(21) ‘conformity assessment body’ means a body that performs third-party conformity assessment activities, including testing, certification and inspection;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_22 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(22)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(22) ‘notified body’ means a conformity assessment body notified in accordance with this Regulation and other relevant Union harmonisation legislation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_23 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(23)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(23) ‘substantial modification’ means a change to an AI system after its placing on the market or putting into service which is not foreseen or planned in the initial conformity assessment carried out by the provider and as a result of which the compliance of the AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 is affected or results in a modification to the intended purpose for which the AI system has been assessed;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_24 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(24)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(24) ‘CE marking’ means a marking by which a provider indicates that an AI system is in conformity with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 and other applicable Union harmonisation legislation providing for its affixing;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_25 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(25)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(25) ‘post-market monitoring system’ means all activities carried out by providers of AI systems to collect and review experience gained from the use of AI systems they place on the market or put into service for the purpose of identifying any need to immediately apply any necessary corrective or preventive actions;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_26 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(26)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(26) ‘market surveillance authority’ means the national authority carrying out the activities and taking the measures pursuant to Regulation (EU) 2019/1020;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_27 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(27)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(27) ‘harmonised standard’ means a harmonised standard as defined in Article 2(1), point (c), of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_28 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(28)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(28) ‘common specification’ means a set of technical specifications as defined in Article 2, point (4) of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, providing means to comply with certain requirements established under this Regulation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_29 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(29)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(29) ‘training data’ means data used for training an AI system through fitting its learnable parameters;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(3) ‘provider’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body that develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model or that has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed and places it on the market or puts the AI system into service under its own name or trademark, whether for payment or free of charge;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_30 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(30)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(30) ‘validation data’ means data used for providing an evaluation of the trained AI system and for tuning its non-learnable parameters and its learning process in order, inter alia, to prevent underfitting or overfitting;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_31 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(31)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(31) ‘validation data set’ means a separate data set or part of the training data set, either as a fixed or variable split;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_32 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(32)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(32) ‘testing data’ means data used for providing an independent evaluation of the AI system in order to confirm the expected performance of that system before its placing on the market or putting into service;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_33 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(33)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(33) ‘input data’ means data provided to or directly acquired by an AI system on the basis of which the system produces an output;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_34 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(34)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(34) ‘biometric data’ means personal data resulting from specific technical processing relating to the physical, physiological or behavioural characteristics of a natural person, such as facial images or dactyloscopic data;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_35 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(35)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(35) ‘biometric identification’ means the automated recognition of physical, physiological, behavioural, or psychological human features for the purpose of establishing the identity of a natural person by comparing biometric data of that individual to biometric data of individuals stored in a database;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_36 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(36)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(36) ‘biometric verification’ means the automated, one-to-one verification, including authentication, of the identity of natural persons by comparing their biometric data to previously provided biometric data;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_37 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(37)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(37) ‘special categories of personal data’ means the categories of personal data referred to in Article 9(1) of Regulation (EU) 2016/679, Article 10 of Directive (EU) 2016/680 and Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_38 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(38)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(38) ‘sensitive operational data’ means operational data related to activities of prevention, detection, investigation or prosecution of criminal offences, the disclosure of which could jeopardise the integrity of criminal proceedings;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_39 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(39)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(39) ‘emotion recognition system’ means an AI system for the purpose of identifying or inferring emotions or intentions of natural persons on the basis of their biometric data;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(4) ‘deployer’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body using an AI system under its authority except where the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_40 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(40)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(40) ‘biometric categorisation system’ means an AI system for the purpose of assigning natural persons to specific categories on the basis of their biometric data, unless it is ancillary to another commercial service and strictly necessary for objective technical reasons;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_41 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(41)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(41) ‘remote biometric identification system’ means an AI system for the purpose of identifying natural persons, without their active involvement, typically at a distance through the comparison of a person’s biometric data with the biometric data contained in a reference database;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_42 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(42)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(42) ‘real-time remote biometric identification system’ means a remote biometric identification system, whereby the capturing of biometric data, the comparison and the identification all occur without a significant delay, comprising not only instant identification, but also limited short delays in order to avoid circumvention;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_43 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(43)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(43) ‘post-remote biometric identification system’ means a remote biometric identification system other than a real-time remote biometric identification system;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_44 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(44)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(44) ‘publicly accessible space’ means any publicly or privately owned physical place accessible to an undetermined number of natural persons, regardless of whether certain conditions for access may apply, and regardless of the potential capacity restrictions;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_45 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(45)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(45) ‘law enforcement authority’ means:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_46 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(46)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(46) ‘law enforcement’ means activities carried out by law enforcement authorities or on their behalf for the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_47 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(47)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(47) ‘AI Office’ means the Commission’s function of contributing to the implementation, monitoring and supervision of AI systems and general-purpose AI models, and AI governance, provided for in Commission Decision of 24 January 2024; references in this Regulation to the AI Office shall be construed as references to the Commission;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_48 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(48)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(48) ‘national competent authority’ means a notifying authority or a market surveillance authority; as regards AI systems put into service or used by Union institutions, agencies, offices and bodies, references to national competent authorities or market surveillance authorities in this Regulation shall be construed as references to the European Data Protection Supervisor;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_49 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(49)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(49) ‘serious incident’ means an incident or malfunctioning of an AI system that directly or indirectly leads to any of the following:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(5) ‘authorised representative’ means a natural or legal person located or established in the Union who has received and accepted a written mandate from a provider of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model to, respectively, perform and carry out on its behalf the obligations and procedures established by this Regulation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_50 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(50)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(50) ‘personal data’ means personal data as defined in Article 4, point (1), of Regulation (EU) 2016/679;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_51 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(51)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(51) ‘non-personal data’ means data other than personal data as defined in Article 4, point (1), of Regulation (EU) 2016/679;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_52 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(52)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(52) ‘profiling’ means profiling as defined in Article 4, point (4), of Regulation (EU) 2016/679;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_53 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(53)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(53) ‘real-world testing plan’ means a document that describes the objectives, methodology, geographical, population and temporal scope, monitoring, organisation and conduct of testing in real-world conditions;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_54 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(54)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(54) ‘sandbox plan’ means a document agreed between the participating provider and the competent authority describing the objectives, conditions, timeframe, methodology and requirements for the activities carried out within the sandbox;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_55 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(55)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(55) ‘AI regulatory sandbox’ means a controlled framework set up by a competent authority which offers providers or prospective providers of AI systems the possibility to develop, train, validate and test, where appropriate in real-world conditions, an innovative AI system, pursuant to a sandbox plan for a limited time under regulatory supervision;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_56 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(56)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(56) ‘AI literacy’ means skills, knowledge and understanding that allow providers, deployers and affected persons, taking into account their respective rights and obligations in the context of this Regulation, to make an informed deployment of AI systems, as well as to gain awareness about the opportunities and risks of AI and possible harm it can cause;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_57 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(57)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(57) ‘testing in real-world conditions’ means the temporary testing of an AI system for its intended purpose in real-world conditions outside a laboratory or otherwise simulated environment, with a view to gathering reliable and robust data and to assessing and verifying the conformity of the AI system with the requirements of this Regulation and it does not qualify as placing the AI system on the market or putting it into service within the meaning of this Regulation, provided that all the conditions laid down in Article 57 or 60 are fulfilled;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_58 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(58)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(58) ‘subject’, for the purpose of real-world testing, means a natural person who participates in testing in real-world conditions;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_59 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(59)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(59) ‘informed consent’ means a subject’s freely given, specific, unambiguous and voluntary expression of his or her willingness to participate in a particular testing in real-world conditions, after having been informed of all aspects of the testing that are relevant to the subject’s decision to participate;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(6) ‘importer’ means a natural or legal person located or established in the Union that places on the market an AI system that bears the name or trademark of a natural or legal person established in a third country;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_60 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(60)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(60) ‘deep fake’ means AI-generated or manipulated image, audio or video content that resembles existing persons, objects, places, entities or events and would falsely appear to a person to be authentic or truthful;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_61 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(61)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(61) ‘widespread infringement’ means any act or omission contrary to Union law protecting the interest of individuals, which:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_62 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(62)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(62) ‘critical infrastructure’ means critical infrastructure as defined in Article 2, point (4), of Directive (EU) 2022/2557;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_63 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(63)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(63) ‘general-purpose AI model’ means an AI model, including where such an AI model is trained with a large amount of data using self-supervision at scale, that displays significant generality and is capable of competently performing a wide range of distinct tasks regardless of the way the model is placed on the market and that can be integrated into a variety of downstream systems or applications, except AI models that are used for research, development or prototyping activities before they are placed on the market;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_64 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(64)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(64) ‘high-impact capabilities’ means capabilities that match or exceed the capabilities recorded in the most advanced general-purpose AI models;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_65 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(65)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(65) ‘systemic risk’ means a risk that is specific to the high-impact capabilities of general-purpose AI models, having a significant impact on the Union market due to their reach, or due to actual or reasonably foreseeable negative effects on public health, safety, public security, fundamental rights, or the society as a whole, that can be propagated at scale across the value chain;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_66 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(66)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(66) ‘general-purpose AI system’ means an AI system which is based on a general-purpose AI model and which has the capability to serve a variety of purposes, both for direct use as well as for integration in other AI systems;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_67 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(67)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(67) ‘floating-point operation’ means any mathematical operation or assignment involving floating-point numbers, which are a subset of the real numbers typically represented on computers by an integer of fixed precision scaled by an integer exponent of a fixed base;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_68 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(68)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(68) ‘downstream provider’ means a provider of an AI system, including a general-purpose AI system, which integrates an AI model, regardless of whether the AI model is provided by themselves and vertically integrated or provided by another entity based on contractual relations."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(7) ‘distributor’ means a natural or legal person in the supply chain, other than the provider or the importer, that makes an AI system available on the Union market;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(8) ‘operator’ means a provider, product manufacturer, deployer, authorised representative, importer or distributor;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(9) ‘placing on the market’ means the first making available of an AI system or a general-purpose AI model on the Union market;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) any public authority competent for the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including the safeguarding against and the prevention of threats to public security; or"^^xsd:string,
        "(a) has harmed or is likely to harm the collective interests of individuals residing in at least two Member States other than the Member State in which:"^^xsd:string,
        "(a) the death of a person, or serious harm to a person’s health;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) a serious and irreversible disruption of the management or operation of critical infrastructure;"^^xsd:string,
        "(b) any other body or entity entrusted by Member State law to exercise public authority and public powers for the purposes of the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including the safeguarding against and the prevention of threats to public security;"^^xsd:string,
        "(b) has caused, causes or is likely to cause harm to the collective interests of individuals and has common features, including the same unlawful practice or the same interest being infringed, and is occurring concurrently, committed by the same operator, in at least three Member States;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the infringement of obligations under Union law intended to protect fundamental rights;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) serious harm to property or the environment;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) the act or omission originated or took place;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_ii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(ii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(ii) the provider concerned, or, where applicable, its authorised representative is located or established; or"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_3_iii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 3(iii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iii) the deployer is established, when the infringement is committed by the deployer;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 4"@en ;
    :hasSummary "Providers and deployers of AI systems shall take measures to ensure, to their best extent, a sufficient level of AI literacy of their staff and other persons dealing with the operation and use of AI systems on their behalf, taking into account their technical knowledge, experience, education and training and the context the AI systems are to be used in, and considering the persons or groups of persons on whom the AI systems are to be used."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_40_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 40(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. High-risk AI systems or general-purpose AI models which are in conformity with harmonised standards or parts thereof the references of which have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 shall be presumed to be in conformity with the requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, with the obligations set out in of Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3, of this Regulation, to the extent that those standards cover those requirements or obligations."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_40_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 40(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. In accordance with Article 10 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, the Commission shall issue, without undue delay, standardisation requests covering all requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter and, as applicable, standardisation requests covering obligations set out in Chapter V, Sections 2 and 3, of this Regulation. The standardisation request shall also ask for deliverables on reporting and documentation processes to improve AI systems’ resource performance, such as reducing the high-risk AI system’s consumption of energy and of other resources during its lifecycle, and on the energy-efficient development of general-purpose AI models. When preparing a standardisation request, the Commission shall consult the Board and relevant stakeholders, including the advisory forum."^^xsd:string,
        "The Commission shall request the European standardisation organisations to provide evidence of their best efforts to fulfil the objectives referred to in the first and the second subparagraph of this paragraph in accordance with Article 24 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012."^^xsd:string,
        "When issuing a standardisation request to European standardisation organisations, the Commission shall specify that standards have to be clear, consistent, including with the standards developed in the various sectors for products covered by the existing Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, and aiming to ensure that high-risk AI systems or general-purpose AI models placed on the market or put into service in the Union meet the relevant requirements or obligations laid down in this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_40_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 40(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The participants in the standardisation process shall seek to promote investment and innovation in AI, including through increasing legal certainty, as well as the competitiveness and growth of the Union market, to contribute to strengthening global cooperation on standardisation and taking into account existing international standards in the field of AI that are consistent with Union values, fundamental rights and interests, and to enhance multi-stakeholder governance ensuring a balanced representation of interests and the effective participation of all relevant stakeholders in accordance with Articles 5, 6, and 7 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission may adopt, implementing acts establishing common specifications for the requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, for the obligations set out in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V where the following conditions have been fulfilled:"^^xsd:string,
        "The implementing acts referred to in the first subparagraph of this paragraph shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)."^^xsd:string,
        "When drafting the common specifications, the Commission shall consult the advisory forum referred to in Article 67."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the Commission has requested, pursuant to Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, one or more European standardisation organisations to draft a harmonised standard for the requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter, or, as applicable, for the obligations set out in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V, and:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) no reference to harmonised standards covering the requirements referred to in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, the obligations referred to in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V has been published in the Official Journal of the European Union in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012, and no such reference is expected to be published within a reasonable period."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_1_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(1)(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) the request has not been accepted by any of the European standardisation organisations; or"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_1_ii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(1)(ii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(ii) the harmonised standards addressing that request are not delivered within the deadline set in accordance with Article 10(1) of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012; or"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_1_iii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(1)(iii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iii) the relevant harmonised standards insufficiently address fundamental rights concerns; or"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_1_iv a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(1)(iv)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iv) the harmonised standards do not comply with the request; and"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Before preparing a draft implementing act, the Commission shall inform the committee referred to in Article 22 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012 that it considers the conditions laid down in paragraph 1 of this Article to be fulfilled."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. High-risk AI systems or general-purpose AI models which are in conformity with the common specifications referred to in paragraph 1, or parts of those specifications, shall be presumed to be in conformity with the requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, to comply with the obligations referred to in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V, to the extent those common specifications cover those requirements or those obligations."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Where a harmonised standard is adopted by a European standardisation organisation and proposed to the Commission for the publication of its reference in the Official Journal of the European Union , the Commission shall assess the harmonised standard in accordance with Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012. When reference to a harmonised standard is published in the Official Journal of the European Union , the Commission shall repeal the implementing acts referred to in paragraph 1, or parts thereof which cover the same requirements set out in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, the same obligations set out in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. Where providers of high-risk AI systems or general-purpose AI models do not comply with the common specifications referred to in paragraph 1, they shall duly justify that they have adopted technical solutions that meet the requirements referred to in Section 2 of this Chapter or, as applicable, comply with the obligations set out in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V to a level at least equivalent thereto."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_41_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 41(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. Where a Member State considers that a common specification does not entirely meet the requirements set out in Section 2 or, as applicable, comply with obligations set out in Sections 2 and 3 of Chapter V, it shall inform the Commission thereof with a detailed explanation. The Commission shall assess that information and, if appropriate, amend the implementing act establishing the common specification concerned."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_42_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 42(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. High-risk AI systems that have been trained and tested on data reflecting the specific geographical, behavioural, contextual or functional setting within which they are intended to be used shall be presumed to comply with the relevant requirements laid down in Article 10(4)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_42_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 42(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. High-risk AI systems that have been certified or for which a statement of conformity has been issued under a cybersecurity scheme pursuant to Regulation (EU) 2019/881 and the references of which have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union shall be presumed to comply with the cybersecurity requirements set out in Article 15 of this Regulation in so far as the cybersecurity certificate or statement of conformity or parts thereof cover those requirements."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_43_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 43(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the common specifications referred to in point (a) exist, but the provider has not applied them;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_43_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 43(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) one or more of the harmonised standards referred to in point (a) has been published with a restriction, and only on the part of the standard that was restricted."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_43_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 43(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend Annexes VI and VII by updating them in light of technical progress."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_43_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 43(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend paragraphs 1 and 2 of this Article in order to subject high-risk AI systems referred to in points 2 to 8 of Annex III to the conformity assessment procedure referred to in Annex VII or parts thereof. The Commission shall adopt such delegated acts taking into account the effectiveness of the conformity assessment procedure based on internal control referred to in Annex VI in preventing or minimising the risks to health and safety and protection of fundamental rights posed by such systems, as well as the availability of adequate capacities and resources among notified bodies."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_44_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 44(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Certificates issued by notified bodies in accordance with Annex VII shall be drawn-up in a language which can be easily understood by the relevant authorities in the Member State in which the notified body is established."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_44_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 44(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Certificates shall be valid for the period they indicate, which shall not exceed five years for AI systems covered by Annex I, and four years for AI systems covered by Annex III. At the request of the provider, the validity of a certificate may be extended for further periods, each not exceeding five years for AI systems covered by Annex I, and four years for AI systems covered by Annex III, based on a re-assessment in accordance with the applicable conformity assessment procedures. Any supplement to a certificate shall remain valid, provided that the certificate which it supplements is valid."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_44_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 44(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Where a notified body finds that an AI system no longer meets the requirements set out in Section 2, it shall, taking account of the principle of proportionality, suspend or withdraw the certificate issued or impose restrictions on it, unless compliance with those requirements is ensured by appropriate corrective action taken by the provider of the system within an appropriate deadline set by the notified body. The notified body shall give reasons for its decision."^^xsd:string,
        "An appeal procedure against decisions of the notified bodies, including on conformity certificates issued, shall be available."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Notified bodies shall inform the notifying authority of the following:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) any Union technical documentation assessment certificates, any supplements to those certificates, and any quality management system approvals issued in accordance with the requirements of Annex VII;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) any refusal, restriction, suspension or withdrawal of a Union technical documentation assessment certificate or a quality management system approval issued in accordance with the requirements of Annex VII;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) any circumstances affecting the scope of or conditions for notification;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) any request for information which they have received from market surveillance authorities regarding conformity assessment activities;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_1_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(1)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) on request, conformity assessment activities performed within the scope of their notification and any other activity performed, including cross-border activities and subcontracting."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Each notified body shall inform the other notified bodies of:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) quality management system approvals which it has refused, suspended or withdrawn, and, upon request, of quality system approvals which it has issued;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) Union technical documentation assessment certificates or any supplements thereto which it has refused, withdrawn, suspended or otherwise restricted, and, upon request, of the certificates and/or supplements thereto which it has issued."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Each notified body shall provide the other notified bodies carrying out similar conformity assessment activities covering the same types of AI systems with relevant information on issues relating to negative and, on request, positive conformity assessment results."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_45_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 45(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Notified bodies shall safeguard the confidentiality of the information that they obtain, in accordance with Article 78."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_47_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 47(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The EU declaration of conformity shall state that the high-risk AI system concerned meets the requirements set out in Section 2. The EU declaration of conformity shall contain the information set out in Annex V, and shall be translated into a language that can be easily understood by the national competent authorities of the Member States in which the high-risk AI system is placed on the market or made available."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_47_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 47(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Where high-risk AI systems are subject to other Union harmonisation legislation which also requires an EU declaration of conformity, a single EU declaration of conformity shall be drawn up in respect of all Union law applicable to the high-risk AI system. The declaration shall contain all the information required to identify the Union harmonisation legislation to which the declaration relates."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_47_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 47(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. By drawing up the EU declaration of conformity, the provider shall assume responsibility for compliance with the requirements set out in Section 2. The provider shall keep the EU declaration of conformity up-to-date as appropriate."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_47_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 47(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend Annex V by updating the content of the EU declaration of conformity set out in that Annex, in order to introduce elements that become necessary in light of technical progress."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_49_4_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 49(4)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) Section A, points 1 to 10, of Annex VIII, with the exception of points 6, 8 and 9;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_49_4_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 49(4)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) Section B, points 1 to 5, and points 8 and 9 of Annex VIII;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_49_4_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 49(4)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) Section C, points 1 to 3, of Annex VIII;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_49_4_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 49(4)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) points 1, 2, 3 and 5, of Annex IX."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_50_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 50(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. Paragraphs 1 to 4 shall not affect the requirements and obligations set out in Chapter III, and shall be without prejudice to other transparency obligations laid down in Union or national law for deployers of AI systems."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_51_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 51(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. A general-purpose AI model shall be classified as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk if it meets any of the following conditions:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_52_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 52(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Where a general-purpose AI model meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a), the relevant provider shall notify the Commission without delay and in any event within two weeks after that requirement is met or it becomes known that it will be met. That notification shall include the information necessary to demonstrate that the relevant requirement has been met. If the Commission becomes aware of a general-purpose AI model presenting systemic risks of which it has not been notified, it may decide to designate it as a model with systemic risk."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_52_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 52(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The provider of a general-purpose AI model that meets the condition referred to in Article 51(1), point (a), may present, with its notification, sufficiently substantiated arguments to demonstrate that, exceptionally, although it meets that requirement, the general-purpose AI model does not present, due to its specific characteristics, systemic risks and therefore should not be classified as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_52_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 52(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Where the Commission concludes that the arguments submitted pursuant to paragraph 2 are not sufficiently substantiated and the relevant provider was not able to demonstrate that the general-purpose AI model does not present, due to its specific characteristics, systemic risks, it shall reject those arguments, and the general-purpose AI model shall be considered to be a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_52_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 52(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. The Commission may designate a general-purpose AI model as presenting systemic risks, ex officio or following a qualified alert from the scientific panel pursuant to Article 90(1), point (a), on the basis of criteria set out in Annex XIII."^^xsd:string,
        "The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend Annex XIII by specifying and updating the criteria set out in that Annex."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_52_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 52(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. Upon a reasoned request of a provider whose model has been designated as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk pursuant to paragraph 4, the Commission shall take the request into account and may decide to reassess whether the general-purpose AI model can still be considered to present systemic risks on the basis of the criteria set out in Annex XIII. Such a request shall contain objective, detailed and new reasons that have arisen since the designation decision. Providers may request reassessment at the earliest six months after the designation decision. Where the Commission, following its reassessment, decides to maintain the designation as a general-purpose AI model with systemic risk, providers may request reassessment at the earliest six months after that decision."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_52_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 52(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. The Commission shall ensure that a list of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk is published and shall keep that list up to date, without prejudice to the need to observe and protect intellectual property rights and confidential business information or trade secrets in accordance with Union and national law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_53_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 53(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Providers of general-purpose AI models shall:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_53_1_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 53(1)(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) enable providers of AI systems to have a good understanding of the capabilities and limitations of the general-purpose AI model and to comply with their obligations pursuant to this Regulation; and"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_53_1_ii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 53(1)(ii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(ii) contain, at a minimum, the elements set out in Annex XII;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_53_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 53(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The obligations set out in paragraph 1, points (a) and (b), shall not apply to providers of AI models that are released under a free and open-source licence that allows for the access, usage, modification, and distribution of the model, and whose parameters, including the weights, the information on the model architecture, and the information on model usage, are made publicly available. This exception shall not apply to general-purpose AI models with systemic risks."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_53_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 53(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Providers of general-purpose AI models shall cooperate as necessary with the Commission and the national competent authorities in the exercise of their competences and powers pursuant to this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_53_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 53(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Providers of general-purpose AI models may rely on codes of practice within the meaning of Article 56 to demonstrate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1 of this Article, until a harmonised standard is published. Compliance with European harmonised standards grants providers the presumption of conformity to the extent that those standards cover those obligations. Providers of general-purpose AI models who do not adhere to an approved code of practice or do not comply with a European harmonised standard shall demonstrate alternative adequate means of compliance for assessment by the Commission."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_53_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 53(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. For the purpose of facilitating compliance with Annex XI, in particular points 2 (d) and (e) thereof, the Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 to detail measurement and calculation methodologies with a view to allowing for comparable and verifiable documentation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_53_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 53(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97(2) to amend Annexes XI and XII in light of evolving technological developments."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_53_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 53(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. Any information or documentation obtained pursuant to this Article, including trade secrets, shall be treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_54_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 54(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The provider shall enable its authorised representative to perform the tasks specified in the mandate received from the provider."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_54_3_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 54(3)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) verify that the technical documentation specified in Annex XI has been drawn up and all obligations referred to in Article 53 and, where applicable, Article 55 have been fulfilled by the provider;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_54_3_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 54(3)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) keep a copy of the technical documentation specified in Annex XI at the disposal of the AI Office and national competent authorities, for a period of 10 years after the general-purpose AI model has been placed on the market, and the contact details of the provider that appointed the authorised representative;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_54_3_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 54(3)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) provide the AI Office, upon a reasoned request, with all the information and documentation, including that referred to in point (b), necessary to demonstrate compliance with the obligations in this Chapter;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_54_3_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 54(3)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) cooperate with the AI Office and competent authorities, upon a reasoned request, in any action they take in relation to the general-purpose AI model, including when the model is integrated into AI systems placed on the market or put into service in the Union."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_55_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 55(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. In addition to the obligations listed in Articles 53 and 54, providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk shall:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_55_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 55(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk may rely on codes of practice within the meaning of Article 56 to demonstrate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1 of this Article, until a harmonised standard is published. Compliance with European harmonised standards grants providers the presumption of conformity to the extent that those standards cover those obligations. Providers of general-purpose AI models with systemic risks who do not adhere to an approved code of practice or do not comply with a European harmonised standard shall demonstrate alternative adequate means of compliance for assessment by the Commission."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_55_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 55(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Any information or documentation obtained pursuant to this Article, including trade secrets, shall be treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_56_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 56(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The AI Office shall encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice at Union level in order to contribute to the proper application of this Regulation, taking into account international approaches."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_56_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 56(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the means to ensure that the information referred to in Article 53(1), points (a) and (b), is kept up to date in light of market and technological developments;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_56_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 56(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the adequate level of detail for the summary about the content used for training;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_56_2_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 56(2)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the identification of the type and nature of the systemic risks at Union level, including their sources, where appropriate;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_56_2_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 56(2)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the measures, procedures and modalities for the assessment and management of the systemic risks at Union level, including the documentation thereof, which shall be proportionate to the risks, take into consideration their severity and probability and take into account the specific challenges of tackling those risks in light of the possible ways in which such risks may emerge and materialise along the AI value chain."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Member States shall ensure that their competent authorities establish at least one AI regulatory sandbox at national level, which shall be operational by 2 August 2026. That sandbox may also be established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States. The Commission may provide technical support, advice and tools for the establishment and operation of AI regulatory sandboxes."^^xsd:string,
        "The obligation under the first subparagraph may also be fulfilled by participating in an existing sandbox in so far as that participation provides an equivalent level of national coverage for the participating Member States."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_10 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(10)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "10. National competent authorities shall ensure that, to the extent the innovative AI systems involve the processing of personal data or otherwise fall under the supervisory remit of other national authorities or competent authorities providing or supporting access to data, the national data protection authorities and those other national or competent authorities are associated with the operation of the AI regulatory sandbox and involved in the supervision of those aspects to the extent of their respective tasks and powers."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_11 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(11)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "11. The AI regulatory sandboxes shall not affect the supervisory or corrective powers of the competent authorities supervising the sandboxes, including at regional or local level. Any significant risks to health and safety and fundamental rights identified during the development and testing of such AI systems shall result in an adequate mitigation. National competent authorities shall have the power to temporarily or permanently suspend the testing process, or the participation in the sandbox if no effective mitigation is possible, and shall inform the AI Office of such decision. National competent authorities shall exercise their supervisory powers within the limits of the relevant law, using their discretionary powers when implementing legal provisions in respect of a specific AI regulatory sandbox project, with the objective of supporting innovation in AI in the Union."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_12 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(12)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "12. Providers and prospective providers participating in the AI regulatory sandbox shall remain liable under applicable Union and national liability law for any damage inflicted on third parties as a result of the experimentation taking place in the sandbox. However, provided that the prospective providers observe the specific plan and the terms and conditions for their participation and follow in good faith the guidance given by the national competent authority, no administrative fines shall be imposed by the authorities for infringements of this Regulation. Where other competent authorities responsible for other Union and national law were actively involved in the supervision of the AI system in the sandbox and provided guidance for compliance, no administrative fines shall be imposed regarding that law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_13 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(13)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "13. The AI regulatory sandboxes shall be designed and implemented in such a way that, where relevant, they facilitate cross-border cooperation between national competent authorities."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_14 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(14)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "14. National competent authorities shall coordinate their activities and cooperate within the framework of the Board."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_15 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(15)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "15. National competent authorities shall inform the AI Office and the Board of the establishment of a sandbox, and may ask them for support and guidance. The AI Office shall make publicly available a list of planned and existing sandboxes and keep it up to date in order to encourage more interaction in the AI regulatory sandboxes and cross-border cooperation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_16 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(16)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "16. National competent authorities shall submit annual reports to the AI Office and to the Board, from one year after the establishment of the AI regulatory sandbox and every year thereafter until its termination, and a final report. Those reports shall provide information on the progress and results of the implementation of those sandboxes, including best practices, incidents, lessons learnt and recommendations on their setup and, where relevant, on the application and possible revision of this Regulation, including its delegated and implementing acts, and on the application of other Union law supervised by the competent authorities within the sandbox. The national competent authorities shall make those annual reports or abstracts thereof available to the public, online. The Commission shall, where appropriate, take the annual reports into account when exercising its tasks under this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_17 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(17)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "17. The Commission shall develop a single and dedicated interface containing all relevant information related to AI regulatory sandboxes to allow stakeholders to interact with AI regulatory sandboxes and to raise enquiries with competent authorities, and to seek non-binding guidance on the conformity of innovative products, services, business models embedding AI technologies, in accordance with Article 62(1), point (c). The Commission shall proactively coordinate with national competent authorities, where relevant."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Additional AI regulatory sandboxes at regional or local level, or established jointly with the competent authorities of other Member States may also be established."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The European Data Protection Supervisor may also establish an AI regulatory sandbox for Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, and may exercise the roles and the tasks of national competent authorities in accordance with this Chapter."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Member States shall ensure that the competent authorities referred to in paragraphs 1 and 2 allocate sufficient resources to comply with this Article effectively and in a timely manner. Where appropriate, national competent authorities shall cooperate with other relevant authorities, and may allow for the involvement of other actors within the AI ecosystem. This Article shall not affect other regulatory sandboxes established under Union or national law. Member States shall ensure an appropriate level of cooperation between the authorities supervising those other sandboxes and the national competent authorities."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. AI regulatory sandboxes established under paragraph 1 shall provide for a controlled environment that fosters innovation and facilitates the development, training, testing and validation of innovative AI systems for a limited time before their being placed on the market or put into service pursuant to a specific sandbox plan agreed between the providers or prospective providers and the competent authority. Such sandboxes may include testing in real world conditions supervised therein."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. Competent authorities shall provide, as appropriate, guidance, supervision and support within the AI regulatory sandbox with a view to identifying risks, in particular to fundamental rights, health and safety, testing, mitigation measures, and their effectiveness in relation to the obligations and requirements of this Regulation and, where relevant, other Union and national law supervised within the sandbox."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. Competent authorities shall provide providers and prospective providers participating in the AI regulatory sandbox with guidance on regulatory expectations and how to fulfil the requirements and obligations set out in this Regulation."^^xsd:string,
        "Upon request of the provider or prospective provider of the AI system, the competent authority shall provide a written proof of the activities successfully carried out in the sandbox. The competent authority shall also provide an exit report detailing the activities carried out in the sandbox and the related results and learning outcomes. Providers may use such documentation to demonstrate their compliance with this Regulation through the conformity assessment process or relevant market surveillance activities. In this regard, the exit reports and the written proof provided by the national competent authority shall be taken positively into account by market surveillance authorities and notified bodies, with a view to accelerating conformity assessment procedures to a reasonable extent."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "8. Subject to the confidentiality provisions in Article 78, and with the agreement of the provider or prospective provider, the Commission and the Board shall be authorised to access the exit reports and shall take them into account, as appropriate, when exercising their tasks under this Regulation. If both the provider or prospective provider and the national competent authority explicitly agree, the exit report may be made publicly available through the single information platform referred to in this Article."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. The establishment of AI regulatory sandboxes shall aim to contribute to the following objectives:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_9_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(9)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) improving legal certainty to achieve regulatory compliance with this Regulation or, where relevant, other applicable Union and national law;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_9_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(9)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) supporting the sharing of best practices through cooperation with the authorities involved in the AI regulatory sandbox;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_9_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(9)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) fostering innovation and competitiveness and facilitating the development of an AI ecosystem;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_9_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(9)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) contributing to evidence-based regulatory learning;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_57_9_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 57(9)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) facilitating and accelerating access to the Union market for AI systems, in particular when provided by SMEs, including start-ups."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. In order to avoid fragmentation across the Union, the Commission shall adopt implementing acts specifying the detailed arrangements for the establishment, development, implementation, operation and supervision of the AI regulatory sandboxes. The implementing acts shall include common principles on the following issues:"^^xsd:string,
        "Those implementing acts shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) eligibility and selection criteria for participation in the AI regulatory sandbox;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) procedures for the application, participation, monitoring, exiting from and termination of the AI regulatory sandbox, including the sandbox plan and the exit report;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the terms and conditions applicable to the participants."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The implementing acts referred to in paragraph 1 shall ensure:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) that AI regulatory sandboxes are open to any applying provider or prospective provider of an AI system who fulfils eligibility and selection criteria, which shall be transparent and fair, and that national competent authorities inform applicants of their decision within three months of the application;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) that AI regulatory sandboxes allow broad and equal access and keep up with demand for participation; providers and prospective providers may also submit applications in partnerships with deployers and other relevant third parties;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_2_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(2)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) that the detailed arrangements for, and conditions concerning AI regulatory sandboxes support, to the best extent possible, flexibility for national competent authorities to establish and operate their AI regulatory sandboxes;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_2_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(2)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) that access to the AI regulatory sandboxes is free of charge for SMEs, including start-ups, without prejudice to exceptional costs that national competent authorities may recover in a fair and proportionate manner;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_2_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(2)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) that they facilitate providers and prospective providers, by means of the learning outcomes of the AI regulatory sandboxes, in complying with conformity assessment obligations under this Regulation and the voluntary application of the codes of conduct referred to in Article 95;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_2_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(2)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) that AI regulatory sandboxes facilitate the involvement of other relevant actors within the AI ecosystem, such as notified bodies and standardisation organisations, SMEs, including start-ups, enterprises, innovators, testing and experimentation facilities, research and experimentation labs and European Digital Innovation Hubs, centres of excellence, individual researchers, in order to allow and facilitate cooperation with the public and private sectors;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_2_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(2)(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) that procedures, processes and administrative requirements for application, selection, participation and exiting the AI regulatory sandbox are simple, easily intelligible, and clearly communicated in order to facilitate the participation of SMEs, including start-ups, with limited legal and administrative capacities and are streamlined across the Union, in order to avoid fragmentation and that participation in an AI regulatory sandbox established by a Member State, or by the European Data Protection Supervisor is mutually and uniformly recognised and carries the same legal effects across the Union;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_2_h a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(2)(h)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(h) that participation in the AI regulatory sandbox is limited to a period that is appropriate to the complexity and scale of the project and that may be extended by the national competent authority;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_2_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(2)(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) that AI regulatory sandboxes facilitate the development of tools and infrastructure for testing, benchmarking, assessing and explaining dimensions of AI systems relevant for regulatory learning, such as accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity, as well as measures to mitigate risks to fundamental rights and society at large."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Prospective providers in the AI regulatory sandboxes, in particular SMEs and start-ups, shall be directed, where relevant, to pre-deployment services such as guidance on the implementation of this Regulation, to other value-adding services such as help with standardisation documents and certification, testing and experimentation facilities, European Digital Innovation Hubs and centres of excellence."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_58_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 58(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Where national competent authorities consider authorising testing in real world conditions supervised within the framework of an AI regulatory sandbox to be established under this Article, they shall specifically agree the terms and conditions of such testing and, in particular, the appropriate safeguards with the participants, with a view to protecting fundamental rights, health and safety. Where appropriate, they shall cooperate with other national competent authorities with a view to ensuring consistent practices across the Union."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. In the AI regulatory sandbox, personal data lawfully collected for other purposes may be processed solely for the purpose of developing, training and testing certain AI systems in the sandbox when all of the following conditions are met:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) AI systems shall be developed for safeguarding substantial public interest by a public authority or another natural or legal person and in one or more of the following areas:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the data processed are necessary for complying with one or more of the requirements referred to in Chapter III, Section 2 where those requirements cannot effectively be fulfilled by processing anonymised, synthetic or other non-personal data;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) there are effective monitoring mechanisms to identify if any high risks to the rights and freedoms of the data subjects, as referred to in Article 35 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 and in Article 39 of Regulation (EU) 2018/1725, may arise during the sandbox experimentation, as well as response mechanisms to promptly mitigate those risks and, where necessary, stop the processing;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) any personal data to be processed in the context of the sandbox are in a functionally separate, isolated and protected data processing environment under the control of the prospective provider and only authorised persons have access to those data;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) providers can further share the originally collected data only in accordance with Union data protection law; any personal data created in the sandbox cannot be shared outside the sandbox;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) any processing of personal data in the context of the sandbox neither leads to measures or decisions affecting the data subjects nor does it affect the application of their rights laid down in Union law on the protection of personal data;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) any personal data processed in the context of the sandbox are protected by means of appropriate technical and organisational measures and deleted once the participation in the sandbox has terminated or the personal data has reached the end of its retention period;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_h a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(h)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(h) the logs of the processing of personal data in the context of the sandbox are kept for the duration of the participation in the sandbox, unless provided otherwise by Union or national law;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) a complete and detailed description of the process and rationale behind the training, testing and validation of the AI system is kept together with the testing results as part of the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV;"^^xsd:string,
        "(i) public safety and public health, including disease detection, diagnosis prevention, control and treatment and improvement of health care systems;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_ii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(ii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(ii) a high level of protection and improvement of the quality of the environment, protection of biodiversity, protection against pollution, green transition measures, climate change mitigation and adaptation measures;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_iii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(iii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iii) energy sustainability;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_iv a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(iv)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iv) safety and resilience of transport systems and mobility, critical infrastructure and networks;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_j a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(j)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(j) a short summary of the AI project developed in the sandbox, its objectives and expected results is published on the website of the competent authorities; this obligation shall not cover sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_1_v a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(1)(v)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(v) efficiency and quality of public administration and public services;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. For the purposes of the prevention, investigation, detection or prosecution of criminal offences or the execution of criminal penalties, including safeguarding against and preventing threats to public security, under the control and responsibility of law enforcement authorities, the processing of personal data in AI regulatory sandboxes shall be based on a specific Union or national law and subject to the same cumulative conditions as referred to in paragraph 1."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_59_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 59(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Paragraph 1 is without prejudice to Union or national law which excludes processing of personal data for other purposes than those explicitly mentioned in that law, as well as to Union or national law laying down the basis for the processing of personal data which is necessary for the purpose of developing, testing or training of innovative AI systems or any other legal basis, in compliance with Union law on the protection of personal data."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_5_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 5(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The following AI practices shall be prohibited:"^^xsd:string,
        "Point (h) of the first subparagraph is without prejudice to Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 for the processing of biometric data for purposes other than law enforcement."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_5_1_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 5(1)(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) detrimental or unfavourable treatment of certain natural persons or groups of persons in social contexts that are unrelated to the contexts in which the data was originally generated or collected;"^^xsd:string,
        "(i) the targeted search for specific victims of abduction, trafficking in human beings or sexual exploitation of human beings, as well as the search for missing persons;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_5_1_ii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 5(1)(ii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(ii) detrimental or unfavourable treatment of certain natural persons or groups of persons that is unjustified or disproportionate to their social behaviour or its gravity;"^^xsd:string,
        "(ii) the prevention of a specific, substantial and imminent threat to the life or physical safety of natural persons or a genuine and present or genuine and foreseeable threat of a terrorist attack;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_5_1_iii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 5(1)(iii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iii) the localisation or identification of a person suspected of having committed a criminal offence, for the purpose of conducting a criminal investigation or prosecution or executing a criminal penalty for offences referred to in Annex II and punishable in the Member State concerned by a custodial sentence or a detention order for a maximum period of at least four years."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_5_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 5(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the nature of the situation giving rise to the possible use, in particular the seriousness, probability and scale of the harm that would be caused if the system were not used;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_5_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 5(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the consequences of the use of the system for the rights and freedoms of all persons concerned, in particular the seriousness, probability and scale of those consequences."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_5_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 5(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. A Member State may decide to provide for the possibility to fully or partially authorise the use of ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for the purposes of law enforcement within the limits and under the conditions listed in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), and paragraphs 2 and 3. Member States concerned shall lay down in their national law the necessary detailed rules for the request, issuance and exercise of, as well as supervision and reporting relating to, the authorisations referred to in paragraph 3. Those rules shall also specify in respect of which of the objectives listed in paragraph 1, first subparagraph, point (h), including which of the criminal offences referred to in point (h)(iii) thereof, the competent authorities may be authorised to use those systems for the purposes of law enforcement. Member States shall notify those rules to the Commission at the latest 30 days following the adoption thereof. Member States may introduce, in accordance with Union law, more restrictive laws on the use of remote biometric identification systems."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_5_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 5(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "8. This Article shall not affect the prohibitions that apply where an AI practice infringes other Union law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_60_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 60(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions outside AI regulatory sandboxes may be conducted by providers or prospective providers of high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III, in accordance with this Article and the real-world testing plan referred to in this Article, without prejudice to the prohibitions under Article 5."^^xsd:string,
        "The Commission shall, by means of implementing acts, specify the detailed elements of the real-world testing plan. Those implementing acts shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)."^^xsd:string,
        "This paragraph shall be without prejudice to Union or national law on the testing in real world conditions of high-risk AI systems related to products covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_60_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 60(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Providers or prospective providers may conduct testing of high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III in real world conditions at any time before the placing on the market or the putting into service of the AI system on their own or in partnership with one or more deployers or prospective deployers."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_60_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 60(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The testing of high-risk AI systems in real world conditions under this Article shall be without prejudice to any ethical review that is required by Union or national law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_60_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 60(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Providers or prospective providers may conduct the testing in real world conditions only where all of the following conditions are met:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_60_4_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 60(4)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the market surveillance authority in the Member State where the testing in real world conditions is to be conducted has approved the testing in real world conditions and the real-world testing plan; where the market surveillance authority has not provided an answer within 30 days, the testing in real world conditions and the real-world testing plan shall be understood to have been approved; where national law does not provide for a tacit approval, the testing in real world conditions shall remain subject to an authorisation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_60_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 60(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. The provider or prospective provider shall be liable under applicable Union and national liability law for any damage caused in the course of their testing in real world conditions."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_62_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 62(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Member States shall undertake the following actions:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_62_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 62(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The AI Office shall undertake the following actions:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_63_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 63(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Microenterprises within the meaning of Recommendation 2003/361/EC may comply with certain elements of the quality management system required by Article 17 of this Regulation in a simplified manner, provided that they do not have partner enterprises or linked enterprises within the meaning of that Recommendation. For that purpose, the Commission shall develop guidelines on the elements of the quality management system which may be complied with in a simplified manner considering the needs of microenterprises, without affecting the level of protection or the need for compliance with the requirements in respect of high-risk AI systems."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_63_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 63(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Paragraph 1 of this Article shall not be interpreted as exempting those operators from fulfilling any other requirements or obligations laid down in this Regulation, including those established in Articles 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 72 and 73."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_64_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 64(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission shall develop Union expertise and capabilities in the field of AI through the AI Office."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_64_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 64(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Member States shall facilitate the tasks entrusted to the AI Office, as reflected in this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. A European Artificial Intelligence Board (the ‘Board’) is hereby established."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The Board shall be composed of one representative per Member State. The European Data Protection Supervisor shall participate as observer. The AI Office shall also attend the Board’s meetings, without taking part in the votes. Other national and Union authorities, bodies or experts may be invited to the meetings by the Board on a case by case basis, where the issues discussed are of relevance for them."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Each representative shall be designated by their Member State for a period of three years, renewable once."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Member States shall ensure that their representatives on the Board:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_4_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(4)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) have the relevant competences and powers in their Member State so as to contribute actively to the achievement of the Board’s tasks referred to in Article 66;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_4_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(4)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) are designated as a single contact point vis-à-vis the Board and, where appropriate, taking into account Member States’ needs, as a single contact point for stakeholders;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_4_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(4)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) are empowered to facilitate consistency and coordination between national competent authorities in their Member State as regards the implementation of this Regulation, including through the collection of relevant data and information for the purpose of fulfilling their tasks on the Board."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The designated representatives of the Member States shall adopt the Board’s rules of procedure by a two-thirds majority. The rules of procedure shall, in particular, lay down procedures for the selection process, the duration of the mandate of, and specifications of the tasks of, the Chair, detailed arrangements for voting, and the organisation of the Board’s activities and those of its sub-groups."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. The Board shall establish two standing sub-groups to provide a platform for cooperation and exchange among market surveillance authorities and notifying authorities about issues related to market surveillance and notified bodies respectively."^^xsd:string,
        "The Board may establish other standing or temporary sub-groups as appropriate for the purpose of examining specific issues. Where appropriate, representatives of the advisory forum referred to in Article 67 may be invited to such sub-groups or to specific meetings of those subgroups as observers."^^xsd:string,
        "The standing sub-group for market surveillance should act as the administrative cooperation group (ADCO) for this Regulation within the meaning of Article 30 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. The Board shall be organised and operated so as to safeguard the objectivity and impartiality of its activities."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_65_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 65(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "8. The Board shall be chaired by one of the representatives of the Member States. The AI Office shall provide the secretariat for the Board, convene the meetings upon request of the Chair, and prepare the agenda in accordance with the tasks of the Board pursuant to this Regulation and its rules of procedure."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66"@en ;
    :hasSummary "The Board shall advise and assist the Commission and the Member States in order to facilitate the consistent and effective application of this Regulation. To that end, the Board may in particular:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) contribute to the coordination among national competent authorities responsible for the application of this Regulation and, in cooperation with and subject to the agreement of the market surveillance authorities concerned, support joint activities of market surveillance authorities referred to in Article 74(11);"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) collect and share technical and regulatory expertise and best practices among Member States;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) provide advice on the implementation of this Regulation, in particular as regards the enforcement of rules on general-purpose AI models;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) contribute to the harmonisation of administrative practices in the Member States, including in relation to the derogation from the conformity assessment procedures referred to in Article 46, the functioning of AI regulatory sandboxes, and testing in real world conditions referred to in Articles 57, 59 and 60;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) at the request of the Commission or on its own initiative, issue recommendations and written opinions on any relevant matters related to the implementation of this Regulation and to its consistent and effective application, including:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) support the Commission in promoting AI literacy, public awareness and understanding of the benefits, risks, safeguards and rights and obligations in relation to the use of AI systems;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) facilitate the development of common criteria and a shared understanding among market operators and competent authorities of the relevant concepts provided for in this Regulation, including by contributing to the development of benchmarks;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_h a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(h)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(h) cooperate, as appropriate, with other Union institutions, bodies, offices and agencies, as well as relevant Union expert groups and networks, in particular in the fields of product safety, cybersecurity, competition, digital and media services, financial services, consumer protection, data and fundamental rights protection;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) contribute to effective cooperation with the competent authorities of third countries and with international organisations;"^^xsd:string,
        "(i) on the development and application of codes of conduct and codes of practice pursuant to this Regulation, as well as of the Commission’s guidelines;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_ii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(ii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(ii) the evaluation and review of this Regulation pursuant to Article 112, including as regards the serious incident reports referred to in Article 73, and the functioning of the EU database referred to in Article 71, the preparation of the delegated or implementing acts, and as regards possible alignments of this Regulation with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_iii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(iii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iii) on technical specifications or existing standards regarding the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_iv a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(iv)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iv) on the use of harmonised standards or common specifications referred to in Articles 40 and 41;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_j a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(j)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(j) assist national competent authorities and the Commission in developing the organisational and technical expertise required for the implementation of this Regulation, including by contributing to the assessment of training needs for staff of Member States involved in implementing this Regulation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_k a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(k)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(k) assist the AI Office in supporting national competent authorities in the establishment and development of AI regulatory sandboxes, and facilitate cooperation and information-sharing among AI regulatory sandboxes;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_l a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(l)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(l) contribute to, and provide relevant advice on, the development of guidance documents;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_m a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(m)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(m) advise the Commission in relation to international matters on AI;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_n a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(n)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(n) provide opinions to the Commission on the qualified alerts regarding general-purpose AI models;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_o a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(o)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(o) receive opinions by the Member States on qualified alerts regarding general-purpose AI models, and on national experiences and practices on the monitoring and enforcement of AI systems, in particular systems integrating the general-purpose AI models."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_v a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(v)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(v) trends, such as European global competitiveness in AI, the uptake of AI in the Union, and the development of digital skills;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_vi a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(vi)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(vi) trends on the evolving typology of AI value chains, in particular on the resulting implications in terms of accountability;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_66_vii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 66(vii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(vii) on the potential need for amendment to Annex III in accordance with Article 7, and on the potential need for possible revision of Article 5 pursuant to Article 112, taking into account relevant available evidence and the latest developments in technology;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_67_10 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 67(10)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "10. The advisory forum shall prepare an annual report on its activities. That report shall be made publicly available."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_67_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 67(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The membership of the advisory forum shall represent a balanced selection of stakeholders, including industry, start-ups, SMEs, civil society and academia. The membership of the advisory forum shall be balanced with regard to commercial and non-commercial interests and, within the category of commercial interests, with regard to SMEs and other undertakings."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_67_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 67(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The Commission shall appoint the members of the advisory forum, in accordance with the criteria set out in paragraph 2, from amongst stakeholders with recognised expertise in the field of AI."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_67_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 67(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. The term of office of the members of the advisory forum shall be two years, which may be extended by up to no more than four years."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_67_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 67(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The Fundamental Rights Agency, ENISA, the European Committee for Standardization (CEN), the European Committee for Electrotechnical Standardization (CENELEC), and the European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI) shall be permanent members of the advisory forum."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_67_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 67(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. The advisory forum shall draw up its rules of procedure. It shall elect two co-chairs from among its members, in accordance with criteria set out in paragraph 2. The term of office of the co-chairs shall be two years, renewable once."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_67_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 67(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. The advisory forum shall hold meetings at least twice a year. The advisory forum may invite experts and other stakeholders to its meetings."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_67_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 67(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. The advisory forum may establish standing or temporary sub-groups as appropriate for the purpose of examining specific questions related to the objectives of this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission shall, by means of an implementing act, make provisions on the establishment of a scientific panel of independent experts (the ‘scientific panel’) intended to support the enforcement activities under this Regulation. That implementing act shall be adopted in accordance with the examination procedure referred to in Article 98(2)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The scientific panel shall consist of experts selected by the Commission on the basis of up-to-date scientific or technical expertise in the field of AI necessary for the tasks set out in paragraph 3, and shall be able to demonstrate meeting all of the following conditions:"^^xsd:string,
        "The Commission, in consultation with the Board, shall determine the number of experts on the panel in accordance with the required needs and shall ensure fair gender and geographical representation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) having particular expertise and competence and scientific or technical expertise in the field of AI;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) independence from any provider of AI systems or general-purpose AI models;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_2_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(2)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) an ability to carry out activities diligently, accurately and objectively."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The scientific panel shall advise and support the AI Office, in particular with regard to the following tasks:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_3_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(3)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) supporting the implementation and enforcement of this Regulation as regards general-purpose AI models and systems, in particular by:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_3_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(3)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) supporting the work of market surveillance authorities, at their request;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_3_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(3)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) supporting cross-border market surveillance activities as referred to in Article 74(11), without prejudice to the powers of market surveillance authorities;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_3_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(3)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) supporting the AI Office in carrying out its duties in the context of the Union safeguard procedure pursuant to Article 81."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_3_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(3)(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) alerting the AI Office of possible systemic risks at Union level of general-purpose AI models, in accordance with Article 90;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_3_ii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(3)(ii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(ii) contributing to the development of tools and methodologies for evaluating capabilities of general-purpose AI models and systems, including through benchmarks;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_3_iii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(3)(iii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iii) providing advice on the classification of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_3_iv a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(3)(iv)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(iv) providing advice on the classification of various general-purpose AI models and systems;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_3_v a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(3)(v)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(v) contributing to the development of tools and templates;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. The experts on the scientific panel shall perform their tasks with impartiality and objectivity, and shall ensure the confidentiality of information and data obtained in carrying out their tasks and activities. They shall neither seek nor take instructions from anyone when exercising their tasks under paragraph 3. Each expert shall draw up a declaration of interests, which shall be made publicly available. The AI Office shall establish systems and procedures to actively manage and prevent potential conflicts of interest."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_68_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 68(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The implementing act referred to in paragraph 1 shall include provisions on the conditions, procedures and detailed arrangements for the scientific panel and its members to issue alerts, and to request the assistance of the AI Office for the performance of the tasks of the scientific panel."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_69_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 69(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Member States may call upon experts of the scientific panel to support their enforcement activities under this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_69_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 69(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The Member States may be required to pay fees for the advice and support provided by the experts. The structure and the level of fees as well as the scale and structure of recoverable costs shall be set out in the implementing act referred to in Article 68(1), taking into account the objectives of the adequate implementation of this Regulation, cost-effectiveness and the necessity of ensuring effective access to experts for all Member States."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_69_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 69(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The Commission shall facilitate timely access to the experts by the Member States, as needed, and ensure that the combination of support activities carried out by Union AI testing support pursuant to Article 84 and experts pursuant to this Article is efficiently organised and provides the best possible added value."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Irrespective of whether an AI system is placed on the market or put into service independently of the products referred to in points (a) and (b), that AI system shall be considered to be high-risk where both of the following conditions are fulfilled:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the AI system is intended to be used as a safety component of a product, or the AI system is itself a product, covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the product whose safety component pursuant to point (a) is the AI system, or the AI system itself as a product, is required to undergo a third-party conformity assessment, with a view to the placing on the market or the putting into service of that product pursuant to the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. In addition to the high-risk AI systems referred to in paragraph 1, AI systems referred to in Annex III shall be considered to be high-risk."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. By derogation from paragraph 2, an AI system referred to in Annex III shall not be considered to be high-risk where it does not pose a significant risk of harm to the health, safety or fundamental rights of natural persons, including by not materially influencing the outcome of decision making."^^xsd:string,
        "Notwithstanding the first subparagraph, an AI system referred to in Annex III shall always be considered to be high-risk where the AI system performs profiling of natural persons."^^xsd:string,
        "The first subparagraph shall apply where any of the following conditions is fulfilled:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_3_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(3)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the AI system is intended to perform a narrow procedural task;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_3_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(3)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the AI system is intended to improve the result of a previously completed human activity;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_3_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(3)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the AI system is intended to detect decision-making patterns or deviations from prior decision-making patterns and is not meant to replace or influence the previously completed human assessment, without proper human review; or"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_3_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(3)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the AI system is intended to perform a preparatory task to an assessment relevant for the purposes of the use cases listed in Annex III."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. A provider who considers that an AI system referred to in Annex III is not high-risk shall document its assessment before that system is placed on the market or put into service. Such provider shall be subject to the registration obligation set out in Article 49(2). Upon request of national competent authorities, the provider shall provide the documentation of the assessment."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The Commission shall, after consulting the European Artificial Intelligence Board (the ‘Board’), and no later than 2 February 2026, provide guidelines specifying the practical implementation of this Article in line with Article 96 together with a comprehensive list of practical examples of use cases of AI systems that are high-risk and not high-risk."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend paragraph 3, second subparagraph, of this Article by adding new conditions to those laid down therein, or by modifying them, where there is concrete and reliable evidence of the existence of AI systems that fall under the scope of Annex III, but do not pose a significant risk of harm to the health, safety or fundamental rights of natural persons."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. The Commission shall adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 in order to amend paragraph 3, second subparagraph, of this Article by deleting any of the conditions laid down therein, where there is concrete and reliable evidence that this is necessary to maintain the level of protection of health, safety and fundamental rights provided for by this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_6_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 6(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "8. Any amendment to the conditions laid down in paragraph 3, second subparagraph, adopted in accordance with paragraphs 6 and 7 of this Article shall not decrease the overall level of protection of health, safety and fundamental rights provided for by this Regulation and shall ensure consistency with the delegated acts adopted pursuant to Article 7(1), and take account of market and technological developments."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_70_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 70(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Member States shall communicate to the Commission the identity of the notifying authorities and the market surveillance authorities and the tasks of those authorities, as well as any subsequent changes thereto. Member States shall make publicly available information on how competent authorities and single points of contact can be contacted, through electronic communication means by 2 August 2025. Member States shall designate a market surveillance authority to act as the single point of contact for this Regulation, and shall notify the Commission of the identity of the single point of contact. The Commission shall make a list of the single points of contact publicly available."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_70_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 70(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. The Commission shall facilitate the exchange of experience between national competent authorities."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_70_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 70(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. Where Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies fall within the scope of this Regulation, the European Data Protection Supervisor shall act as the competent authority for their supervision."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_71_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 71(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission shall, in collaboration with the Member States, set up and maintain an EU database containing information referred to in paragraphs 2 and 3 of this Article concerning high-risk AI systems referred to in Article 6(2) which are registered in accordance with Articles 49 and 60 and AI systems that are not considered as high-risk pursuant to Article 6(3) and which are registered in accordance with Article 6(4) and Article 49. When setting the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the relevant experts, and when updating the functional specifications of such database, the Commission shall consult the Board."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_71_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 71(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The data listed in Sections A and B of Annex VIII shall be entered into the EU database by the provider or, where applicable, by the authorised representative."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_71_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 71(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The data listed in Section C of Annex VIII shall be entered into the EU database by the deployer who is, or who acts on behalf of, a public authority, agency or body, in accordance with Article 49(3) and (4)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_71_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 71(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. With the exception of the section referred to in Article 49(4) and Article 60(4), point (c), the information contained in the EU database registered in accordance with Article 49 shall be accessible and publicly available in a user-friendly manner. The information should be easily navigable and machine-readable. The information registered in accordance with Article 60 shall be accessible only to market surveillance authorities and the Commission, unless the prospective provider or provider has given consent for also making the information accessible the public."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_71_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 71(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The EU database shall contain personal data only in so far as necessary for collecting and processing information in accordance with this Regulation. That information shall include the names and contact details of natural persons who are responsible for registering the system and have the legal authority to represent the provider or the deployer, as applicable."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_71_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 71(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. The Commission shall be the controller of the EU database. It shall make available to providers, prospective providers and deployers adequate technical and administrative support. The EU database shall comply with the applicable accessibility requirements."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_73_10 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 73(10)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "10. For high-risk AI systems which are safety components of devices, or are themselves devices, covered by Regulations (EU) 2017/745 and (EU) 2017/746, the notification of serious incidents shall be limited to those referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c) of this Regulation, and shall be made to the national competent authority chosen for that purpose by the Member States where the incident occurred."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_73_11 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 73(11)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "11. National competent authorities shall immediately notify the Commission of any serious incident, whether or not they have taken action on it, in accordance with Article 20 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_73_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 73(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. Upon receiving a notification related to a serious incident referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c), the relevant market surveillance authority shall inform the national public authorities or bodies referred to in Article 77(1). The Commission shall develop dedicated guidance to facilitate compliance with the obligations set out in paragraph 1 of this Article. That guidance shall be issued by 2 August 2025, and shall be assessed regularly."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_73_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 73(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. For high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III that are placed on the market or put into service by providers that are subject to Union legislative instruments laying down reporting obligations equivalent to those set out in this Regulation, the notification of serious incidents shall be limited to those referred to in Article 3, point (49)(c)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply to AI systems covered by this Regulation. For the purposes of the effective enforcement of this Regulation:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_10 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(10)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "10. Member States shall facilitate coordination between market surveillance authorities designated under this Regulation and other relevant national authorities or bodies which supervise the application of Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, or in other Union law, that might be relevant for the high-risk AI systems referred to in Annex III."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_11 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(11)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "11. Market surveillance authorities and the Commission shall be able to propose joint activities, including joint investigations, to be conducted by either market surveillance authorities or market surveillance authorities jointly with the Commission, that have the aim of promoting compliance, identifying non-compliance, raising awareness or providing guidance in relation to this Regulation with respect to specific categories of high-risk AI systems that are found to present a serious risk across two or more Member States in accordance with Article 9 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. The AI Office shall provide coordination support for joint investigations."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_12 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(12)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "12. Without prejudice to the powers provided for under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, and where relevant and limited to what is necessary to fulfil their tasks, the market surveillance authorities shall be granted full access by providers to the documentation as well as the training, validation and testing data sets used for the development of high-risk AI systems, including, where appropriate and subject to security safeguards, through application programming interfaces (API) or other relevant technical means and tools enabling remote access."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_13 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(13)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "13. Market surveillance authorities shall be granted access to the source code of the high-risk AI system upon a reasoned request and only when both of the following conditions are fulfilled:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_13_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(13)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) access to source code is necessary to assess the conformity of a high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2; and"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_13_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(13)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) testing or auditing procedures and verifications based on the data and documentation provided by the provider have been exhausted or proved insufficient."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_14 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(14)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "14. Any information or documentation obtained by market surveillance authorities shall be treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) any reference to an economic operator under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall be understood as including all operators identified in Article 2(1) of this Regulation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) any reference to a product under Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall be understood as including all AI systems falling within the scope of this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. As part of their reporting obligations under Article 34(4) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, the market surveillance authorities shall report annually to the Commission and relevant national competition authorities any information identified in the course of market surveillance activities that may be of potential interest for the application of Union law on competition rules. They shall also annually report to the Commission about the use of prohibited practices that occurred during that year and about the measures taken."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. For high-risk AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section A of Annex I, the market surveillance authority for the purposes of this Regulation shall be the authority responsible for market surveillance activities designated under those legal acts."^^xsd:string,
        "By derogation from the first subparagraph, and in appropriate circumstances, Member States may designate another relevant authority to act as a market surveillance authority, provided they ensure coordination with the relevant sectoral market surveillance authorities responsible for the enforcement of the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. The procedures referred to in Articles 79 to 83 of this Regulation shall not apply to AI systems related to products covered by the Union harmonisation legislation listed in section A of Annex I, where such legal acts already provide for procedures ensuring an equivalent level of protection and having the same objective. In such cases, the relevant sectoral procedures shall apply instead."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. Without prejudice to the powers of market surveillance authorities under Article 14 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, for the purpose of ensuring the effective enforcement of this Regulation, market surveillance authorities may exercise the powers referred to in Article 14(4), points (d) and (j), of that Regulation remotely, as appropriate."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. For high-risk AI systems placed on the market, put into service, or used by financial institutions regulated by Union financial services law, the market surveillance authority for the purposes of this Regulation shall be the relevant national authority responsible for the financial supervision of those institutions under that legislation in so far as the placing on the market, putting into service, or the use of the AI system is in direct connection with the provision of those financial services."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. By way of derogation from paragraph 6, in appropriate circumstances, and provided that coordination is ensured, another relevant authority may be identified by the Member State as market surveillance authority for the purposes of this Regulation."^^xsd:string,
        "National market surveillance authorities supervising regulated credit institutions regulated under Directive 2013/36/EU, which are participating in the Single Supervisory Mechanism established by Regulation (EU) No 1024/2013, should report, without delay, to the European Central Bank any information identified in the course of their market surveillance activities that may be of potential interest for the prudential supervisory tasks of the European Central Bank specified in that Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "8. For high-risk AI systems listed in point 1 of Annex III to this Regulation, in so far as the systems are used for law enforcement purposes, border management and justice and democracy, and for high-risk AI systems listed in points 6, 7 and 8 of Annex III to this Regulation, Member States shall designate as market surveillance authorities for the purposes of this Regulation either the competent data protection supervisory authorities under Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Directive (EU) 2016/680, or any other authority designated pursuant to the same conditions laid down in Articles 41 to 44 of Directive (EU) 2016/680. Market surveillance activities shall in no way affect the independence of judicial authorities, or otherwise interfere with their activities when acting in their judicial capacity."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_74_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 74(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. Where Union institutions, bodies, offices or agencies fall within the scope of this Regulation, the European Data Protection Supervisor shall act as their market surveillance authority, except in relation to the Court of Justice of the European Union acting in its judicial capacity."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_76_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 76(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Where a market surveillance authority has been informed by the prospective provider, the provider or any third party of a serious incident or has other grounds for considering that the conditions set out in Articles 60 and 61 are not met, it may take either of the following decisions on its territory, as appropriate:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_77_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 77(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. By 2 November 2024, each Member State shall identify the public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 and make a list of them publicly available. Member States shall notify the list to the Commission and to the other Member States, and shall keep the list up to date."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_77_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 77(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Any information or documentation obtained by the national public authorities or bodies referred to in paragraph 1 of this Article pursuant to this Article shall be treated in accordance with the confidentiality obligations set out in Article 78."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_78_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 78(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission, market surveillance authorities and notified bodies and any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation shall, in accordance with Union or national law, respect the confidentiality of information and data obtained in carrying out their tasks and activities in such a manner as to protect, in particular:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_78_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 78(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the intellectual property rights and confidential business information or trade secrets of a natural or legal person, including source code, except in the cases referred to in Article 5 of Directive (EU) 2016/943 of the European Parliament and of the Council ( 57 ) ;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_78_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 78(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the effective implementation of this Regulation, in particular for the purposes of inspections, investigations or audits;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_78_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 78(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) public and national security interests;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_78_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 78(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the conduct of criminal or administrative proceedings;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_78_1_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 78(1)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) information classified pursuant to Union or national law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_78_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 78(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The authorities involved in the application of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1 shall request only data that is strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of their powers in accordance with this Regulation and with Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. They shall put in place adequate and effective cybersecurity measures to protect the security and confidentiality of the information and data obtained, and shall delete the data collected as soon as it is no longer needed for the purpose for which it was obtained, in accordance with applicable Union or national law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_78_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 78(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Without prejudice to paragraphs 1 and 2, information exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission shall not be disclosed without prior consultation of the originating national competent authority and the deployer when high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities and when such disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests. This exchange of information shall not cover sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities."^^xsd:string,
        "When the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III, the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV shall remain within the premises of those authorities. Those authorities shall ensure that the market surveillance authorities referred to in Article 74(8) and (9), as applicable, can, upon request, immediately access the documentation or obtain a copy thereof. Only staff of the market surveillance authority holding the appropriate level of security clearance shall be allowed to access that documentation or any copy thereof."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_78_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 78(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 shall not affect the rights or obligations of the Commission, Member States and their relevant authorities, as well as those of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings, including in the context of cross-border cooperation, nor shall they affect the obligations of the parties concerned to provide information under criminal law of the Member States."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_78_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 78(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The Commission and Member States may exchange, where necessary and in accordance with relevant provisions of international and trade agreements, confidential information with regulatory authorities of third countries with which they have concluded bilateral or multilateral confidentiality arrangements guaranteeing an adequate level of confidentiality."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_79_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 79(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. AI systems presenting a risk shall be understood as a ‘product presenting a risk’ as defined in Article 3, point 19 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, in so far as they present risks to the health or safety, or to fundamental rights, of persons."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_79_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 79(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. The operator shall ensure that all appropriate corrective action is taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned that it has made available on the Union market."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_79_6_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 79(6)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_79_6_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 79(6)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) a failure of a high-risk AI system to meet requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_79_6_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 79(6)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) shortcomings in the harmonised standards or common specifications referred to in Articles 40 and 41 conferring a presumption of conformity;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_79_6_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 79(6)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) non-compliance with Article 50."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 to amend Annex III by adding or modifying use-cases of high-risk AI systems where both of the following conditions are fulfilled:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the AI systems are intended to be used in any of the areas listed in Annex III;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the AI systems pose a risk of harm to health and safety, or an adverse impact on fundamental rights, and that risk is equivalent to, or greater than, the risk of harm or of adverse impact posed by the high-risk AI systems already referred to in Annex III."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. When assessing the condition under paragraph 1, point (b), the Commission shall take into account the following criteria:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the intended purpose of the AI system;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the extent to which an AI system has been used or is likely to be used;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the nature and amount of the data processed and used by the AI system, in particular whether special categories of personal data are processed;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the extent to which the AI system acts autonomously and the possibility for a human to override a decision or recommendations that may lead to potential harm;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) the extent to which the use of an AI system has already caused harm to health and safety, has had an adverse impact on fundamental rights or has given rise to significant concerns in relation to the likelihood of such harm or adverse impact, as demonstrated, for example, by reports or documented allegations submitted to national competent authorities or by other reports, as appropriate;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) the potential extent of such harm or such adverse impact, in particular in terms of its intensity and its ability to affect multiple persons or to disproportionately affect a particular group of persons;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) the extent to which persons who are potentially harmed or suffer an adverse impact are dependent on the outcome produced with an AI system, in particular because for practical or legal reasons it is not reasonably possible to opt-out from that outcome;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_h a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(h)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(h) the extent to which there is an imbalance of power, or the persons who are potentially harmed or suffer an adverse impact are in a vulnerable position in relation to the deployer of an AI system, in particular due to status, authority, knowledge, economic or social circumstances, or age;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) effective measures of redress in relation to the risks posed by an AI system, with the exclusion of claims for damages;"^^xsd:string,
        "(i) the extent to which the outcome produced involving an AI system is easily corrigible or reversible, taking into account the technical solutions available to correct or reverse it, whereby outcomes having an adverse impact on health, safety or fundamental rights, shall not be considered to be easily corrigible or reversible;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_ii a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(ii)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(ii) effective measures to prevent or substantially minimise those risks."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_j a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(j)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(j) the magnitude and likelihood of benefit of the deployment of the AI system for individuals, groups, or society at large, including possible improvements in product safety;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_2_k a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(2)(k)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(k) the extent to which existing Union law provides for:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The Commission is empowered to adopt delegated acts in accordance with Article 97 to amend the list in Annex III by removing high-risk AI systems where both of the following conditions are fulfilled:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_3_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(3)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the high-risk AI system concerned no longer poses any significant risks to fundamental rights, health or safety, taking into account the criteria listed in paragraph 2;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_7_3_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 7(3)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the deletion does not decrease the overall level of protection of health, safety and fundamental rights under Union law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_80_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 80(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Where, in the course of that evaluation, the market surveillance authority finds that the AI system concerned is high-risk, it shall without undue delay require the relevant provider to take all necessary actions to bring the AI system into compliance with the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation, as well as take appropriate corrective action within a period the market surveillance authority may prescribe."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_80_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 80(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Where the market surveillance authority considers that the use of the AI system concerned is not restricted to its national territory, it shall inform the Commission and the other Member States without undue delay of the results of the evaluation and of the actions which it has required the provider to take."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_80_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 80(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The provider shall ensure that all appropriate corrective action is taken in respect of all the AI systems concerned that it has made available on the Union market."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_80_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 80(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. Where the provider of the AI system concerned does not take adequate corrective action within the period referred to in paragraph 2 of this Article, Article 79(5) to (9) shall apply."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_81_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 81(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Where, within three months of receipt of the notification referred to in Article 79(5), or within 30 days in the case of non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5, objections are raised by the market surveillance authority of a Member State to a measure taken by another market surveillance authority, or where the Commission considers the measure to be contrary to Union law, the Commission shall without undue delay enter into consultation with the market surveillance authority of the relevant Member State and the operator or operators, and shall evaluate the national measure. On the basis of the results of that evaluation, the Commission shall, within six months, or within 60 days in the case of non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5, starting from the notification referred to in Article 79(5), decide whether the national measure is justified and shall notify its decision to the market surveillance authority of the Member State concerned. The Commission shall also inform all other market surveillance authorities of its decision."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_81_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 81(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Where the Commission considers the measure taken by the relevant Member State to be justified, all Member States shall ensure that they take appropriate restrictive measures in respect of the AI system concerned, such as requiring the withdrawal of the AI system from their market without undue delay, and shall inform the Commission accordingly. Where the Commission considers the national measure to be unjustified, the Member State concerned shall withdraw the measure and shall inform the Commission accordingly."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_81_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 81(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Where the national measure is considered justified and the non-compliance of the AI system is attributed to shortcomings in the harmonised standards or common specifications referred to in Articles 40 and 41 of this Regulation, the Commission shall apply the procedure provided for in Article 11 of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_83_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 83(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the CE marking has been affixed in violation of Article 48;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_83_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 83(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the CE marking has not been affixed;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_83_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 83(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 has not been drawn up;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_83_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 83(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 has not been drawn up correctly;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_83_1_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 83(1)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) the registration in the EU database referred to in Article 71 has not been carried out;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_83_1_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 83(1)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) where applicable, no authorised representative has been appointed;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_83_1_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 83(1)(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) technical documentation is not available."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_84_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 84(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission shall designate one or more Union AI testing support structures to perform the tasks listed under Article 21(6) of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 in the area of AI."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_84_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 84(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Without prejudice to the tasks referred to in paragraph 1, Union AI testing support structures shall also provide independent technical or scientific advice at the request of the Board, the Commission, or of market surveillance authorities."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_85 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 85"@en ;
    :hasSummary "In accordance with Regulation (EU) 2019/1020, such complaints shall be taken into account for the purpose of conducting market surveillance activities, and shall be handled in line with the dedicated procedures established therefor by the market surveillance authorities."^^xsd:string,
        "Without prejudice to other administrative or judicial remedies, any natural or legal person having grounds to consider that there has been an infringement of the provisions of this Regulation may submit complaints to the relevant market surveillance authority."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_86_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 86(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Paragraph 1 shall not apply to the use of AI systems for which exceptions from, or restrictions to, the obligation under that paragraph follow from Union or national law in compliance with Union law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_86_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 86(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. This Article shall apply only to the extent that the right referred to in paragraph 1 is not otherwise provided for under Union law."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_87 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 87"@en ;
    :hasSummary "Directive (EU) 2019/1937 shall apply to the reporting of infringements of this Regulation and the protection of persons reporting such infringements."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_88_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 88(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission shall have exclusive powers to supervise and enforce Chapter V, taking into account the procedural guarantees under Article 94. The Commission shall entrust the implementation of these tasks to the AI Office, without prejudice to the powers of organisation of the Commission and the division of competences between Member States and the Union based on the Treaties."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_88_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 88(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Without prejudice to Article 75(3), market surveillance authorities may request the Commission to exercise the powers laid down in this Section, where that is necessary and proportionate to assist with the fulfilment of their tasks under this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_89_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 89(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Downstream providers shall have the right to lodge a complaint alleging an infringement of this Regulation. A complaint shall be duly reasoned and indicate at least:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_89_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 89(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the point of contact of the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_89_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 89(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) a description of the relevant facts, the provisions of this Regulation concerned, and the reason why the downstream provider considers that the provider of the general-purpose AI model concerned infringed this Regulation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_89_2_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 89(2)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) any other information that the downstream provider that sent the request considers relevant, including, where appropriate, information gathered on its own initiative."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_90_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 90(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The scientific panel may provide a qualified alert to the AI Office where it has reason to suspect that:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_90_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 90(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) a general-purpose AI model poses concrete identifiable risk at Union level; or"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_90_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 90(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) a general-purpose AI model meets the conditions referred to in Article 51."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_90_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 90(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Upon such qualified alert, the Commission, through the AI Office and after having informed the Board, may exercise the powers laid down in this Section for the purpose of assessing the matter. The AI Office shall inform the Board of any measure according to Articles 91 to 94."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_90_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 90(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. A qualified alert shall be duly reasoned and indicate at least:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_90_3_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 90(3)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the point of contact of the provider of the general-purpose AI model with systemic risk concerned;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_90_3_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 90(3)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) a description of the relevant facts and the reasons for the alert by the scientific panel;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_90_3_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 90(3)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) any other information that the scientific panel considers to be relevant, including, where appropriate, information gathered on its own initiative."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_92_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 92(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) to assess compliance of the provider with obligations under this Regulation, where the information gathered pursuant to Article 91 is insufficient; or"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_92_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 92(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) to investigate systemic risks at Union level of general-purpose AI models with systemic risk, in particular following a qualified alert from the scientific panel in accordance with Article 90(1), point (a)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_93_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 93(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. Where necessary and appropriate, the Commission may request providers to:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_93_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 93(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) take appropriate measures to comply with the obligations set out in Articles 53 and 54;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_93_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 93(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) implement mitigation measures, where the evaluation carried out in accordance with Article 92 has given rise to serious and substantiated concern of a systemic risk at Union level;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_93_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 93(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) restrict the making available on the market, withdraw or recall the model."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_93_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 93(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Before a measure is requested, the AI Office may initiate a structured dialogue with the provider of the general-purpose AI model."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_93_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 93(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. If, during the structured dialogue referred to in paragraph 2, the provider of the general-purpose AI model with systemic risk offers commitments to implement mitigation measures to address a systemic risk at Union level, the Commission may, by decision, make those commitments binding and declare that there are no further grounds for action."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_94 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 94"@en ;
    :hasSummary "Article 18 of Regulation (EU) 2019/1020 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the providers of the general-purpose AI model, without prejudice to more specific procedural rights provided for in this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_95_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 95(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The AI Office and the Member States shall encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct, including related governance mechanisms, intended to foster the voluntary application to AI systems, other than high-risk AI systems, of some or all of the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2 taking into account the available technical solutions and industry best practices allowing for the application of such requirements."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_95_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 95(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The AI Office and the Member States shall facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct concerning the voluntary application, including by deployers, of specific requirements to all AI systems, on the basis of clear objectives and key performance indicators to measure the achievement of those objectives, including elements such as, but not limited to:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_95_2_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 95(2)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) applicable elements provided for in Union ethical guidelines for trustworthy AI;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_95_2_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 95(2)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) assessing and minimising the impact of AI systems on environmental sustainability, including as regards energy-efficient programming and techniques for the efficient design, training and use of AI;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_95_2_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 95(2)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) promoting AI literacy, in particular that of persons dealing with the development, operation and use of AI;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_95_2_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 95(2)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) facilitating an inclusive and diverse design of AI systems, including through the establishment of inclusive and diverse development teams and the promotion of stakeholders’ participation in that process;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_95_2_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 95(2)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) assessing and preventing the negative impact of AI systems on vulnerable persons or groups of vulnerable persons, including as regards accessibility for persons with a disability, as well as on gender equality."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_95_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 95(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Codes of conduct may be drawn up by individual providers or deployers of AI systems or by organisations representing them or by both, including with the involvement of any interested stakeholders and their representative organisations, including civil society organisations and academia. Codes of conduct may cover one or more AI systems taking into account the similarity of the intended purpose of the relevant systems."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_96_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 96(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission shall develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation, and in particular on:"^^xsd:string,
        "The guidelines referred to in the first subparagraph of this paragraph shall take due account of the generally acknowledged state of the art on AI, as well as of relevant harmonised standards and common specifications that are referred to in Articles 40 and 41, or of those harmonised standards or technical specifications that are set out pursuant to Union harmonisation law."^^xsd:string,
        "When issuing such guidelines, the Commission shall pay particular attention to the needs of SMEs including start-ups, of local public authorities and of the sectors most likely to be affected by this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_96_1_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 96(1)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the application of the requirements and obligations referred to in Articles 8 to 15 and in Article 25;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_96_1_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 96(1)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the prohibited practices referred to in Article 5;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_96_1_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 96(1)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the practical implementation of the provisions related to substantial modification;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_96_1_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 96(1)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the practical implementation of transparency obligations laid down in Article 50;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_96_1_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 96(1)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) detailed information on the relationship of this Regulation with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, as well as with other relevant Union law, including as regards consistency in their enforcement;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_96_1_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 96(1)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) the application of the definition of an AI system as set out in Article 3, point (1)."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_96_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 96(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. At the request of the Member States or the AI Office, or on its own initiative, the Commission shall update guidelines previously adopted when deemed necessary."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_97_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 97(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The power to adopt delegated acts is conferred on the Commission subject to the conditions laid down in this Article."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_97_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 97(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The power to adopt delegated acts referred to in Article 6(6) and (7), Article 7(1) and (3), Article 11(3), Article 43(5) and (6), Article 47(5), Article 51(3), Article 52(4) and Article 53(5) and (6) shall be conferred on the Commission for a period of five years from 1 August 2024. The Commission shall draw up a report in respect of the delegation of power not later than nine months before the end of the five-year period. The delegation of power shall be tacitly extended for periods of an identical duration, unless the European Parliament or the Council opposes such extension not later than three months before the end of each period."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_97_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 97(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. The delegation of power referred to in Article 6(6) and (7), Article 7(1) and (3), Article 11(3), Article 43(5) and (6), Article 47(5), Article 51(3), Article 52(4) and Article 53(5) and (6) may be revoked at any time by the European Parliament or by the Council. A decision of revocation shall put an end to the delegation of power specified in that decision. It shall take effect the day following that of its publication in the Official Journal of the European Union or at a later date specified therein. It shall not affect the validity of any delegated acts already in force."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_97_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 97(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Before adopting a delegated act, the Commission shall consult experts designated by each Member State in accordance with the principles laid down in the Interinstitutional Agreement of 13 April 2016 on Better Law-Making."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_97_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 97(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. As soon as it adopts a delegated act, the Commission shall notify it simultaneously to the European Parliament and to the Council."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_97_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 97(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. Any delegated act adopted pursuant to Article 6(6) or (7), Article 7(1) or (3), Article 11(3), Article 43(5) or (6), Article 47(5), Article 51(3), Article 52(4) or Article 53(5) or (6) shall enter into force only if no objection has been expressed by either the European Parliament or the Council within a period of three months of notification of that act to the European Parliament and the Council or if, before the expiry of that period, the European Parliament and the Council have both informed the Commission that they will not object. That period shall be extended by three months at the initiative of the European Parliament or of the Council."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_98_1 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 98(1)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "1. The Commission shall be assisted by a committee. That committee shall be a committee within the meaning of Regulation (EU) No 182/2011."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_98_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 98(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. Where reference is made to this paragraph, Article 5 of Regulation (EU) No 182/2011 shall apply."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_10 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(10)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "10. The exercise of powers under this Article shall be subject to appropriate procedural safeguards in accordance with Union and national law, including effective judicial remedies and due process."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_11 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(11)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "11. Member States shall, on an annual basis, report to the Commission about the administrative fines they have issued during that year, in accordance with this Article, and about any related litigation or judicial proceedings."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The Member States shall, without delay and at the latest by the date of entry into application, notify the Commission of the rules on penalties and of other enforcement measures referred to in paragraph 1, and shall notify it, without delay, of any subsequent amendment to them."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_3 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(3)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "3. Non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5 shall be subject to administrative fines of up to EUR 35 000 000 or, if the offender is an undertaking, up to 7 % of its total worldwide annual turnover for the preceding financial year, whichever is higher."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_4 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(4)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "4. Non-compliance with any of the following provisions related to operators or notified bodies, other than those laid down in Articles 5, shall be subject to administrative fines of up to EUR 15 000 000 or, if the offender is an undertaking, up to 3 % of its total worldwide annual turnover for the preceding financial year, whichever is higher:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_4_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(4)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_4_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(4)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_4_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(4)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) obligations of importers pursuant to Article 23;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_4_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(4)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) obligations of distributors pursuant to Article 24;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_4_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(4)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) obligations of deployers pursuant to Article 26;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_4_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(4)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_4_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(4)(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) transparency obligations for providers and deployers pursuant to Article 50."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_5 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(5)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "5. The supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request shall be subject to administrative fines of up to EUR 7 500 000 or, if the offender is an undertaking, up to 1 % of its total worldwide annual turnover for the preceding financial year, whichever is higher."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_6 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(6)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "6. In the case of SMEs, including start-ups, each fine referred to in this Article shall be up to the percentages or amount referred to in paragraphs 3, 4 and 5, whichever thereof is lower."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "7. When deciding whether to impose an administrative fine and when deciding on the amount of the administrative fine in each individual case, all relevant circumstances of the specific situation shall be taken into account and, as appropriate, regard shall be given to the following:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement and of its consequences, taking into account the purpose of the AI system, as well as, where appropriate, the number of affected persons and the level of damage suffered by them;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) whether administrative fines have already been applied by other market surveillance authorities to the same operator for the same infringement;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) whether administrative fines have already been applied by other authorities to the same operator for infringements of other Union or national law, when such infringements result from the same activity or omission constituting a relevant infringement of this Regulation;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7_d a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)(d)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the size, the annual turnover and market share of the operator committing the infringement;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7_e a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)(e)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(e) any other aggravating or mitigating factor applicable to the circumstances of the case, such as financial benefits gained, or losses avoided, directly or indirectly, from the infringement;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7_f a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)(f)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(f) the degree of cooperation with the national competent authorities, in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7_g a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)(g)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(g) the degree of responsibility of the operator taking into account the technical and organisational measures implemented by it;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7_h a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)(h)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(h) the manner in which the infringement became known to the national competent authorities, in particular whether, and if so to what extent, the operator notified the infringement;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7_i a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)(i)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(i) the intentional or negligent character of the infringement;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_7_j a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(7)(j)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(j) any action taken by the operator to mitigate the harm suffered by the affected persons."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_8 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(8)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "8. Each Member State shall lay down rules on to what extent administrative fines may be imposed on public authorities and bodies established in that Member State."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_99_9 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 99(9)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "9. Depending on the legal system of the Member States, the rules on administrative fines may be applied in such a manner that the fines are imposed by competent national courts or by other bodies, as applicable in those Member States. The application of such rules in those Member States shall have an equivalent effect."^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_9_2 a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 9(2)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "2. The risk management system shall be understood as a continuous iterative process planned and run throughout the entire lifecycle of a high-risk AI system, requiring regular systematic review and updating. It shall comprise the following steps:"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_9_5_a a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 9(5)(a)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(a) elimination or reduction of risks identified and evaluated pursuant to paragraph 2 in as far as technically feasible through adequate design and development of the high-risk AI system;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_9_5_b a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 9(5)(b)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(b) where appropriate, implementation of adequate mitigation and control measures addressing risks that cannot be eliminated;"^^xsd:string .

:Paragraph_Article_9_5_c a :Paragraph ;
    rdfs:label "Article 9(5)(c)"@en ;
    :hasSummary "(c) provision of information required pursuant to Article 13 and, where appropriate, training to deployers."^^xsd:string .

:TestingPlan_Annex_IX a airo:Documentation ;
    rdfs:label "Annex IX real-world testing plan"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IX ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasRequiredComponent :testing_plan_field_annix .

:advisory_power_art56 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art56"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office shall encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of practice at Union level"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_56 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office shall encourage, facilitate, monitor, and assess the drawing up, implementation, and adequacy of codes of practice at Union level for the proper application of this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art56_2 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art56_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office and the Board shall aim to ensure that the codes of practice cover at least the obligations provided for in Articles 53 and 55"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_56 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_56_2 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office and the Board shall aim to ensure that codes of practice cover obligations from Articles 53 and 55 including systemic risks and risk management measures."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art56_3 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art56_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office may invite all providers of general-purpose AI models, as well as relevant national competent authorities, to participate"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_56 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_56_3 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office may invite providers of general-purpose AI models and relevant authorities to participate in drawing up codes of practice."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art56_4 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art56_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office and the Board shall aim to ensure that the codes of practice clearly set out their specific objectives and contain commitments"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_56 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_56_4 ;
    :hasSummary "Codes of practice shall clearly set out specific objectives, commitments or measures, and consider needs of all interested parties at Union level."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art56_5 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art56_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office shall aim to ensure that participants to the codes of practice report regularly to the AI Office on the implementation"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_56 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_56_5 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office shall aim to ensure participants in codes of practice report regularly on implementation and outcomes, reflecting differences between participants."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art56_6 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art56_6"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office and the Board shall regularly monitor and evaluate the achievement of the objectives of the codes of practice"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_56 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_56_6 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office and the Board shall regularly monitor and evaluate codes of practice achievement and publish assessments; the Commission may approve codes by implementing act."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art56_7 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art56_7"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office may invite all providers of general-purpose AI models to adhere to the codes of practice"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_56 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_56_7 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office may invite providers of general-purpose AI models to adhere to codes of practice, limiting obligations for those not presenting systemic risks unless they opt-in fully."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art56_8 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art56_8"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office shall, as appropriate, also encourage and facilitate the review and adaptation of the codes of practice"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_56 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_56_8 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office shall encourage and facilitate the review and adaptation of codes of practice as appropriate, including assessing available standards."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art56_9 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art56_9"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Codes of practice shall be ready at the latest by 2 May 2025...If a code cannot be finalised or is deemed inadequate, the Commission may provide common rules"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_56 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_56_9 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office shall take steps to have codes of practice ready by 2 May 2025 and may trigger Commission implementing acts to establish common rules if codes are inadequate or delayed."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art66 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art66"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The Board shall advise and assist the Commission and the Member States in order to facilitate the consistent and effective application of this Regulation."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_66 ;
    :hasSummary "The Board shall advise and assist the Commission and Member States for consistent and effective application of the Regulation, including issuing recommendations, opinions, and supporting the Commission in multiple roles."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art67 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art67"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: An advisory forum shall be established to provide technical expertise and advise the Board and the Commission"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_67 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_67_1 ;
    :hasSummary "An advisory forum shall be established to provide technical expertise, advise the Board and the Commission, and contribute to their tasks under this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art67_8 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art67_8"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The advisory forum may prepare opinions, recommendations and written contributions at the request of the Board or the Commission"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_67 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_67_8 ;
    :hasSummary "The advisory forum may prepare opinions, recommendations and written contributions at the request of the Board or the Commission."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art70_8 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art70_8"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: National competent authorities may provide guidance and advice on the implementation of this Regulation...consulted, as appropriate."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_70 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_70_8 ;
    :hasSummary "National competent authorities may provide guidance and advice on implementing this Regulation, especially to SMEs and start-ups, consulting other Union law authorities when relevant."^^xsd:string .

:advisory_power_art92_6 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "advisory_power_art92_6"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The Commission shall adopt implementing acts setting out detailed arrangements and the conditions for the evaluations"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_92 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_92_6 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission shall adopt implementing acts detailing arrangements and conditions for evaluations, including involving independent experts and their selection procedure."^^xsd:string .

:ai_office_voluntary_model_terms_art25_4 a :AdvisoryPower ;
    rdfs:label "ai_office_voluntary_model_terms_art25_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM5"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office may develop and recommend voluntary model terms for contracts...shall be published and be available free of charge in an easily usable electronic format"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_25 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_25_4 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office may develop and recommend voluntary model contract terms between high-risk AI system providers and third parties, considering sector-specific contractual requirements, and publish them free of charge in an electronic format."^^xsd:string .

:appropriate_data_transfer_safeguards_art60_4e a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "appropriate_data_transfer_safeguards_art60_4e"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM9"@en,
        "evidence: data collected and processed...shall be transferred to third countries only provided that appropriate and applicable safeguards under Union law are implemented"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_4_e ;
    :hasSummary "Data collected for testing may be transferred to third countries only if appropriate and applicable safeguards under Union law are implemented."^^xsd:string .

:appropriate_measures_deployers_high_risk_ai_art26_1 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "appropriate_measures_deployers_high_risk_ai_art26_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: Deployers of high-risk AI systems shall take appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure they use such systems in accordance with the instructions for use"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_26 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_26_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Deployers of high-risk AI systems shall take appropriate technical and organisational measures to ensure use in accordance with instructions for use."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_assessment_obligation_art15_1 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_assessment_obligation_art15_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: High-risk AI systems shall be designed and developed ... appropriate level of accuracy, robustness, and cybersecurity"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_15 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_15_1 ;
    :hasSummary "High-risk AI systems must be designed and developed to achieve appropriate levels of accuracy, robustness, and cybersecurity, and perform consistently throughout their lifecycle."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_assessment_obligation_art23_1_a a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_assessment_obligation_art23_1_a"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: importers shall ensure ... the relevant conformity assessment procedure ... has been carried out"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_23 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_23_1_a ;
    :hasSummary "Importers must verify that the relevant conformity assessment procedure has been carried out by the provider before placing a high-risk AI system on the market."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_assessment_obligation_art23_1_b a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_assessment_obligation_art23_1_b"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the provider has drawn up the technical documentation in accordance with Article 11 and Annex IV"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_11,
        :Article_23 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_23_1_b ;
    :hasSummary "Importers must verify that the provider has drawn up the technical documentation according to Article 11 and Annex IV before placing a high-risk AI system on the market."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_assessment_obligation_art23_1_c a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_assessment_obligation_art23_1_c"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM3"@en,
        "evidence: the system bears the required CE marking and is accompanied by the EU declaration of conformity ... and instructions for use"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_23 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_23_1_c ;
    :hasSummary "Importers must verify that the system bears the required CE marking and is accompanied by the EU declaration of conformity and instructions for use before market placement."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_assessment_obligation_art23_1_d a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_assessment_obligation_art23_1_d"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the provider has appointed an authorised representative in accordance with Article 22(1)"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_22,
        :Article_23 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_23_1_d ;
    :hasSummary "Importers must verify that the provider appointed an authorised representative in accordance with Article 22(1) before placing the system on the market."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_assessment_obligation_art34_1 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_assessment_obligation_art34_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "evidence: Notified bodies shall verify the conformity of high-risk AI systems in accordance with the conformity assessment procedures set out in Article 43."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_34,
        :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_34_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Notified bodies must verify the conformity of high-risk AI systems following the procedures in Article 43."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_assessment_obligation_continuously_learning_art43_4 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_assessment_obligation_continuously_learning_art43_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: changes... that have been pre-determined by the provider... shall not constitute a substantial modification"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_43_4 ;
    :hasSummary "Changes predetermined and documented at initial conformity assessment for high-risk AI systems that continue to learn are not considered substantial modifications."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_assessment_obligation_substantial_modification_art43_4 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_assessment_obligation_substantial_modification_art43_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: shall undergo a new conformity assessment procedure in the event of a substantial modification"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_43_4 ;
    :hasSummary "High-risk AI systems already assessed must undergo a new conformity assessment if substantially modified, regardless of distribution or usage continuation."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_1 a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_1"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "1. Introduction"^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_2 a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_2"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "2. Overview"^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_3 a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_3"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "3. Quality management system"^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_3_a a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_3_a"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the name and address of the provider and, if the application is lodged by an authorised representative, also their name and address;"^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_3_b a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_3_b"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "(b) the list of AI systems covered under the same quality management system;"^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_3_c a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_3_c"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the technical documentation for each AI system covered under the same quality management system;"^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_3_d a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_3_d"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the documentation concerning the quality management system which shall cover all the aspects listed under Article 17;"^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_3_e a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_3_e"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "(e) a description of the procedures in place to ensure that the quality management system remains adequate and effective;"^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_3_f a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_3_f"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "(f) a written declaration that the same application has not been lodged with any other notified body."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_4 a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_4"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "4. Control of the technical documentation."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_4_a a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_4_a"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "(a) the name and address of the provider;"^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_4_b a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_4_b"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "(b) a written declaration that the same application has not been lodged with any other notified body;"^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_4_c a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_4_c"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV."^^xsd:string .

:conformity_step_annvii_5 a :ConformityAssessmentStep ;
    rdfs:label "conformity_step_annvii_5"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VII ;
    :hasComponentOf :ThirdPartyAssessment_Annex_VII ;
    :hasSummary "The approved quality management system for the design, development and testing of AI systems pursuant to Article 17 shall be examined in accordance with point 3 and shall be subject to surveillance as specified in point 5. The technical documentation of the AI system shall be examined in accordance with point 4."^^xsd:string .

:cooperation_and_roles_in_testing_art60_4h a :ProceduralCondition ;
    rdfs:label "cooperation_and_roles_in_testing_art60_4h"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "evidence: provider...and the deployer...shall conclude an agreement specifying their roles and responsibilities to ensure compliance with testing provisions"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_4_h ;
    :hasSummary "If testing involves deployers, they must be informed of relevant aspects, given instructions for use, and an agreement specifying roles and responsibilities must be concluded."^^xsd:string .

:cooperation_obligation_between_market_authorities_and_ai_office_art75_2 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "cooperation_obligation_between_market_authorities_and_ai_office_art75_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: shall cooperate with the AI Office to carry out compliance evaluations, and shall inform the Board and other market surveillance authorities"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_75 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_75_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities shall cooperate with the AI Office to carry out compliance evaluations of general-purpose AI systems potentially used for high-risk purposes and inform the Board and other authorities."^^xsd:string .

:cooperation_with_authorities_deployers_art26_12 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "cooperation_with_authorities_deployers_art26_12"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: Deployers shall cooperate with the relevant competent authorities in any action those authorities take"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_26 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_26_12 ;
    :hasSummary "Deployers shall cooperate with competent authorities in actions related to the high-risk AI system to ensure implementation of this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:corrective_action_obligation_art20_1 a :PostMarketMonitoringObligation ;
    rdfs:label "corrective_action_obligation_art20_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: Providers... shall immediately take the necessary corrective actions to bring that system into conformity, to withdraw it, to disable it, or to recall it"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_20 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_20_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems must immediately take corrective actions if a system is not in conformity, including bringing it into conformity, withdrawal, disabling, or recall, and inform relevant parties."^^xsd:string .

:data_governance_obligation_art10_2 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "data_governance_obligation_art10_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: Training, validation and testing data sets shall be subject to data governance and management practices appropriate for the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_10 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_10_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Training, validation, and testing data sets must be subject to data governance practices appropriate for the intended purpose, covering design, collection, preparation, assumptions, availability, bias examination and mitigation, and addressing data gaps."^^xsd:string .

:data_protection_impact_assessment_deployers_art26_9 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "data_protection_impact_assessment_deployers_art26_9"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: deployers ... shall use the information provided under Article 13 ... to comply with their obligation to carry out a data protection impact assessment"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_13,
        :Article_26 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_26_9 ;
    :hasSummary "Deployers shall use information provided under Article 13 to comply with data protection impact assessments under EU data protection law."^^xsd:string .

:data_quality_obligation_art10_3 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "data_quality_obligation_art10_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: Training, validation and testing data sets shall be relevant, sufficiently representative, and to the best extent possible, free of errors and complete in view of the intended purpose."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_10 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_10_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Training, validation, and testing data sets must be relevant, sufficiently representative, as error-free and complete as possible, and have appropriate statistical properties relevant to the intended purpose."^^xsd:string .

:data_relevance_and_representation_deployers_art26_4 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "data_relevance_and_representation_deployers_art26_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: deployers shall ensure that input data is relevant and sufficiently representative in view of the intended purpose of the high-risk AI system"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_26 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_26_4 ;
    :hasSummary "Deployers exercising control over input data shall ensure it is relevant and sufficiently representative for the AI system's intended purpose."^^xsd:string .

:deployer_human_oversight_measures_art14_3b a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "deployer_human_oversight_measures_art14_3b"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: Measures identified by provider before placing ... that are appropriate to be implemented by the deployer."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_3_b ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must identify human oversight measures appropriate for implementation by the deployer before market placement or service."^^xsd:string .

:distributor_cooperation_with_authorities_art24_6 a :PostMarketMonitoringObligation ;
    rdfs:label "distributor_cooperation_with_authorities_art24_6"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: Distributors shall cooperate with the relevant competent authorities in any action those authorities take"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_24 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_24_6 ;
    :hasSummary "Distributors shall cooperate with competent authorities in actions to reduce or mitigate risks posed by high-risk AI systems they made available on the market."^^xsd:string .

:distributor_corrective_actions_art24_4 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "distributor_corrective_actions_art24_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM10"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: shall take the corrective actions necessary to bring that system into conformity ... withdraw it or recall it ... distributor shall immediately inform the provider or importer and the authorities"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_24 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_24_4 ;
    :hasSummary "If a distributor considers a high-risk AI system non-conformant after market availability, they must act to bring it into conformity, withdraw, recall, or ensure corrective actions by others and inform authorities if risk exists."^^xsd:string .

:distributor_info_provide_to_authorities_art24_5 a :PostMarketMonitoringObligation ;
    rdfs:label "distributor_info_provide_to_authorities_art24_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: distributors of a high-risk AI system shall provide that authority with all the information and documentation"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_24 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_24_5 ;
    :hasSummary "Distributors must provide competent authorities with information and documentation on their actions related to the conformity of high-risk AI systems upon reasoned request."^^xsd:string .

:distributor_nonconformity_prevent_market_art24_2 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "distributor_nonconformity_prevent_market_art24_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: shall not make the high-risk AI system available on the market until the system has been brought into conformity... distributor shall inform the provider or the importer"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_24 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_24_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Distributors shall not make a high-risk AI system available on the market if they consider it non-conformant with Section 2 requirements and must inform provider or importer if it presents a risk."^^xsd:string .

:distributor_storage_transport_compliance_art24_3 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "distributor_storage_transport_compliance_art24_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: Distributors shall ensure that... storage or transport conditions... do not jeopardise the compliance of the system"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_24 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_24_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Distributors shall ensure that storage or transport conditions do not jeopardise compliance of a high-risk AI system while under their responsibility."^^xsd:string .

:distributor_verification_before_market_art24_1 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "distributor_verification_before_market_art24_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: distributors shall verify that it bears the required CE marking, that it is accompanied by a copy of the EU declaration of conformity ... and instructions for use"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_24 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_24_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Distributors must verify that a high-risk AI system bears the required CE marking, has the EU declaration of conformity and instructions, and that the provider/importer complied with their obligations before making it available on the market."^^xsd:string .

:documentation_component_anniv a :DocumentationComponent ;
    rdfs:label "documentation_component_anniv"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IV ;
    :hasComponentOf :TechnicalDocumentation_Annex_IV ;
    :hasSummary "The technical documentation referred to in Article 11(1) shall contain at least the following information, as applicable to the relevant AI system:"^^xsd:string .

:documentation_component_anniv_a a :DocumentationComponent ;
    rdfs:label "documentation_component_anniv_a"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IV ;
    :hasComponentOf :TechnicalDocumentation_Annex_IV ;
    :hasSummary "(a) its intended purpose, the name of the provider and the version of the system reflecting its relation to previous versions;"^^xsd:string .

:documentation_component_anniv_b a :DocumentationComponent ;
    rdfs:label "documentation_component_anniv_b"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IV ;
    :hasComponentOf :TechnicalDocumentation_Annex_IV ;
    :hasSummary "(b) how the AI system interacts with, or can be used to interact with, hardware or software, including with other AI systems, that are not part of the AI system itself, where applicable;"^^xsd:string .

:documentation_component_anniv_c a :DocumentationComponent ;
    rdfs:label "documentation_component_anniv_c"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IV ;
    :hasComponentOf :TechnicalDocumentation_Annex_IV ;
    :hasSummary "(c) the versions of relevant software or firmware, and any requirements related to version updates;"^^xsd:string .

:documentation_component_anniv_d a :DocumentationComponent ;
    rdfs:label "documentation_component_anniv_d"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IV ;
    :hasComponentOf :TechnicalDocumentation_Annex_IV ;
    :hasSummary "(d) the description of all the forms in which the AI system is placed on the market or put into service, such as software packages embedded into hardware, downloads, or APIs;"^^xsd:string .

:documentation_component_anniv_e a :DocumentationComponent ;
    rdfs:label "documentation_component_anniv_e"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IV ;
    :hasComponentOf :TechnicalDocumentation_Annex_IV ;
    :hasSummary "(e) the description of the hardware on which the AI system is intended to run;"^^xsd:string .

:documentation_component_anniv_f a :DocumentationComponent ;
    rdfs:label "documentation_component_anniv_f"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IV ;
    :hasComponentOf :TechnicalDocumentation_Annex_IV ;
    :hasSummary "(f) where the AI system is a component of products, photographs or illustrations showing external features, the marking and internal layout of those products;"^^xsd:string .

:documentation_component_anniv_g a :DocumentationComponent ;
    rdfs:label "documentation_component_anniv_g"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IV ;
    :hasComponentOf :TechnicalDocumentation_Annex_IV ;
    :hasSummary "(g) a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer;"^^xsd:string .

:documentation_component_anniv_h a :DocumentationComponent ;
    rdfs:label "documentation_component_anniv_h"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IV ;
    :hasComponentOf :TechnicalDocumentation_Annex_IV ;
    :hasSummary "(h) instructions for use for the deployer, and a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer, where applicable;"^^xsd:string .

:double_verification_requirement_for_identification_systems_art14_5 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "double_verification_requirement_for_identification_systems_art14_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: No action or decision is taken ... unless identification has been separately verified and confirmed by at least two natural persons."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_5 ;
    :hasSummary "For high-risk AI systems used for identification per Annex III point 1(a), deployer actions or decisions based on identification require separate verification by at least two competent natural persons, except where disproportionate under law for law enforcement, migration, border control or asylum."^^xsd:string .

:effective_oversight_and_qualified_personnel_art60_4j a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "effective_oversight_and_qualified_personnel_art60_4j"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM9"@en,
        "evidence: testing...is effectively overseen by...persons who are suitably qualified and have necessary capacity, training and authority"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_4_j ;
    :hasSummary "Testing must be effectively overseen by the provider and deployers through suitably qualified and authorized persons with necessary training and capacity."^^xsd:string .

:enforcement_power_art101 a :EnforcementPower ;
    rdfs:label "enforcement_power_art101"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM4"@en,
        "evidence: The Commission may impose on providers of general-purpose AI models fines not exceeding 3 % of their annual total worldwide turnover... or EUR 15 000 000, whichever is higher."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_101 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_101_1 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission may impose fines on providers of general-purpose AI models for infringements of this Regulation and related obligations, with fines up to 3% of annual worldwide turnover or EUR 15 million, whichever is higher."^^xsd:string .

:enforcement_power_art37_4 a :EnforcementPower ;
    rdfs:label "enforcement_power_art37_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM4"@en,
        "evidence: Where the Commission ascertains that a notified body does not meet the requirements... it shall inform the notifying Member State... the Commission may... suspend, restrict or withdraw the designation"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_37 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_37_4 ;
    :hasSummary "If a notified body does not meet or no longer meets requirements, the Commission shall inform the notifying Member State and may suspend, restrict, or withdraw the designation by an implementing act if necessary."^^xsd:string .

:enforcement_power_art73_8 a :EnforcementPower ;
    rdfs:label "enforcement_power_art73_8"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM4"@en,
        "evidence: The market surveillance authority shall take appropriate measures ... within seven days from the date it received the notification ... and shall follow the notification procedures."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_73 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_73_8 ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authority shall take appropriate measures within seven days after receiving serious incident notifications and follow notification procedures per Regulation (EU) 2019/1020."^^xsd:string .

:enforcement_power_art80_4 a :EnforcementPower ;
    rdfs:label "enforcement_power_art80_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM4"@en,
        "evidence: the provider shall be subject to fines in accordance with Article 99"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_80,
        :Article_99 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_80_4 ;
    :hasSummary "If a provider does not bring a misclassified AI system into compliance within the prescribed period, the provider shall be subject to fines under Article 99."^^xsd:string .

:enforcement_power_art80_7 a :EnforcementPower ;
    rdfs:label "enforcement_power_art80_7"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM4"@en,
        "evidence: the provider shall be subject to fines in accordance with Article 99"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_80,
        :Article_99 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_80_7 ;
    :hasSummary "If the provider misclassified an AI system as non-high-risk to circumvent requirements, the provider shall be subject to fines in accordance with Article 99."^^xsd:string .

:enforcement_power_art83 a :EnforcementPower ;
    rdfs:label "enforcement_power_art83"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM4"@en,
        "evidence: it shall require the relevant provider to put an end to the non-compliance concerned, within a period it may prescribe"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_83 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_83_1 ;
    :hasSummary "The market surveillance authority shall require the provider to end non-compliance regarding CE marking, declaration of conformity, registration, authorized representative, and technical documentation within a prescribed period."^^xsd:string .

:enforcement_power_art83_restriction_prohibition a :EnforcementPower ;
    rdfs:label "enforcement_power_art83_restriction_prohibition"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM4"@en,
        "evidence: the market surveillance authority...shall take appropriate and proportionate measures to restrict or prohibit the high-risk AI system being made available on the market or to ensure that it is recalle"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_83 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_83_2 ;
    :hasSummary "If non-compliance persists, the market surveillance authority shall take appropriate and proportionate measures to restrict, prohibit, recall, or withdraw the high-risk AI system from the market without delay."^^xsd:string .

:enforcement_power_art99 a :EnforcementPower ;
    rdfs:label "enforcement_power_art99"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM4"@en,
        "evidence: Member States shall lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures...effective, proportionate and dissuasive."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_99 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_99_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Member States shall lay down rules on penalties and enforcement measures applicable to infringements of this Regulation and ensure their effective and proportionate implementation."^^xsd:string .

:fria_obligation_art27_1 a :FRIAObligation ;
    rdfs:label "fria_obligation_art27_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: deployers... shall perform an assessment of the impact on fundamental rights that the use of such system may produce"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_27 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_27_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Before deploying a high-risk AI system, certain deployers must perform a fundamental rights impact assessment including descriptions of use, affected persons, risks, human oversight, and risk mitigation measures."^^xsd:string .

:fria_obligation_art27_2 a :FRIAObligation ;
    rdfs:label "fria_obligation_art27_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: The obligation laid down in paragraph 1 applies to the first use... deployer shall take the necessary steps to update"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_27 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_27_2 ;
    :hasSummary "The fundamental rights impact assessment obligation applies at first use, can rely on previous assessments, and must be updated if relevant elements change."^^xsd:string .

:fria_obligation_art27_3 a :FRIAObligation ;
    rdfs:label "fria_obligation_art27_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: deployer shall notify the market surveillance authority of its results... submitting the filled-out template"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_27,
        :Article_46 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_27_3 ;
    :hasSummary "After performing the fundamental rights impact assessment, deployers must notify the market surveillance authority with a completed template, except when exempted by Article 46(1)."^^xsd:string .

:fria_obligation_art27_4 a :FRIAObligation ;
    rdfs:label "fria_obligation_art27_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: If any of the obligations... met through the data protection impact assessment... fundamental rights impact assessment shall complement it"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_27 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_27_4 ;
    :hasSummary "When a data protection impact assessment exists as per Regulation (EU) 2016/679 or Directive (EU) 2016/680, the fundamental rights impact assessment shall complement it."^^xsd:string .

:fria_obligation_art27_5 a :FRIAObligation ;
    rdfs:label "fria_obligation_art27_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office shall develop a template for a questionnaire, including through an automated tool"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_27 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_27_5 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office must develop a template questionnaire, possibly as an automated tool, to help deployers comply with the fundamental rights impact assessment obligations."^^xsd:string .

:high_risk_ai_system_compliance_obligation_art8_1 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "high_risk_ai_system_compliance_obligation_art8_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: High-risk AI systems shall comply with the requirements laid down in this Section, taking into account their intended purpose as well as the generally acknowledged state of the art"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_8,
        :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_8_1 ;
    :hasSummary "High-risk AI systems shall comply with the requirements laid down in this Section, considering their intended purpose and the generally acknowledged state of the art on AI and AI-related technologies, taking into account the risk management system in Article 9."^^xsd:string .

:human_oversight_aim_risk_prevention_art14_2 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "human_oversight_aim_risk_prevention_art14_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: Human oversight shall aim to prevent or minimise the risks to health, safety or fundamental rights ..."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Human oversight shall aim to prevent or minimise risks to health, safety or fundamental rights arising from the use or foreseeable misuse of high-risk AI systems."^^xsd:string .

:human_oversight_assignment_deployers_art26_2 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "human_oversight_assignment_deployers_art26_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: Deployers shall assign human oversight to natural persons who have the necessary competence, training and authority, as well as the necessary support"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_26 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_26_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Deployers shall assign human oversight to natural persons with necessary competence, training, authority, and support."^^xsd:string .

:human_oversight_automation_bias_awareness_art14_4b a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "human_oversight_automation_bias_awareness_art14_4b"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: To remain aware of the possible tendency of automatically relying or over-relying on the output..."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_4_b ;
    :hasSummary "Natural persons must be enabled to remain aware of possible automation bias, especially for systems providing information or recommendations for decisions."^^xsd:string .

:human_oversight_enabling_deployer_art14_4 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "human_oversight_enabling_deployer_art14_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: To properly understand relevant capacities and limitations ... and be able to duly monitor its operation, including detecting and addressing anomalies."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_4_a ;
    :hasSummary "High-risk AI systems must enable natural persons assigned human oversight to understand system capacities and limitations, monitor operation, detect anomalies, and address unexpected performance."^^xsd:string .

:human_oversight_intervention_art14_4e a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "human_oversight_intervention_art14_4e"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: To intervene in the operation ... or interrupt the system through a ‘stop’ button or similar procedure."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_4_e ;
    :hasSummary "Natural persons must be able to intervene in or interrupt the operation of the high-risk AI system via a stop button or similar procedure ensuring a safe halt."^^xsd:string .

:human_oversight_measures_commensurate_to_risk_art14_3 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "human_oversight_measures_commensurate_to_risk_art14_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: The oversight measures shall be commensurate with the risks, level of autonomy and context of use ... by provider before placed on market or deployer."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Oversight measures shall be commensurate with the risks, level of autonomy and context of use of the high-risk AI system, ensured through measures built by the provider or implemented by the deployer."^^xsd:string .

:human_oversight_obligation_art14_1 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "human_oversight_obligation_art14_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: High-risk AI systems shall be designed and developed ... that they can be effectively overseen by natural persons during the period in which they are in use."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_1 ;
    :hasSummary "High-risk AI systems must be designed and developed to be effectively overseen by natural persons during their use period, including appropriate human-machine interface tools."^^xsd:string .

:human_oversight_output_interpretation_art14_4c a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "human_oversight_output_interpretation_art14_4c"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: To correctly interpret the high-risk AI system’s output, taking into account interpretation tools available."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_4_c ;
    :hasSummary "Natural persons must be enabled to correctly interpret the high-risk AI system’s output considering available interpretation tools and methods."^^xsd:string .

:human_oversight_override_decision_power_art14_4d a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "human_oversight_override_decision_power_art14_4d"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: To decide ... not to use the high-risk AI system or to disregard, override or reverse the output."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_4_d ;
    :hasSummary "Natural persons overseeing the system must be enabled to decide not to use, or to disregard, override or reverse the AI system’s output in any situation."^^xsd:string .

:information_access_enforcement_power_art75_3 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "information_access_enforcement_power_art75_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: the AI Office shall supply to the applicant authority without delay, and in any event within 30 days, any information that the AI Office considers to be relevant"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_75 ;
    :hasDeadline "P30D"^^xsd:duration ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_75_3 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office shall enforce access to relevant information for market surveillance authorities investigating high-risk AI systems based on general-purpose AI models, providing this information within 30 days upon request."^^xsd:string .

:informed_consent_or_law_enforcement_exception_art60_4i a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "informed_consent_or_law_enforcement_exception_art60_4i"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM9"@en,
        "evidence: subjects...have given informed consent...or...testing in law enforcement shall not have negative effect and personal data shall be deleted after test"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60,
        :Article_61 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_4_i ;
    :hasSummary "Subjects must give informed consent according to Article 61; for law enforcement testing where consent would prevent testing, there may be no negative effect and personal data must be deleted after testing."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art12_1 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art12_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: High-risk AI systems shall technically allow for the automatic recording of events (logs) over the lifetime of the system."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_12 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_12_1 ;
    :hasSummary "High-risk AI systems shall technically allow for the automatic recording of events (logs) over the lifetime of the system to ensure traceability."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art12_2 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art12_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: Logging capabilities shall enable the recording of events relevant for identifying situations that may result in risk, post-market monitoring, and monitoring operation."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_12,
        :Article_26 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_12_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Logging capabilities shall enable the recording of events relevant for identifying risk situations, facilitating post-market monitoring, and monitoring operation as referred in Article 26(5)."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art19_1 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art19_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: Providers of high-risk AI systems shall keep the logs ... logs shall be kept for ... at least six months"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_19 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_19_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems must keep automatically generated logs under their control for at least six months unless otherwise required by applicable Union or national law."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art19_2 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art19_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: Providers that are financial institutions ... shall maintain the logs ... as part of the documentation"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_19 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_19_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers that are financial institutions must maintain automatically generated logs as part of the documentation required by Union financial services law."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art22_3_a a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art22_3_a"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: verify that the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47 and the technical documentation referred to in Article 11 have been drawn up and that an appropriate conformity assessment proced"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_22 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_22_3_a ;
    :hasSummary "The authorised representative shall verify that the EU declaration of conformity and technical documentation have been drawn up and that an appropriate conformity assessment procedure has been carried out by the provider."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art22_3_b a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art22_3_b"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: keep at the disposal of the competent authorities and national authorities ... the contact details of the provider... a copy of the EU declaration of conformity ... technical documentation and, if app"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_22 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_22_3_b ;
    :hasSummary "The authorised representative shall keep, for 10 years after the high-risk AI system has been placed on the market, the contact details of the provider, a copy of the EU declaration of conformity, technical documentation, and if applicable, the certificate issued by the notified body, at the disposal of authorities."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art22_3_c a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art22_3_c"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: provide a competent authority, upon a reasoned request, with all the information and documentation ... including access to the logs automatically generated by the high-risk AI system"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_22 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_22_3_c ;
    :hasSummary "The authorised representative shall provide authorities, upon reasoned request, all information and documentation necessary to demonstrate conformity of a high-risk AI system, including access to logs generated by the system under the provider's control."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art22_3_d a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art22_3_d"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: cooperate with competent authorities, upon a reasoned request, in any action ... to reduce and mitigate the risks posed by the high-risk AI system"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_22 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_22_3_d ;
    :hasSummary "The authorised representative shall cooperate with competent authorities upon reasoned request in actions to reduce and mitigate risks posed by the high-risk AI system."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art22_3_e a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art22_3_e"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: where applicable, comply with the registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1) ... ensure that the information ... is correct"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_22 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_22_3_e ;
    :hasSummary "The authorised representative shall comply with registration obligations or ensure correctness of registration information if executed by the provider."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art22_4 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art22_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: The authorised representative shall terminate the mandate if it considers ... the provider to be acting contrary to its obligations ... and ... inform the relevant market surveillance authority ... ab"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_22 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_22_4 ;
    :hasSummary "The authorised representative shall terminate the mandate if it considers the provider acts contrary to obligations under this Regulation and shall immediately inform relevant authorities about termination and reasons."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art34_3 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art34_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "evidence: Notified bodies shall make available and submit upon request all relevant documentation, including the providers’ documentation, to the notifying authority referred to in Article 28"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_34 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_34_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Notified bodies must make available and submit all relevant documentation, including providers' documentation, to the notifying authority for assessment, designation, notification and monitoring activities."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art43_1_a a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art43_1_a"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: opt for one of the following conformity assessment procedures based on: (a) the internal control referred to in Annex VI"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_43_1_a ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems listed in point 1 of Annex III may choose the internal control procedure in Annex VI as a conformity assessment option when harmonised standards or common specifications are applied."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art43_2 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art43_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: providers shall follow the conformity assessment procedure based on internal control as referred to in Annex VI"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_43_2 ;
    :hasSummary "For high-risk AI systems referred to in points 2 to 8 of Annex III, providers must use the internal control conformity assessment procedure from Annex VI, without a notified body involvement."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_1 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: A risk management system shall be established, implemented, documented and maintained in relation to high-risk AI systems."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_1 ;
    :hasSummary "A risk management system must be established, implemented, documented, and maintained for high-risk AI systems."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_10 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_10"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the aspects provided in paragraphs 1 to 9 may be part of, or combined with, the risk management procedures established pursuant to that law"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_10 ;
    :hasSummary "The risk management system may be integrated with other internal risk management processes under Union law for providers of high-risk AI systems."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_2_a a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_2_a"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the identification and analysis of the known and the reasonably foreseeable risks that the high-risk AI system can pose to health, safety or fundamental rights when the high-risk AI system is used in "@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_2_a ;
    :hasSummary "The risk management system must identify and analyze known and reasonably foreseeable risks to health, safety, or fundamental rights posed by the high-risk AI system when used as intended."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_2_b a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_2_b"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the estimation and evaluation of the risks that may emerge when the high-risk AI system is used in accordance with its intended purpose, and under conditions of reasonably foreseeable misuse"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_2_b ;
    :hasSummary "The system shall estimate and evaluate risks that may emerge under intended use and reasonably foreseeable misuse."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_2_c a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_2_c"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the evaluation of other risks possibly arising, based on the analysis of data gathered from the post-market monitoring system referred to in Article 72"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_2_c ;
    :hasSummary "Evaluation of other risks based on data from the post-market monitoring system is required."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_2_d a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_2_d"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the adoption of appropriate and targeted risk management measures designed to address the risks identified pursuant to point (a)"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_2_d ;
    :hasSummary "Appropriate and targeted risk management measures must be adopted to address identified risks."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_3 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: The risks referred to in this Article shall concern only those which may be reasonably mitigated or eliminated through the development or design of the high-risk AI system, or the provision of adequat"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Risks considered in the risk management system shall be those reasonably mitigable or eliminable through development, design, or technical information."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_4 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: The risk management measures referred to in paragraph 2, point (d), shall give due consideration to the effects and possible interaction resulting from the combined application of the requirements set"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_4 ;
    :hasSummary "Risk management measures shall consider the combined effects and interactions of requirements to minimize risks effectively and balance implementation."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_5 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: risk management measures...such that the relevant residual risk associated with each hazard...is judged to be acceptable"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_5 ;
    :hasSummary "Risk management measures must ensure residual risks are acceptable by eliminating or reducing risks via design, implementing mitigation measures, and providing information and training to deployers."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_6 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_6"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: High-risk AI systems shall be tested for the purpose of identifying the most appropriate and targeted risk management measures"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_6 ;
    :hasSummary "High-risk AI systems shall be tested to identify the most appropriate risk management measures and ensure compliance with requirements."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_7 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_7"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: Testing procedures may include testing in real-world conditions in accordance with Article 60"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60,
        :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_7 ;
    :hasSummary "Testing procedures may include testing in real-world conditions as per Article 60."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_8 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_8"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: The testing of high-risk AI systems shall be performed...prior to their being placed on the market or put into service"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_8 ;
    :hasSummary "Testing shall be conducted throughout development and before market placement against prior defined metrics and thresholds appropriate to the intended purpose."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_art9_9 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_art9_9"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: providers shall give consideration to whether...likely to have an adverse impact on persons under the age of 18 and, as appropriate, other vulnerable groups"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_9_9 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must consider possible adverse impacts on persons under 18 and vulnerable groups when implementing the risk management system."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_cooperation_art23_7 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_cooperation_art23_7"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: Importers shall cooperate with the relevant competent authorities in any action"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_23 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_23_7 ;
    :hasSummary "Importers shall cooperate with competent authorities in actions related to a high-risk AI system they placed on the market, particularly to reduce and mitigate risks posed by it."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_information_provision_art23_6 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_information_provision_art23_6"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: shall provide ... authorities ... with all necessary information and documentation ... to demonstrate the conformity"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_23 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_23_6 ;
    :hasSummary "Importers shall provide competent authorities, upon reasoned request, all necessary information and documentation to demonstrate conformity, including technical documentation in an understandable language."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_recordkeeping_art23_5 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_recordkeeping_art23_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: Importers shall keep, for a period of 10 years ... a copy of the certificate ... instructions for use, and ... EU declaration of conformity"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_23 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_23_5 ;
    :hasSummary "Importers shall keep for 10 years copies of certificates issued by notified bodies, instructions for use, and EU declarations of conformity after placing the high-risk AI system on the market or putting it into service."^^xsd:string .

:internal_control_obligation_storage_art23_4 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "internal_control_obligation_storage_art23_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: Importers shall ensure ... storage or transport conditions ... do not jeopardise its compliance"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_23 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_23_4 ;
    :hasSummary "Importers must ensure that storage or transport conditions do not jeopardise the compliance of a high-risk AI system while under their responsibility."^^xsd:string .

:investigation_and_notification_obligation_art20_2 a :PostMarketMonitoringObligation ;
    rdfs:label "investigation_and_notification_obligation_art20_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: Where the high-risk AI system presents a risk... it shall immediately investigate the causes... and inform the market surveillance authorities... and, where applicable, the notified body..."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_20 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_20_2 ;
    :hasSummary "When a high-risk AI system presents a risk, the provider must immediately investigate causes and inform market surveillance authorities and notified bodies about the non-compliance and corrective actions taken."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art37_1 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art37_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The Commission shall, where necessary, investigate all cases where there are reasons to doubt the competence of a notified body"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_37 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_37_1 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission shall investigate cases where there are reasons to doubt the competence of a notified body or its continued fulfilment of its requirements and responsibilities."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art37_2 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art37_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The notifying authority shall provide the Commission, on request, with all relevant information relating to the notification or the maintenance of the competence"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_37 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_37_2 ;
    :hasSummary "The notifying authority must provide the Commission with all relevant information relating to the notification or competence maintenance of the notified body, upon request."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art37_3 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art37_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The Commission shall ensure that all sensitive information obtained in the course of its investigations... is treated confidentially"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_37 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_37_3 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission must ensure that sensitive information obtained in investigations under this Article is treated confidentially."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art77_3 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art77_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: the public authority...may make a reasoned request to the market surveillance authority, to organise testing of the high-risk AI system through technical means"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_77 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_77_3 ;
    :hasSummary "When documentation is insufficient to determine infringement of fundamental rights laws, the relevant authority may request the market surveillance authority to organise technical testing of high-risk AI systems."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art80_1 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art80_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: the market surveillance authority shall carry out an evaluation of the AI system concerned"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_80 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_80_1 ;
    :hasSummary "The market surveillance authority shall carry out an evaluation of an AI system classified by the provider as non-high-risk if it has sufficient reason to consider it is high-risk."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art91 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art91"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The Commission may request the provider ... to provide the documentation ... or any additional information ... necessary for assessing compliance"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_91 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_91_1 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission may request documentation or additional information from the provider of a general-purpose AI model to assess compliance with the Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art92_2 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art92_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The Commission may decide to appoint independent experts to carry out evaluations on its behalf"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_92 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_92_2 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission may appoint independent experts, including from the scientific panel, to carry out evaluations of general-purpose AI models on its behalf."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art92_3 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art92_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The Commission may request access...through APIs or further appropriate technical means and tools, including source code"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_92 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_92_3 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission may request access to the general-purpose AI model through APIs or other technical means, including source code, to conduct evaluations."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art92_4 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art92_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The request for access shall state the legal basis, the purpose and reasons...and the fines provided for Article 101"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_92 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_92_4 ;
    :hasSummary "Requests for access must state the legal basis, purpose, reasons, timeline, and include fines for failure to provide access."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art92_5 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art92_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Providers or their representative shall supply the information requested"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_92 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_92_5 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers or their authorised representatives must supply requested information or access for evaluations."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_art92_7 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_art92_7"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: AI Office may initiate a structured dialogue with the provider to gather more information on internal testing and safeguards"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_92 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_92_7 ;
    :hasSummary "Prior to access requests, the AI Office may initiate a structured dialogue with providers to gather more information on internal testing, safeguards, and risk mitigation measures."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_information_supply_responsibility_art91_5 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_information_supply_responsibility_art91_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The provider ... or its representative shall supply the information requested ... The clients shall nevertheless remain fully responsible if the information supplied is incomplete, incorrect or mislea"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_91 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_91_5 ;
    :hasSummary "The provider or their authorized representative must supply the requested information; clients remain responsible for information completeness and correctness."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_request_details_art91_4 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_request_details_art91_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The request for information shall state the legal basis and the purpose of the request, specify what information is required, set a period ... and indicate the fines ..."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_101,
        :Article_91 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_91_4 ;
    :hasSummary "Requests for information must specify the legal basis, purpose, required information, deadline, and indicate fines for incorrect, incomplete, or misleading information as per Article 101."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_scientific_panel_request_art91_3 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_scientific_panel_request_art91_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Upon a duly substantiated request from the scientific panel, the Commission may issue a request for information to a provider of a general-purpose AI model"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_68,
        :Article_91 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_91_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Upon a substantiated request from the scientific panel, the Commission may request information from a general-purpose AI model provider necessary for fulfilling the scientific panel's tasks under Article 68(2)."^^xsd:string .

:investigative_power_structured_dialogue_art91_2 a :InvestigativePower ;
    rdfs:label "investigative_power_structured_dialogue_art91_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Before sending the request for information, the AI Office may initiate a structured dialogue with the provider"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_91 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_91_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Before sending a request for information, the AI Office may initiate a structured dialogue with the provider of the general-purpose AI model."^^xsd:string .

:log_keeping_deployers_high_risk_ai_art26_6 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "log_keeping_deployers_high_risk_ai_art26_6"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: Deployers of high-risk AI systems shall keep the logs ... for a period appropriate to the intended purpose ... at least six months"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_26 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_26_6 ;
    :hasSummary "Deployers shall keep automatically generated logs for a period appropriate to the intended purpose, at least six months, unless otherwise provided by law."^^xsd:string .

:market_surveillance_authority_powers_for_testing_art60_6 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "market_surveillance_authority_powers_for_testing_art60_6"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Member States shall confer...powers...to ensure safe development of testing in real world conditions"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_6 ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities have powers to require information, conduct unannounced inspections and checks to ensure safe development of testing in real world conditions."^^xsd:string .

:monitor_operation_and_incident_reporting_deployers_art26_5 a :DeployerIncidentReport ;
    rdfs:label "monitor_operation_and_incident_reporting_deployers_art26_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM10"@en,
        "evidence: Deployers shall monitor the operation ... inform providers ... and shall suspend the use of that system ... immediately inform first the provider ... and the relevant market surveillance authorities"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_26 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_26_5 ;
    :hasReportingTarget :MarketSurveillanceAuthority ;
    :hasSummary "Deployers shall monitor operation, inform providers of risks or incidents without delay, suspend use if risks are found, and notify appropriate authorities."^^xsd:string .

:necessity_condition_realtime_remote_biometric_identification_law_enforcement_5_1_h_art5 a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "necessity_condition_realtime_remote_biometric_identification_law_enforcement_5_1_h_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "evidence: Use of ‘real-time’ remote biometric identification systems in publicly accessible spaces for law enforcement unless strictly necessary for specified objectives"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_1_h ;
    :hasSummary "Use of real-time remote biometric identification in public spaces for law enforcement is prohibited unless strictly necessary for specific objectives like searching for missing persons, preventing threats, or criminal investigations with specific conditions."^^xsd:string .

:notification_of_suspension_termination_and_outcomes_art60_8 a :ProceduralCondition ;
    rdfs:label "notification_of_suspension_termination_and_outcomes_art60_8"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "evidence: Providers...shall notify...authority of suspension or termination and final outcomes"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_8 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must notify national market surveillance authority of any suspension, termination and the final outcomes of testing in real world conditions."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_annual_reporting_realtime_remote_biometric_5_6_art5 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_annual_reporting_realtime_remote_biometric_5_6_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Authorities...shall submit to the Commission annual reports on such use...including number of decisions taken"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_6 ;
    :hasSummary "National authorities notified of real-time remote biometric identification use must submit annual reports to the Commission including number and results of authorisation decisions."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art21_1 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art21_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Providers of high-risk AI systems shall, upon a reasoned request by a competent authority, provide that authority all the information and documentation necessary to demonstrate the conformity..."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_21 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_21_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems must provide competent authorities, upon reasoned request, all necessary information and documentation to demonstrate system conformity."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art21_2 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art21_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Upon a reasoned request by a competent authority, providers shall also give the requesting competent authority access to the automatically generated logs... to the extent such logs are under their con"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_21 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_21_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must grant competent authorities access to automatically generated logs of the high-risk AI system upon reasoned request, to the extent such logs are under their control."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art70_1 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art70_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: national competent authorities shall exercise their powers independently, impartially and without bias so as to safeguard the objectivity of their activities and tasks"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_70 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_70_1 ;
    :hasSummary "National competent authorities shall exercise their powers independently, impartially and without bias to ensure application and implementation of this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art70_3 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art70_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: national competent authorities are provided with adequate technical, financial and human resources, and with infrastructure to fulfil their tasks effectively"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_70 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_70_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Member States shall ensure national competent authorities have adequate technical, financial and human resources, with relevant AI expertise, to fulfill their tasks effectively under this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art70_4 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art70_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: National competent authorities shall take appropriate measures to ensure an adequate level of cybersecurity"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_70 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_70_4 ;
    :hasSummary "National competent authorities shall take appropriate measures to ensure an adequate level of cybersecurity."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art75_1 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art75_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: the AI Office shall have powers to monitor and supervise compliance of that AI system with obligations"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_75 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_75_1 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office has powers to monitor and supervise compliance of general-purpose AI systems developed by the same provider as the base model."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art75_1_ensuring_market_surveillance_authority_powers a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art75_1_ensuring_market_surveillance_authority_powers"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: AI Office shall have all the powers of a market surveillance authority provided for in this Section and Regulation (EU) 2019/1020"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_75 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_75_1 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office shall have all powers of a market surveillance authority for monitoring and supervising general-purpose AI systems."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art76_1 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art76_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Market surveillance authorities shall have competences and powers to ensure that testing in real world conditions is in accordance with this Regulation."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_76 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_76_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities have competences and powers to ensure that testing in real world conditions complies with this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art76_2 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art76_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: market surveillance authorities shall verify the compliance with Article 60 as part of their supervisory role for the AI regulatory sandbox."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60,
        :Article_76 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_76_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities verify compliance with Article 60 as part of their supervisory role for AI regulatory sandboxes when testing in real world conditions is conducted under such sandboxes."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art76_3_a a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art76_3_a"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: it may take... to suspend or terminate the testing in real world conditions;"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_76 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_76_3_a ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities may suspend or terminate testing in real world conditions if serious incidents occur or conditions in Articles 60 and 61 are not met."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art76_3_b a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art76_3_b"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: to require the provider or prospective provider and the deployer or prospective deployer to modify any aspect of the testing in real world conditions."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_76 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_76_3_b ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities may require providers, prospective providers, deployers, or prospective deployers to modify aspects of real world testing if conditions are not met or serious incidents are reported."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art76_4 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art76_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: the decision or the objection shall indicate the grounds therefor and how the provider or prospective provider can challenge the decision or objection."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_76 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_76_4 ;
    :hasSummary "Decisions or objections by market surveillance authorities to suspend, terminate, or object to real world testing must state grounds and how affected parties can challenge them."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art76_5 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art76_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: it shall communicate the grounds therefor to the market surveillance authorities of other Member States in which the AI system has been tested."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_76 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_76_5 ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities must communicate grounds for decisions affecting real world testing to authorities in other Member States where testing occurred."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art77_1 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art77_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: National public authorities...shall have the power to request and access any documentation...when access to that documentation is necessary for effectively fulfilling their mandates"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_77 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_77_1 ;
    :hasSummary "National public authorities supervising fundamental rights related to high-risk AI systems have the power to request and access documentation necessary to fulfill their mandates."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art79_2 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art79_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: it shall carry out an evaluation of the AI system concerned in respect of its compliance with all the requirements and obligations laid down in this Regulation"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_79 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_79_2 ;
    :hasSummary "The market surveillance authority shall evaluate AI systems presenting a risk for compliance with all requirements and obligations of this Regulation."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art79_2_cooperation a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art79_2_cooperation"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Where risks to fundamental rights are identified, the market surveillance authority shall also inform and fully cooperate with the relevant national public authorities"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_79 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_79_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities shall inform and cooperate with relevant national public authorities when risks to fundamental rights are identified."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art79_2_corrective_action_requirements a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art79_2_corrective_action_requirements"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: shall...require the relevant operator to take all appropriate corrective actions to bring the AI system into compliance, to withdraw the AI system from the market, or to recall it within a period... w"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_79 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_79_2 ;
    :hasSummary "The market surveillance authority shall require operators to take corrective actions including compliance measures, withdrawal or recall within 15 working days or as provided in Union legislation."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art79_3 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art79_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: it shall inform the Commission and the other Member States without undue delay of the results of the evaluation and of the actions"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_79 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_79_3 ;
    :hasSummary "If non-compliance is not restricted to one Member State, the market surveillance authority shall inform the Commission and other Member States without undue delay."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art79_5 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art79_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: the market surveillance authority shall take all appropriate provisional measures... and shall without undue delay notify the Commission and the other Member States"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_79 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_79_5 ;
    :hasSummary "The market surveillance authority shall take provisional measures such as prohibition, restriction, withdrawal or recall if the operator fails to take corrective action timely and notify Commission and other Member States."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art79_6_non_compliance_reasons a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art79_6_non_compliance_reasons"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: authorities shall indicate whether the non-compliance is due to... (a)...Article 5; (b)...Chapter III, Section 2; (c)...Articles 40 and 41; (d) non-compliance with Article 50"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_50,
        :Article_79 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_79_6 ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities shall indicate if non-compliance relates to (a) prohibited AI practices, (b) failures of high-risk AI systems to meet requirements, (c) shortcomings in harmonised standards, or (d) non-compliance with Article 50."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art79_6_notification_contents a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art79_6_notification_contents"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The notification... shall include all available details, in particular the information necessary for the identification of the non-compliant AI system"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_79 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_79_6 ;
    :hasSummary "Notifications of provisional measures must include details identifying the AI system, origin, supply chain, nature of non-compliance and risk, and arguments of the operator."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art79_7 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art79_7"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: market surveillance authorities... shall, without undue delay, inform the Commission and the other Member States of any measures adopted and of any additional information"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_79 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_79_7 ;
    :hasSummary "Other market surveillance authorities shall report adopted measures, additional information, or objections regarding non-compliance measures taken by another Member State."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art79_8_deemed_justification a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art79_8_deemed_justification"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: within three months of receipt... no objection... the measure shall be deemed justified... reduced to 30 days in the event of non-compliance with... Article 5"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5,
        :Article_79 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_79_8 ;
    :hasSummary "If within three months no objections are raised to provisional measures, those measures are deemed justified; this period shortens to 30 days if non-compliance involves prohibited AI practices under Article 5."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art79_9_restrictive_measures a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art79_9_restrictive_measures"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: shall ensure that appropriate restrictive measures are taken... such as withdrawal of the product or the AI system from their market, without undue delay"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_79 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_79_9 ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities shall ensure restrictive measures such as withdrawal are taken without undue delay for non-compliant AI systems or products."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art80_8 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art80_8"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: market surveillance authorities may perform appropriate checks, taking into account information stored in the EU database"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_80 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_80_8 ;
    :hasSummary "Market surveillance authorities may perform appropriate checks in exercising their power to monitor the application of this Article, including considering information stored in the EU database."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art82_1 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art82_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: the market surveillance authority ... shall require the relevant operator to take all appropriate measures ... no longer presents that risk"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_82 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_82_1 ;
    :hasSummary "The market surveillance authority has the power to require operators to take measures if a compliant high-risk AI system presents a risk to health, safety, fundamental rights, or public interest."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art82_3 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art82_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The Member States shall immediately inform the Commission and the other Member States of a finding ... including all available details"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_82 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_82_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Member States must immediately inform the Commission and other Member States about findings that a compliant high-risk AI system presents a risk including system identification, origin, risk, and measures taken."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art82_4 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art82_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The Commission shall ... enter into consultation ... and shall evaluate the national measures taken ... decide whether the measure is justified"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_82 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_82_4 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission shall consult Member States and operators to evaluate national measures taken and decide whether the measures are justified or if other measures are needed."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art82_5 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art82_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The Commission shall immediately communicate its decision to the Member States concerned and to the relevant operators."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_82 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_82_5 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission shall immediately communicate its decision on the evaluation of national measures to Member States and relevant operators and inform other Member States."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art89_1 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art89_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: the AI Office may take the necessary actions to monitor the effective implementation and compliance with this Regulation by providers of general-purpose AI models"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_89 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_89_1 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office may take necessary actions to monitor the effective implementation and compliance with this Regulation by providers of general-purpose AI models, including adherence to approved codes of practice."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_art92_1 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_art92_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: The AI Office...may conduct evaluations...to assess compliance...or to investigate systemic risks"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_92 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_92_1 ;
    :hasSummary "The AI Office may conduct evaluations of the general-purpose AI model to assess provider compliance or investigate systemic risks when prior information is insufficient, especially after consulting the Board or receiving qualified alerts."^^xsd:string .

:oversight_power_commission_annual_reports_realtime_remote_biometric_5_7_art5 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "oversight_power_commission_annual_reports_realtime_remote_biometric_5_7_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Commission shall publish annual reports...based on aggregated data...excluding sensitive operational data"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_7 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission shall publish annual aggregated reports on real-time remote biometric identification use for law enforcement based on Member State data, excluding sensitive operational data."^^xsd:string .

:post_market_monitoring_obligation_art72_1 a :PostMarketMonitoringObligation ;
    rdfs:label "post_market_monitoring_obligation_art72_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: Providers shall establish and document a post-market monitoring system in a manner that is proportionate to the nature of the AI technologies and the risks of the high-risk AI system."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_72 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_72_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must establish and document a post-market monitoring system proportionate to the nature and risks of the high-risk AI system."^^xsd:string .

:post_market_monitoring_obligation_art72_2 a :PostMarketMonitoringObligation ;
    rdfs:label "post_market_monitoring_obligation_art72_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: post-market monitoring system shall actively and systematically collect, document and analyse relevant data ... to evaluate the continuous compliance of AI systems"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_72 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_72_2 ;
    :hasSummary "The post-market monitoring system must actively collect, document, and analyse data on performance over the AI system's lifetime to evaluate continuous compliance."^^xsd:string .

:post_market_monitoring_obligation_art72_3 a :PostMarketMonitoringObligation ;
    rdfs:label "post_market_monitoring_obligation_art72_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: post-market monitoring system shall be based on a post-market monitoring plan ... part of the technical documentation"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_72 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_72_3 ;
    :hasSummary "The post-market monitoring system must be based on a documented post-market monitoring plan included in the technical documentation."^^xsd:string .

:post_market_monitoring_obligation_art72_4 a :PostMarketMonitoringObligation ;
    rdfs:label "post_market_monitoring_obligation_art72_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: providers shall have a choice of integrating ... the necessary elements ... into systems and plans already existing under that legislation, provided that it achieves an equivalent level of protection."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_72 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_72_4 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers may integrate the required post-market monitoring elements into existing systems under Union harmonisation legislation where already established, ensuring an equivalent level of protection."^^xsd:string .

:post_market_monitoring_obligation_art82_2 a :PostMarketMonitoringObligation ;
    rdfs:label "post_market_monitoring_obligation_art82_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: The provider or other relevant operator shall ensure that corrective action is taken ... within the timeline prescribed"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_82 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_82_2 ;
    :hasSummary "The provider or relevant operator must ensure corrective action is taken on all concerned AI systems within the prescribed timeline."^^xsd:string .

:prior_authorisation_condition_realtime_remote_biometric_5_3_art5 a :ProceduralCondition ;
    rdfs:label "prior_authorisation_condition_realtime_remote_biometric_5_3_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "evidence: Each use...shall be subject to a prior authorisation granted by a judicial authority or an independent administrative authority"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Use of real-time remote biometric identification for law enforcement requires prior judicial or independent administrative authority authorisation except in urgent cases with conditions."^^xsd:string .

:product_compliance_obligation_harmonisation_legislation_art8_2 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "product_compliance_obligation_harmonisation_legislation_art8_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: providers shall be responsible for ensuring that their product is fully compliant with all applicable requirements under applicable Union harmonisation legislation"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_8 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_8_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of products containing AI systems subject to this Regulation and Union harmonisation legislation are responsible for ensuring full compliance with all applicable requirements under applicable Union harmonisation legislation."^^xsd:string .

:product_manufacturer_as_provider_art25_3 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "product_manufacturer_as_provider_art25_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: product manufacturer shall be considered to be the provider...when the high-risk AI system is placed on the market or put into service under the product manufacturer's name or trademark"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16,
        :Article_25 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_25_3 ;
    :hasSummary "For high-risk AI safety components of products covered by Union harmonisation legislation, the product manufacturer is considered the provider and is subject to obligations under Article 16 when the AI system is placed on the market or put into service under their name or trademark."^^xsd:string .

:prohibited_ai_practice_biometric_categorisation_sensitive_data_5_1_g_art5 a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "prohibited_ai_practice_biometric_categorisation_sensitive_data_5_1_g_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "evidence: Use of biometric categorisation systems to deduce race, political opinions, trade union membership, religious beliefs, sex life or sexual orientation"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_1_g ;
    :hasSummary "AI biometric categorisation systems inferring sensitive personal characteristics are prohibited except for lawful labelling/filtering or law enforcement categorisation."^^xsd:string .

:prohibited_ai_practice_criminal_offense_risk_assessment_5_1_d_art5 a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "prohibited_ai_practice_criminal_offense_risk_assessment_5_1_d_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "evidence: AI system for making risk assessments...based solely on the profiling of a natural person or on assessing their personality traits"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_1_d ;
    :hasSummary "AI systems assessing criminal offense risk based solely on profiling or personality traits are prohibited, except supporting human assessment based on objective facts."^^xsd:string .

:prohibited_ai_practice_emotion_inference_workplace_education_5_1_f_art5 a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "prohibited_ai_practice_emotion_inference_workplace_education_5_1_f_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "evidence: AI systems to infer emotions...in workplace and education institutions, except...for medical or safety reasons"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_1_f ;
    :hasSummary "AI systems inferring emotions in workplace or education are prohibited except for medical or safety reasons."^^xsd:string .

:prohibited_ai_practice_exploitation_vulnerabilities_5_1_b_art5 a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "prohibited_ai_practice_exploitation_vulnerabilities_5_1_b_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "evidence: AI system that exploits any of the vulnerabilities...causing...significant harm"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_1_b ;
    :hasSummary "AI systems exploiting vulnerabilities due to age, disability or social/economic situation to distort behavior causing significant harm are prohibited."^^xsd:string .

:prohibited_ai_practice_social_scoring_5_1_c_art5 a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "prohibited_ai_practice_social_scoring_5_1_c_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "evidence: AI systems for evaluation or classification based on social behaviour...leading to detrimental or unfavourable treatment"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_1_c ;
    :hasSummary "AI systems using social scoring for detrimental or unjustified treatment of persons or groups in unrelated social contexts are prohibited."^^xsd:string .

:prohibited_ai_practice_subliminal_manipulative_5_1_a_art5 a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "prohibited_ai_practice_subliminal_manipulative_5_1_a_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "evidence: AI system that deploys subliminal techniques beyond a person’s consciousness or purposefully manipulative...causing...significant harm"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_1_a ;
    :hasSummary "AI systems deploying subliminal or manipulative techniques that materially distort behavior causing significant harm are prohibited."^^xsd:string .

:prohibited_ai_practice_untargeted_facial_recognition_databases_5_1_e_art5 a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "prohibited_ai_practice_untargeted_facial_recognition_databases_5_1_e_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "evidence: AI systems that create or expand facial recognition databases through the untargeted scraping of facial images"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_1_e ;
    :hasSummary "AI systems that create or expand facial recognition databases through untargeted scraping of internet or CCTV images are prohibited."^^xsd:string .

:proportionality_condition_law_enforcement_realtime_remote_biometric_use_5_2_art5 a :ProportionalityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "proportionality_condition_law_enforcement_realtime_remote_biometric_use_5_2_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM9"@en,
        "evidence: Use shall take into account...seriousness, probability and scale of the harm...and consequences for rights and freedoms"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Use of real-time remote biometric identification must consider seriousness, probability, and scale of harm and consequences for rights and freedoms, with safeguards and limitations."^^xsd:string .

:proportionality_condition_realtime_remote_biometric_5_3_art5 a :ProportionalityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "proportionality_condition_realtime_remote_biometric_5_3_art5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ9"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM9"@en,
        "evidence: Authority shall grant authorisation only where...use is necessary for, and proportionate to, achieving one of the objectives"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_5 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_5_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Judicial or independent authority must ensure use of real-time remote biometric identification is necessary and proportionate to the law enforcement objective, limited in scope and time."^^xsd:string .

:protection_of_vulnerable_groups_art60_4g a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "protection_of_vulnerable_groups_art60_4g"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM9"@en,
        "evidence: subjects...who are persons belonging to vulnerable groups due to their age or disability, are appropriately protected"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_4_g ;
    :hasSummary "Subjects belonging to vulnerable groups due to age or disability must be appropriately protected during testing in real world conditions."^^xsd:string .

:provider_establishment_or_representative_art60_4d a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "provider_establishment_or_representative_art60_4d"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM9"@en,
        "evidence: the provider...conducting the testing...is established in the Union or has appointed a legal representative who is established in the Union"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_4_d ;
    :hasSummary "Providers conducting testing in real world conditions must be established in the Union or have appointed a legal representative established in the Union."^^xsd:string .

:provider_human_oversight_measures_art14_3a a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_human_oversight_measures_art14_3a"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: Measures identified and built, when technically feasible, into the high-risk AI system by the provider before it is placed on the market or put into service."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_14 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_14_3_a ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must identify and build technically feasible human oversight measures into the high-risk AI system before market placement or service."^^xsd:string .

:provider_incident_report_art73_1 a :ProviderIncidentReport ;
    rdfs:label "provider_incident_report_art73_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM10"@en,
        "evidence: Providers of high-risk AI systems placed on the Union market shall report any serious incident to the market surveillance authorities of the Member States where that incident occurred."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_73 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_73_1 ;
    :hasReportingTarget :MarketSurveillanceAuthority ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems shall report any serious incident to market surveillance authorities in Member States where the incident occurred."^^xsd:string .

:provider_incident_report_art73_2 a :ProviderIncidentReport ;
    rdfs:label "provider_incident_report_art73_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM10"@en,
        "evidence: The report referred to in paragraph 1 shall be made immediately... and, in any event, not later than 15 days after the provider ... becomes aware of the serious incident."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_73 ;
    :hasDeadline "P15D"^^xsd:duration ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_73_2 ;
    :hasReportingTarget :MarketSurveillanceAuthority ;
    :hasSummary "Serious incident reports must be made immediately after establishing or reasonably suspecting a causal link, and no later than 15 days after awareness, considering severity."^^xsd:string .

:provider_incident_report_art73_3 a :ProviderIncidentReport ;
    rdfs:label "provider_incident_report_art73_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM10"@en,
        "evidence: ...the report ... shall be provided immediately, and not later than two days after the provider... becomes aware of that incident."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_3,
        :Article_73 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_73_3 ;
    :hasReportingTarget :MarketSurveillanceAuthority ;
    :hasSummary "For widespread infringements or serious incidents as defined in Article 3(49)(b), reports must be submitted immediately and no later than two days after awareness."^^xsd:string .

:provider_incident_report_art73_4 a :ProviderIncidentReport ;
    rdfs:label "provider_incident_report_art73_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM10"@en,
        "evidence: In the event of the death of a person, the report shall be provided immediately ... but not later than 10 days after the date ... becomes aware."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_73 ;
    :hasDeadline "P10D"^^xsd:duration ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_73_4 ;
    :hasReportingTarget :MarketSurveillanceAuthority ;
    :hasSummary "In case of death, the report is required immediately after establishing or suspecting a causal link, and no later than 10 days after awareness."^^xsd:string .

:provider_incident_report_art73_5 a :ProviderIncidentReport ;
    rdfs:label "provider_incident_report_art73_5"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM10"@en,
        "evidence: ...may submit an initial report that is incomplete, followed by a complete report."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_73 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_73_5 ;
    :hasReportingTarget :MarketSurveillanceAuthority ;
    :hasSummary "Providers or deployers may submit an initial incomplete report to ensure timely reporting, followed by a complete report."^^xsd:string .

:provider_incident_report_art73_6 a :ProviderIncidentReport ;
    rdfs:label "provider_incident_report_art73_6"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM10"@en,
        "evidence: Following the reporting of a serious incident...the provider shall ... perform the necessary investigations ... shall cooperate with the competent authorities ... and shall not perform any investigati"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_73 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_73_6 ;
    :hasReportingTarget :MarketSurveillanceAuthority ;
    :hasSummary "After reporting a serious incident, providers must promptly investigate the incident and AI system, including risk assessment and corrective actions, cooperating with authorities, and inform before altering the AI system."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art111_2 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art111_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: Providers and deployers of high-risk AI systems intended to be used by public authorities shall take the necessary steps to comply with the requirements and obligations ... by 2 August 2030."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_111 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_111_2 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems intended for public authorities must comply with the Regulation requirements and obligations by 2 August 2030."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art111_3 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art111_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "evidence: Providers of general-purpose AI models that have been placed on the market before 2 August 2025 shall take the necessary steps in order to comply with the obligations laid down in this Regulation by 2"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_111 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_111_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of general-purpose AI models placed on the market before 2 August 2025 must comply with Regulation obligations by 2 August 2027."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_a a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_a"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: ensure that their high-risk AI systems are compliant with the requirements set out in Section 2"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems shall ensure their systems comply with the requirements set out in Section 2."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_c a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_c"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: have a quality management system in place which complies with Article 17"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16,
        :Article_17 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers shall have a quality management system in place that complies with Article 17."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_d a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_d"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: keep the documentation referred to in Article 18"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16,
        :Article_18 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must keep the documentation referred to in Article 18."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_e a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_e"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: keep the logs automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems as referred to in Article 19"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16,
        :Article_19 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must keep logs automatically generated by their high-risk AI systems when under their control, as referred to in Article 19."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_f a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_f"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: ensure that the high-risk AI system undergoes the relevant conformity assessment procedure as referred to in Article 43"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16,
        :Article_43 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must ensure the high-risk AI system undergoes the relevant conformity assessment procedure in Article 43 before being placed on the market or put into service."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_g a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_g"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: draw up an EU declaration of conformity in accordance with Article 47"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16,
        :Article_47 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers shall draw up an EU declaration of conformity in accordance with Article 47."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_h a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_h"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM3"@en,
        "evidence: affix the CE marking to the high-risk AI system or ... packaging or its accompanying documentation"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16,
        :Article_48 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers shall affix the CE marking to the high-risk AI system or its packaging or accompanying documentation to indicate conformity with this Regulation per Article 48."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_i a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_i"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: comply with the registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1)"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16,
        :Article_49 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers shall comply with the registration obligations referred to in Article 49(1)."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_j a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_j"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: take the necessary corrective actions and provide information as required in Article 20"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16,
        :Article_20 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must take necessary corrective actions and provide information as required in Article 20."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_k a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_k"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: upon a reasoned request of a national competent authority, demonstrate the conformity"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must, upon a reasoned request of a national competent authority, demonstrate the conformity of the high-risk AI system with the requirements set out in Section 2."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_art16_l a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_art16_l"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "evidence: ensure that the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements in accordance with Directives (EU) 2016/2102 and (EU) 2019/882"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers shall ensure the high-risk AI system complies with accessibility requirements according to Directives (EU) 2016/2102 and (EU) 2019/882."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_as_third_party_art25_1 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_as_third_party_art25_1"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: Any distributor, importer, deployer or other third-party shall be considered to be a provider...subject to the obligations of the provider under Article 16"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_16,
        :Article_25 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_25_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Distributors, importers, deployers or other third parties are considered providers of high-risk AI systems if they put their name or trademark on a high-risk AI system, make substantial modifications, or modify its intended purpose, thus subject to provider obligations under Article 16."^^xsd:string .

:provider_obligation_loss_by_initial_provider_art25_2 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "provider_obligation_loss_by_initial_provider_art25_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: initial provider shall no longer be considered to be a provider...shall closely cooperate with new providers and shall make available necessary information and provide...technical access"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_25 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_25_2 ;
    :hasSummary "When circumstances in paragraph 1 occur, the initial provider is no longer considered a provider for that specific AI system but shall cooperate and provide necessary information and technical access to the new provider."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_a a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_a"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: a strategy for regulatory compliance, including compliance with conformity assessment procedures and procedures for the management of modifications to the high-risk AI system"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_a ;
    :hasSummary "The quality management system must include a strategy for regulatory compliance, including conformity assessment procedures and modification management for the high-risk AI system."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_b a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_b"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: techniques, procedures and systematic actions to be used for the design, design control and design verification of the high-risk AI system"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_b ;
    :hasSummary "The quality management system must include techniques, procedures and systematic actions for design, design control, and design verification of the high-risk AI system."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_c a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_c"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: techniques, procedures and systematic actions to be used for the development, quality control and quality assurance of the high-risk AI system"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_c ;
    :hasSummary "The quality management system must include techniques, procedures and systematic actions for development, quality control, and quality assurance of the high-risk AI system."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_d a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_d"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: examination, test and validation procedures to be carried out before, during and after the development of the high-risk AI system"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_d ;
    :hasSummary "The quality management system must cover examination, test and validation procedures before, during, and after development, including their frequency."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_e a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_e"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: technical specifications, including standards, to be applied and... the means to be used to ensure that the high-risk AI system complies with those requirements"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_e ;
    :hasSummary "The quality management system must include technical specifications and standards to be applied, and means to ensure compliance when harmonised standards are not fully applied or covering."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_f a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_f"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: systems and procedures for data management, including data acquisition, data collection, data analysis, data labelling, data storage, data filtration, data mining, data aggregation, data retention"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_f ;
    :hasSummary "The system must have data management procedures including acquisition, collection, analysis, labelling, storage, filtration, mining, aggregation, retention, and other data operations before placing on the market or service."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_g a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_g"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the risk management system referred to in Article 9"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17,
        :Article_9 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_g ;
    :hasSummary "The quality management system must include the risk management system referred to in Article 9."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_h a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_h"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the setting-up, implementation and maintenance of a post-market monitoring system, in accordance with Article 72"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17,
        :Article_72 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_h ;
    :hasSummary "The system must provide for setting-up, implementation, and maintenance of a post-market monitoring system as per Article 72."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_i a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_i"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM10"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: procedures related to the reporting of a serious incident in accordance with Article 73"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17,
        :Article_73 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_i ;
    :hasSummary "Procedures related to reporting serious incidents in accordance with Article 73 must be included in the quality management system."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_j a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_j"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the handling of communication with national competent authorities, other relevant authorities... notified bodies, other operators, customers or other interested parties"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_j ;
    :hasSummary "The system must handle communication with national competent authorities, other relevant authorities, notified bodies, operators, customers or interested parties."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_k a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_k"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: systems and procedures for record-keeping of all relevant documentation and information"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_k ;
    :hasSummary "Systems and procedures for record-keeping of all relevant documentation and information must be included."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_l a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_l"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: resource management, including security-of-supply related measures"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_l ;
    :hasSummary "The system must cover resource management, including measures related to security of supply."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_m a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_aspects_art17_1_m"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: an accountability framework setting out the responsibilities of the management and other staff with regard to all the aspects listed in this paragraph"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1_m ;
    :hasSummary "An accountability framework setting out responsibilities of management and staff regarding all aspects listed in paragraph 1 must be included."^^xsd:string .

:quality_management_system_obligation_art17 a :InternalControlObligation ;
    rdfs:label "quality_management_system_obligation_art17"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM1"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: Providers of high-risk AI systems shall put a quality management system in place that ensures compliance with this Regulation."@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_17 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_17_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems shall put a quality management system in place ensuring compliance with this Regulation, documented systematically with specified policies, procedures, and instructions."^^xsd:string .

:registration_field_annviii_a a :RegistrationField ;
    rdfs:label "registration_field_annviii_a"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VIII ;
    :hasComponentOf :RegistrationRecord_Annex_VIII ;
    :hasSummary "The following information shall be provided and thereafter kept up to date with regard to high-risk AI systems to be registered in accordance with Article 49(1):"^^xsd:string .

:registration_field_annviii_b a :RegistrationField ;
    rdfs:label "registration_field_annviii_b"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VIII ;
    :hasComponentOf :RegistrationRecord_Annex_VIII ;
    :hasSummary "The following information shall be provided and thereafter kept up to date with regard to AI systems to be registered in accordance with Article 49(2):"^^xsd:string .

:registration_field_annviii_c a :RegistrationField ;
    rdfs:label "registration_field_annviii_c"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_VIII ;
    :hasComponentOf :RegistrationRecord_Annex_VIII ;
    :hasSummary "The following information shall be provided and thereafter kept up to date with regard to high-risk AI systems to be registered in accordance with Article 49(3):"^^xsd:string .

:registration_obligation_deployers_public_authorities_art26_8 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "registration_obligation_deployers_public_authorities_art26_8"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: Deployers ... shall comply with the registration obligations ... When such deployers find ... not been registered ... shall not use that system"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_26 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_26_8 ;
    :hasSummary "Deployers who are public authorities or EU institutions must comply with AI system registration obligations and must not use unregistered high-risk AI systems."^^xsd:string .

:registration_of_testing_art60_4c a :ProceduralCondition ;
    rdfs:label "registration_of_testing_art60_4c"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "evidence: the provider...has registered the testing in real world conditions with a Union-wide unique single identification number and the information specified"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_4_c ;
    :hasSummary "Testing must be registered with a Union-wide unique single identification number and other specified information depending on the AI system's Annex III classification."^^xsd:string .

:reporting_obligation_art70_6 a :OversightPower ;
    rdfs:label "reporting_obligation_art70_6"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ7"@en,
        "evidence: Member States shall report to the Commission on the status of the financial and human resources of the national competent authorities"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_70 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_70_6 ;
    :hasSummary "Member States shall report by 2 August 2025 and biennially thereafter on the status and adequacy of financial and human resources of national competent authorities to the Commission, which transmits to the Board for recommendations."^^xsd:string .

:reversibility_of_ai_system_outputs_art60_4k a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "reversibility_of_ai_system_outputs_art60_4k"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM9"@en,
        "evidence: predictions, recommendations or decisions of the AI system can be effectively reversed and disregarded"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_4_k ;
    :hasSummary "Predictions, recommendations or decisions of the AI system during testing can be effectively reversed and disregarded."^^xsd:string .

:serious_incident_reporting_and_mitigation_art60_7 a :ProviderIncidentReport ;
    rdfs:label "serious_incident_reporting_and_mitigation_art60_7"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM10"@en,
        "evidence: Any serious incident...shall be reported...provider shall adopt immediate mitigation or suspend testing or terminate it"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_7 ;
    :hasReportingTarget :MarketSurveillanceAuthority ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must report serious incidents during testing to national market surveillance authorities, adopt mitigation measures or suspend/terminate testing, and have recall procedures for terminated testing."^^xsd:string .

:systemic_risk_gpai_necessity_condition_art51_1_a a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "systemic_risk_gpai_necessity_condition_art51_1_a"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ5"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM6"@en,
        "evidence: it has high impact capabilities evaluated on the basis of appropriate technical tools and methodologies, including indicators and benchmarks"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_51 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_51_1_a ;
    :hasSummary "A general-purpose AI model has systemic risk if it has high impact capabilities evaluated by appropriate technical tools, including indicators and benchmarks."^^xsd:string .

:systemic_risk_gpai_necessity_condition_art51_1_b a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "systemic_risk_gpai_necessity_condition_art51_1_b"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ5"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM6"@en,
        "evidence: based on a decision of the Commission... it has capabilities or an impact equivalent to those set out in point (a)"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_51 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_51_1_b ;
    :hasSummary "A general-purpose AI model has systemic risk based on a Commission decision or qualified alert if it has equivalent capabilities or impact to those with high impact capabilities."^^xsd:string .

:systemic_risk_gpai_necessity_condition_art51_2 a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "systemic_risk_gpai_necessity_condition_art51_2"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ5"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM6"@en,
        "evidence: presumed to have high impact capabilities... when the cumulative amount of computation... is greater than 10 25"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_51 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_51_2 ;
    :hasSummary "A general-purpose AI model is presumed to have high impact capabilities when the cumulative amount of computation for training exceeds 10^25 floating point operations."^^xsd:string .

:systemic_risk_gpai_proportionality_condition_art51_3 a :ProportionalityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "systemic_risk_gpai_proportionality_condition_art51_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ5"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM6"@en,
        "evidence: Commission shall adopt delegated acts... to amend thresholds... and supplement benchmarks and indicators in light of evolving technological developments"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_51 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_51_3 ;
    :hasSummary "The Commission shall amend thresholds and supplement benchmarks and indicators through delegated acts to reflect technological evolution and ensure thresholds reflect the state of the art."^^xsd:string .

:testing_duration_limit_and_extension_art60_4f a :NecessityCondition ;
    rdfs:label "testing_duration_limit_and_extension_art60_4f"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM9"@en,
        "evidence: testing in real world conditions does not last longer than...six months, which may be extended for an additional period of six months, subject to prior notification...to the market surveillance author"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_4_f ;
    :hasSummary "Testing in real world conditions shall not last longer than six months but can be extended for six more months with prior notification and explanation to the market surveillance authority."^^xsd:string .

:testing_plan_field_annix a :TestingPlanField ;
    rdfs:label "testing_plan_field_annix"@en ;
    :hasAnnexReference :Annex_IX ;
    :hasComponentOf :TestingPlan_Annex_IX ;
    :hasSummary "The following information shall be provided and thereafter kept up to date with regard to testing in real world conditions to be registered in accordance with Article 60:"^^xsd:string .

:testing_plan_submission_and_approval_art60_4a_b a :ProceduralCondition ;
    rdfs:label "testing_plan_submission_and_approval_art60_4a_b"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "evidence: the provider...has drawn up a real-world testing plan and submitted it to the market surveillance authority...has approved the testing in real world conditions and the real-world testing plan; where n"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_60 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_60_4_a ;
    :hasSummary "Providers must draw up and submit a real-world testing plan to the market surveillance authority which must approve the plan; tacit approval applies if no response in 30 days unless national law states otherwise."^^xsd:string .

:third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_1_b a :ThirdPartyAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_1_b"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: assessment of the quality management system and the assessment of the technical documentation, with the involvement of a notified body, referred to in Annex VII"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_43_1_b ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems listed in point 1 of Annex III may choose the conformity assessment under Annex VII involving a notified body when harmonised standards or common specifications are applied or when conditions in points (a) to (d) of paragraph 1 occur."^^xsd:string .

:third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_1_b_points a :ThirdPartyAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_1_b_points"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: the provider shall follow the conformity assessment procedure set out in Annex VII where: (a) harmonised standards... (d) one or more... has been published with a restriction"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_43_1 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers shall follow the Annex VII conformity procedure when harmonised standards do not exist or are not fully applied, or common specifications are not available or not fully applied, or standards have restrictions."^^xsd:string .

:third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_1_subordinate_law_enforcement a :ThirdPartyAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_1_subordinate_law_enforcement"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: market surveillance authority... shall act as a notified body"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_43_1 ;
    :hasSummary "For high-risk AI systems intended for law enforcement, immigration, asylum authorities, or Union agencies, the market surveillance authority shall act as a notified body under the Annex VII procedure."^^xsd:string .

:third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_3 a :ThirdPartyAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_3"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: provider shall follow the relevant conformity assessment procedure as required under those legal acts"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_43_3 ;
    :hasSummary "For high-risk AI systems covered by Union harmonisation legislation in Annex I Section A, providers shall follow the conformity assessment procedure of those acts, which include Section 2 requirements of this Chapter and parts of Annex VII."^^xsd:string .

:third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_3_manufacturer_opt_out_condition a :ThirdPartyAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_3_manufacturer_opt_out_condition"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: manufacturer may use that option only if it has also applied harmonised standards or common specifications"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_43_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Manufacturers opting out from third-party conformity assessment under Union legislation may do so only if harmonised standards or common specifications covering all Section 2 requirements have been applied."^^xsd:string .

:third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_3_notified_bodies_entitlement a :ThirdPartyAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "third_party_assessment_obligation_art43_3_notified_bodies_entitlement"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: notified bodies... shall be entitled to control the conformity... provided that the compliance... has been assessed"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_31,
        :Article_43 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_43_3 ;
    :hasSummary "Notified bodies notified under Union harmonisation legislation may control conformity with Section 2 if they comply with Article 31 requirements."^^xsd:string .

:worker_notification_deployers_high_risk_workplace_art26_7 a :WorkerNotificationObligation ;
    rdfs:label "worker_notification_deployers_high_risk_workplace_art26_7"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ6"@en,
        "evidence: Before putting into service ... deployers who are employers shall inform workers’ representatives and the affected workers"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_26 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_26_7 ;
    :hasSummary "Deployers who are employers shall inform workers and their representatives before using a high-risk AI system at the workplace."^^xsd:string .

:written_agreement_between_providers_and_third_parties_art25_4 a :ConformityAssessmentObligation ;
    rdfs:label "written_agreement_between_providers_and_third_parties_art25_4"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "cq_target: CQ2"@en,
        "cq_target: LLM2"@en,
        "evidence: provider and third party...shall by written agreement specify necessary information, capabilities, technical access and other assistance...not apply to third parties making accessible...under a free a"@en ;
    :hasArticleReference :Article_25 ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_25_4 ;
    :hasSummary "Providers of high-risk AI systems and third parties supplying AI systems, tools, services, components, or processes must specify, by written agreement, the information and technical access needed for the provider to comply with obligations under the Regulation, except for third parties providing free open-source tools or general-purpose AI models."^^xsd:string .

:Annex_IX a :Annex ;
    rdfs:label "Annex IX — Information to be submitted upon the registration of high-risk AI systems listed in Annex III in relation to testing in real world conditions in accordance with Article 60"@en ;
    :hasSourceURL "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/annex/9/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "Before any high-risk AI system is tested in real-world conditions, it must be registered according to Article 60.This Annex explains what information needs to be provided when registering high-risk AI systems for real-world testing. This includes a unique identification number for the test, contact details of the provider and those involved in the testing, a brief description of the AI system and its purpose, a summary of the testing plan, and information on any suspension or termination of the testing. This information must be kept up to date."^^xsd:string .

:Article_101 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 101 — Fines for providers of general-purpose AI models"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_101_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_101_1_a,
        :Paragraph_Article_101_1_b,
        :Paragraph_Article_101_1_c,
        :Paragraph_Article_101_1_d,
        :Paragraph_Article_101_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_101_3,
        :Paragraph_Article_101_4,
        :Paragraph_Article_101_5,
        :Paragraph_Article_101_6 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/101/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "The EU can fine companies that provide general-purpose AI models up to 3% of their annual global turnover or €15 million, whichever is higher, if they break the rules. This could be for not following regulations, not providing requested documents or information, not complying with certain measures, or not allowing the EU to access their AI model for evaluation. The severity of the fine depends on the seriousness and length of the infringement. Companies will be told about any preliminary findings and given a chance to respond before a decision is made. The EU Court of Justice can review and change any fines."^^xsd:string .

:Article_11 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 11 — Technical documentation"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_11_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_11_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_11_3 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/11/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "This EU law states that before a high-risk AI system is launched, detailed technical documentation must be prepared and kept updated. This documentation should prove that the AI system meets the law's requirements and provide clear information for authorities to check compliance. It should include certain key elements. Small businesses, including start-ups, can provide this information in a simpler way. The EU will create a simplified form for this purpose. If a high-risk AI system is related to a product covered by other EU laws, one set of documentation should include all necessary information. The EU can update these requirements as technology advances."^^xsd:string .

:Article_12 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 12 — Record-keeping"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_12_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_12_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_12_2_a,
        :Paragraph_Article_12_2_b,
        :Paragraph_Article_12_2_c,
        :Paragraph_Article_12_3,
        :Paragraph_Article_12_3_a,
        :Paragraph_Article_12_3_b,
        :Paragraph_Article_12_3_c,
        :Paragraph_Article_12_3_d ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/12/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "This article states that high-risk AI systems must have the ability to automatically record events throughout their lifespan. This is to ensure that the system's actions can be traced back, especially in situations where the AI might pose a risk or undergo significant changes. The system should also record details like when it was used, the database it checked data against, the data that matched, and who verified the results. This is to ensure accountability and safety in the use of high-risk AI systems."^^xsd:string .

:Article_15 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 15 — Accuracy, robustness and cybersecurity"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_15_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_15_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_15_3,
        :Paragraph_Article_15_4,
        :Paragraph_Article_15_5 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/15/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "The EU AI Act states that high-risk AI systems must be designed to be accurate, robust, and secure. They should perform consistently throughout their lifecycle. The Commission will work with relevant stakeholders to develop ways to measure these qualities. The accuracy of these AI systems should be declared in their instructions. These systems should be resilient to errors and faults, and should have backup plans in place. They should also be designed to reduce the risk of biased outputs. Finally, these systems should be secure against unauthorized third parties trying to exploit their vulnerabilities."^^xsd:string .

:Article_21 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 21 — Cooperation with competent authorities"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_21_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_21_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_21_3 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/21/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "This article states that companies providing high-risk AI systems must, when asked by a relevant authority, provide all the information needed to show that their AI system meets the required standards. This information must be in a language that the authority can easily understand. If asked, these companies must also allow the authority to access automatically generated logs of the AI system, as long as they control these logs. Any information obtained by the authority must be treated confidentially."^^xsd:string .

:Article_31 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 31 — Requirements relating to notified bodies"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_31_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_10,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_11,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_12,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_3,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_4,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_5,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_6,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_7,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_8,
        :Paragraph_Article_31_9 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/31/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "The EU AI Act states that notified bodies, which assess high-risk AI systems, must be established under a member state's national law and have legal personality. They must meet certain organizational, quality management, resource, and cybersecurity requirements. They must be independent of the AI system provider and any other operator with an economic interest in the AI system. They must also maintain confidentiality and take into account the size and complexity of the provider and the AI system. They must have liability insurance and be capable of carrying out their tasks with professional integrity and competence."^^xsd:string .

:Article_34 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 34 — Operational obligations of notified bodies"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_34_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_34_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_34_3 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/34/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "This article states that notified bodies (officially recognized organizations) must check that high-risk AI systems meet the standards outlined in Article 43. They should avoid causing unnecessary work for providers and consider factors like the provider's size, sector, structure, and the complexity of the AI system. They should especially try to reduce administrative work and compliance costs for small businesses. However, they must still ensure the AI system meets the necessary safety standards. These bodies must also provide all relevant documents to the notifying authority (the body that oversees them) when asked, to help with assessments and monitoring."^^xsd:string .

:Article_47 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 47 — EU declaration of conformity"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_47_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_47_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_47_3,
        :Paragraph_Article_47_4,
        :Paragraph_Article_47_5 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/47/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "The EU AI Act requires providers of high-risk AI systems to create a written declaration of conformity for each system. This document, which can be physical or electronic, must be kept available for national authorities for 10 years after the system is launched. The declaration must identify the AI system and confirm that it meets certain requirements. It must also be translated into a language that the authorities can understand. If the AI system is subject to other EU laws, a single declaration covering all applicable laws is required. The provider is responsible for ensuring the declaration is kept up-to-date. The Commission can update the declaration's content as needed."^^xsd:string .

:Article_67 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 67 — Advisory forum"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_67_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_67_10,
        :Paragraph_Article_67_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_67_3,
        :Paragraph_Article_67_4,
        :Paragraph_Article_67_5,
        :Paragraph_Article_67_6,
        :Paragraph_Article_67_7,
        :Paragraph_Article_67_8,
        :Paragraph_Article_67_9 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/67/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "The EU AI Act will establish an advisory forum to provide technical expertise and advice to the Board and the Commission. The forum will include a balanced mix of stakeholders from industry, start-ups, SMEs, civil society, and academia. The Commission will appoint members with recognized AI expertise. Members will serve for two years, with the possibility of a four-year extension. Certain organizations will be permanent members. The forum will create its own rules, elect two co-chairs, and meet at least twice a year. It can prepare opinions, recommendations, and establish sub-groups. An annual report on its activities will be publicly available."^^xsd:string .

:Article_77 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 77 — Powers of authorities protecting fundamental rights"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_77_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_77_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_77_3,
        :Paragraph_Article_77_4 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/77/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "This article states that national authorities who oversee the respect of fundamental rights, including non-discrimination, in relation to high-risk AI systems, can request and access any relevant documentation. This is to ensure they can effectively fulfill their duties. Each EU member state must identify these authorities and make a public list within three months of this regulation coming into effect. If the documentation is insufficient to determine if there's been a breach of fundamental rights, the authority can request testing of the AI system. Any information obtained must be treated confidentially."^^xsd:string .

:Article_8 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 8 — Compliance with the requirements"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_8_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_8_2 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/8/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "This article states that high-risk AI systems must meet certain standards, considering their purpose and the current state of AI technology. If a product contains an AI system, the providers must ensure it meets all relevant EU regulations. To avoid unnecessary duplication and extra work, providers can choose to incorporate necessary testing, reporting, and documentation into existing procedures required by EU legislation."^^xsd:string .

:Article_83 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 83 — Formal non-compliance"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_83_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_83_1_a,
        :Paragraph_Article_83_1_b,
        :Paragraph_Article_83_1_c,
        :Paragraph_Article_83_1_d,
        :Paragraph_Article_83_1_e,
        :Paragraph_Article_83_1_f,
        :Paragraph_Article_83_1_g,
        :Paragraph_Article_83_2 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/83/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "This article states that if a company doesn't follow certain rules, such as not correctly marking their product or not registering it in the EU database, the authorities can ask them to fix these issues within a certain time frame. If the company doesn't comply, the authorities can take further action, like restricting or banning the product from the market, or making sure it's recalled or removed from the market immediately."^^xsd:string .

:Article_86 a :Article ;
    rdfs:label "Article 86 — Right to explanation of individual decision-making"@en ;
    :hasParagraphReference :Paragraph_Article_86_1,
        :Paragraph_Article_86_2,
        :Paragraph_Article_86_3 ;
    :hasSourceURL "data/unstructured/eu_ai_act_content.html"^^xsd:string,
        "https://artificialintelligenceact.eu/article/86/"^^xsd:string ;
    :hasSummary "This article states that if a decision is made about a person using a high-risk AI system, and that decision has a significant impact on the person's health, safety, or basic rights, the person has the right to a clear explanation of how the AI system was involved in the decision-making process. However, this doesn't apply if there are exceptions or restrictions in Union or national law. This right is only applicable if it's not already provided for under Union law."^^xsd:string .

